</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I didn't do the whole Kickstarter thingy, so, I have to ask: when will this beautiful behemoth be available to the public as a whole?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> They've said before that it's planned to come out in the fall.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10243-zenten","name":"zenten","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10243_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"488"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-02T18:54:47-07:00","id":1086938,"title":"","content":"Rats. I went with the PDF only on BackerKit rather than the full book, so I think I'll have to wait until official release. Oh well, that's what I get for being cheap. :-) At least I get to enjoy it vicariously until then.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2430-kalinara","name":"kalinara","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2430_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"582"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-02T18:57:52-07:00","id":1086940,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1086863-it-s-out?p=1086933#post1086933\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, I have a confession to make. I usually skip the opening fiction. But this time, I decided to read it.<br /> <br /> Only, there isn't any. Where the opening fiction usually goes, I instead found several pages worth of testimonials as various people who have been involved with Changeling over the years each explained in a couple paragraphs each what Changeling is to them.<br /> <br /> Cool!</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> There is also opening fiction. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13-blackhatmatt","name":"blackhatmatt","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"464"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-02T19:00:36-07:00","id":1086941,"title":"","content":"2 Notes on houses...<br /> <br /> Balor are no longer categoricaly incapable of becoming Seelie under any circumstances.<br /> <br /> Leahaun, no longer HAVE to commit rhapsody to slow their aging.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-02T20:19:10-07:00","id":1086970,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Demigod Beast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1086863-it-s-out?p=1086894#post1086894\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are Inanimae and Nunnehi in there?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yes, but.... the inanimae, due to how big the original book was, are kinda really cut down to fit in here... Not sure if I like the new version or not.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3071-magusrogue","name":"MagusRogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3071_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"53"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-02T20:38:50-07:00","id":1086980,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MagusRogue</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1086863-it-s-out?p=1086970#post1086970\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Yes, but.... the inanimae, due to how big the original book was, are kinda really cut down to fit in here... Not sure if I like the new version or not.</div> </div> </div> </div>Everything was incredibly cut down, kind of like the Fera were in the W20 core. Expanding upon them is going to be the work of several books. At least the Mannikins have listed birthrights and frailties in this version! (^VVVVVV^)<br /> <br /> On that note, I see that in this cut-down version, the Hsien had their Yin and Yang tempers changed to a 1-5 scale. The one thing I think one might absolutely need to re-evaluate, though, is the name of the metal kamuii, before it gets worked in again as something fixed. I stand by my assumption that chu-ih-yu is a highly mangled form of Ch'ih-yu (Chiyou in Hanyu Pinyin), based on the presence of other notable legendary emperor and divine names in the ranks (Chu-jung being Zhurong and Hou-chi being Houji, Lord of Millet) and... creative misspelling like the Dragon Tear Discipline from KotE, which is so off that I can't even bear to type out right now, or the Mokole floating Gift (ditto). Also, if you are using Wade-Giles Romanization of Mandarin as the Chinese kith names seem to be, each syllable is separated by a dash (i.e. Fu-hsi instead of Fu Hsi).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-02T20:44:27-07:00","id":1086984,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1086863-it-s-out?p=1086980#post1086980\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Everything was incredibly cut down, kind of like the Fera were in the W20 core. Expanding upon them is going to be the work of several books. At least the Mannikins have listed birthrights and frailties in this version! (^VVVVVV^).</div> </div> </div> </div>I will agree, that part made me squee. Now only if they actually gave the Empire of Flickers an actual Phyla. Ooooo that might be good for a secondary book down the line, kinda like the Fera book! That and expand the Slivers into true cantrips in addition to just Unleashing.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3071-magusrogue","name":"MagusRogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3071_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"53"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-02T20:55:21-07:00","id":1086987,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MagusRogue</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1086863-it-s-out?p=1086984#post1086984\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I will agree, that part made me squee. Now only if they actually gave the Empire of Flickers an actual Phyla. Ooooo that might be good for a secondary book down the line, kinda like the Fera book! That and expand the Slivers into true cantrips in addition to just Unleashing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Also, gladeling mannikins. Ironically, my first thought about how that would pan out years ago was with mandrake roots, yet, the name mandragora ended up with the thallain ghille-dhu...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-02T21:00:16-07:00","id":1086990,"title":"","content":"Overall I'm liking it so far. Can't tell you how pleased I am that this is finally a thing, and indeed still getting over disbelief that new C:tD exists at all.<br /> <br /> That being said...<br /> <br /> This is an artistic choice that it's too late to change, and in the grand scheme of things it's not so huge of a detail, but its representative of a thing that happens a lot and always bugs me when it does.<br /> <br /> The Dutchy of Dogwood. West Virginia gets lumped in with Virginia yet again. I still have to explain to people in this the year 2017 that West Virginia is indeed a state. I have to explain why the distinction is important one hundred and fifty four years after West Virginia shed blood to be on the right side of history. I wouldn't be bothered as much if it were at least grouped in with the Dutchy of Appalachia, but for some reason the Dutchy of Appalachia doesn't include the only state entirely within the Appalachians and instead that state is grouped into political union with the state its entire existence is predicated on breaking away from. I also wouldn't be bothered as much if there were even one sentence in Dutchy of Dogwood that mentioned West Virginia, but there isn't. Once again West Virginia is an afterthought, a punchline unworthy of notice.<br /> <br /> Also, not to be that guy, but the Eshu illustration doesn't really match up with the Kith's description. Its very... White.<br /> <br /> I'm not saying that Eshu have to be the token POC Kith, but the Eshu description on the same page calls out the Kith's African heritage multiple times, and the only core Kith illustration that features a POC is the Recap. The one with the monster teeth. I'm just saying maybe some more thought could have been put into those choices.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2507,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","user":"Caitiff Primogen","date":". 05-03-2017, 12:26 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-02T21:18:19-07:00","id":1086994,"title":"","content":"Stark re-organized into a &quot;charity&quot; akin to Autism Speaks, and its ill-informed allies are basically anti-vaxxer diet fad chasers and analogs to the orientation &quot;conversion&quot; religious hate groups. If the shoe fits...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-02T21:27:55-07:00","id":1087001,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1086863-it-s-out?p=1086994#post1086994\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Stark re-organized into a &quot;charity&quot; akin to Autism Speaks, and its ill-informed allies are basically anti-vaxxer diet fad chasers and analogs to the orientation &quot;conversion&quot; religious hate groups. If the shoe fits...</div> </div> </div> </div>Is that what that is? Must be a coincidence.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Luka Carroll</b><br /> Onyx Path Freelancer &amp; Developer<br /> <i>Working On: </i>C20 Player's Guide, Lunars<br /> <i>Worked On: </i>V20 TMR, Demon STG, C20, Book of Freeholds, Conquering Heroes, Building A Legend, Dragon-Blooded, The Realm","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3785-luka-c","name":"Luka C","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3785_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"175"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-02T23:51:43-07:00","id":1087028,"title":"","content":"I'M SO EXCITED.<br /> <br /> Two quick questions:<br /> <br /> 1) where's the corrections thread? Link in the email is invalid? I've found a few already... <b>ETA: nevermind! Found it!</b><br /> <br /> 2) I'm trying to read it linearly, but keep skipping ahead to check things. The new approach to seemings seems to be that they progress linearly from the point of your chrysalis and that in unusual circumstances an infusion of glamour can send you back to a previous seemings. But I haven't been able to find much information about how to determine when these changes take place? I mean, obviously the Golden Rule applies, and it's a roleplaying tool. But C:tD had it tied more strongly to age boundaries and had sections no celebrations, etc., that would be held in Kithain society to mark the occasions, as well as how an existing character would handle temper changes. I haven't been able to find a similar section in C20? Like I'd appreciate starting guidelines about triggers (mechanical or narrative) that would signal a character approaching a change of seeming. Have I not been able to find it or is it not in there? If the latter, how would you handle it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":187,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/187-beccatoria","user":"beccatoria","date":". 05-03-2017, 03:08 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/187-beccatoria","name":"beccatoria","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar187_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"85"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-03T02:11:13-07:00","id":1087056,"title":"","content":"So is it just me, or did C20's history change it so that there are now two Houses that took the Changeling Way during the Shattering, but still only one according to the character creation rules?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-03T02:27:16-07:00","id":1087058,"title":"","content":"Actually reading Thallain I have a question. If Thallain are Nightmare-Fae why are the Redcaps and in a lesser measure the Sluaghs not Thallain?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2225-ganonso","name":"ganonso","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2225_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-03T02:41:24-07:00","id":1087064,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ganonso</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1086863-it-s-out?p=1087058#post1087058\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actually reading Thallain I have a question. If Thallain are Nightmare-Fae why are the Redcaps and in a lesser measure the Sluaghs not Thallain?</div> </div> </div> </div>Thallain are Fomorian. Redcaps and sluagh are Tuathan. They're from different Dreams.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Luka Carroll</b><br /> Onyx Path Freelancer &amp; Developer<br /> <i>Working On: </i>C20 Player's Guide, Lunars<br /> <i>Worked On: </i>V20 TMR, Demon STG, C20, Book of Freeholds, Conquering Heroes, Building A Legend, Dragon-Blooded, The Realm","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3785-luka-c","name":"Luka C","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3785_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"175"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-03T03:29:38-07:00","id":1087078,"title":"","content":"Ok something I hadn't read<br /> <br /> ne&quot;&gt; <span style=\"color:#231F20\"><span style=\"font-family:GoudyStd\">Beginning with the Black Plague, periodic horrors of human<br /> <span style=\"color:#231F20\"><span style=\"font-family:GoudyStd\">history caused Dark Glamour to infuse the ancient Fomorian Trods<br /> <span style=\"color:#231F20\"><span style=\"font-family:GoudyStd\">with enough power to briefl pierce the Silver Ban, allowing small<br /> <span style=\"color:#231F20\"><span style=\"font-family:GoudyStd\">bands of Thallain to return. Any time humanity collectively gave<br /> <span style=\"color:#231F20\"><span style=\"font-family:GoudyStd\">in to despair \u2014 the conquest and plagues of the Native Americans,<br /> <span style=\"color:#231F20\"><span style=\"font-family:GoudyStd\">the African slave trade, the Chinese opium trade,<b> <span style=\"font-size:18px\">the French</span></b><br /> <span style=\"color:#231F20\"><span style=\"font-family:GoudyStd\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><b>Revolution</b></span>, and so many others \u2014 a few more Thallain found<br /> <span style=\"color:#231F20\"><span style=\"font-family:GoudyStd\">their way to Earth. They called the events Tarraroms<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\">What the hell did the French Revolution did to you? An exemple of humanity giving into despair? The overcoming of the ancient regime and the birth of a new democracy, one who actually abolished slavery?<br /> <br /> <br /> If you want to pick a French exemple of Dark Glamour, put the Restoration when the Kings came back or when Napoleon 3 crowned himself Emperor. Not the Revolution, it should be the biggest effusion of Glamour before the Moon's Landing. </span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2225-ganonso","name":"ganonso","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2225_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-03T04:06:12-07:00","id":1087090,"title":"","content":"I like the new write-ups for the Legacies; I can actually see myself playing an Unseelie protagonist now. <br /> <br /> As for the French Revolution: it was motivated by high ideals; but all along, it was an illustration of how the road to Hell is paved with good intentions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-03T04:22:26-07:00","id":1087098,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1086863-it-s-out?p=1087090#post1087090\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like the new write-ups for the Legacies; I can actually see myself playing an Unseelie protagonist now.<br /> <br /> As for the French Revolution: it was motivated by high ideals; but all along, it was an illustration of how the road to Hell is paved with good intentions.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yea but it didn't engineer despair; even in France. The French Revolution exported democracy in Europe and was a model for most revolutions to follow even in South America.<br /> <br /> To see it put in the same breath as the America conquests, the Opium War and the World Wars is a bit jarring.<br /> <br /> How would American feel if the War of Independance was presented as a Tarrarom?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2225-ganonso","name":"ganonso","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2225_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-03T04:26:35-07:00","id":1087099,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Holden</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1086863-it-s-out#post1086863\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><b>It's out!</b></span></div> </div> </div> </div><b><span style=\"font-size:16px\">GOOD.</span></b>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>...","edited":{"userid":5211,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5211-firkraag","user":"Firkraag","date":". 05-03-2017, 08:21 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5211-firkraag","name":"Firkraag","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5211_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-03T04:48:42-07:00","id":1087107,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ganonso</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1086863-it-s-out?p=1087078#post1087078\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">What the hell did the French Revolution did to you? An example of humanity giving into despair? The overcoming of the ancient regime and the birth of a new democracy, one who actually abolished slavery?<br /> <br /> <br /> If you want to pick a French example of Dark Glamour, put the Restoration when the Kings came back or when Napoleon 3 crowned himself Emperor. Not the Revolution, it should be the biggest effusion of Glamour before the Moon's Landing.</span></div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Reign_of_Terror\" target=\"_blank\">https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Reign_of_Terror</a><br /> <br /> All I want to say is that France had a long, rocky path to &quot;Libert\u00e9, \u00e9galit\u00e9, fraternit\u00e9!&quot;<br /> <br /> Revolutions, while at some points of history may be a necessary and inevitable conclusion of an interests conflict, are an indication, that formal leadership of the state and the leaders of public opinion have failed to communicate and achieve a consensus. Revolutions are built on blood and bones of people, who are often called heroes or villains based on the side they nominally supported when they died, not who they were in their lives. And France had seen their heroes turned rotten, violent and oppressive. And there are more peoples I can recall, that did as well.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> How would American feel if the War of Independence was presented as a Tarrarom? </div> </div> </div>It depends on who you ask, how much that person knows about the issue, what she believes, how much she's benefitting from that, etc. etc. and even then - different factors might mean more or less to different people.<br /> <br /> Like, what would a Native North American think about War of Independence? It most likely depends.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>...","edited":{"userid":5211,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5211-firkraag","user":"Firkraag","date":". 05-03-2017, 10:51 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5211-firkraag","name":"Firkraag","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5211_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-03T04:55:26-07:00","id":1087110,"title":"","content":"Kind of wish the Oba frailty of &quot;can't connect to any place I'd be able to play&quot; wasn't still active I mean its not like the Orishas are were worshipped India or or Saudi Arabia and yet Oba can connect there, yet where the Orishas have become the Loa nothing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-03T05:06:57-07:00","id":1087112,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ganonso</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1086863-it-s-out?p=1087058#post1087058\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actually reading Thallain I have a question. If Thallain are Nightmare-Fae why are the Redcaps and in a lesser measure the Sluaghs not Thallain?</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, Denizens of the Dreaming pointed out an irony of that. Like, Aonides being among Adhene and Red Caps - among Kithain.<br /> <br /> This strange division may have something to do with the side they chose to support in the War of Trees, based on their views and predispositions, rather than just heredital or paternal relationships. Sluagh Kithbook indicates, that they have been influenced and shaped into what they are by Thuatha, but it might as well be a justification for how things are. I can imaginme some Unseelie Sluagh, as if they were crippled by Thuatha de Dannan for being true to their nature. Haven't read Red Cap Kithbook, though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5211-firkraag","name":"Firkraag","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5211_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-03T05:33:28-07:00","id":1087115,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ganonso</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1086863-it-s-out?p=1087098#post1087098\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yea but it didn't engineer despair; even in France. The French Revolution exported democracy in Europe and was a model for most revolutions to follow even in South America.<br /> <br /> To see it put in the same breath as the America conquests, the Opium War and the World Wars is a bit jarring.<br /> <br /> How would American feel if the War of Independance was presented as a Tarrarom?</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh yes, the issue was that it ate itself up. When things got so bad that the execution of nobility (not criminals, just for being high class) was a daily event that ladies came to watch and knit by, things went a bit far. I suggest you read Scarlet Pimpernel for a fictional depiction of the issues.<br /> <br /> For my impressions of the book itself? I love LOVE the splat art, really good depictions of the kiths.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-03T06:15:26-07:00","id":1087127,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Firkraag</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1086863-it-s-out?p=1087112#post1087112\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actually, Denizens of the Dreaming pointed out an irony of that. Like, Aonides being among Adhene and Red Caps - among Kithain.<br /> <br /> This strange division may have something to do with the side they chose to support in the War of Trees, based on their views and predispositions, rather than just heredital or paternal relationships. Sluagh Kithbook indicates, that they have been influenced and shaped into what they are by Thuatha, but it might as well be a justification for how things are. I can imaginme some Unseelie Sluagh, as if they were crippled by Thuatha de Dannan for being true to their nature. Haven't read Red Cap Kithbook, though.</div> </div> </div> </div>Kithbook Redcap describe them as &quot;Dreams of Hunger&quot; and puts them as coming from Nightmares. I must reread Shadow Court but I seem to remember they didn't have a Thallain counterpart.<br /> <br /> Of course that asks the question:; Is there a metaphysical difference between Thallain and Kithain or is it simply political with Thallain coming from Nightmares and having backed the losing side in the War of Trees?<br /> <br /> The presence of special Triggers for Thallain points to the former but it doesn't explain what the hell is up with the Redcaps. Perhaps it could be a good campaign hook.<br /> <br /> &quot;The Redcap are only Kithain because they are Oathbound to the Tuhata, someone is disturbing the ancient pledge, go settle this.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2225-ganonso","name":"ganonso","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2225_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-03T06:45:00-07:00","id":1087134,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ganonso</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1086863-it-s-out?p=1087127#post1087127\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Of course that asks the question:; Is there a metaphysical difference between Thallain and Kithain or is it simply political with Thallain coming from Nightmares and having backed the losing side in the War of Trees?</div> </div> </div> </div>This one was purposefully left unanswered. I tried to sprinkle in enough evidence for either answer to be correct.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Charlie Cantrell</b><br /> Onyx Path Freelancer <hr />Changeling: The Dreaming 20th Anniversary Edition, Conquering Heroes, Book of Freeholds, Guide to the Night, C20 Players Guide","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/648-pookaknight","name":"PookaKnight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar648_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"690"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-03T06:48:52-07:00","id":1087135,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ganonso</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1086863-it-s-out?p=1087098#post1087098\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yea but it didn't engineer despair; even in France. The French Revolution exported democracy in Europe and was a model for most revolutions to follow even in South America.<br /> <br /> To see it put in the same breath as the America conquests, the Opium War and the World Wars is a bit jarring.<br /> <br /> How would American feel if the War of Independance was presented as a Tarrarom?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yes, exactly, seconded. And I'm french <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2809-batro","name":"batro","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"24"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-03T07:12:31-07:00","id":1087140,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ganonso</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1086863-it-s-out?p=1087098#post1087098\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yea but it didn't engineer despair; even in France. The French Revolution exported democracy in Europe and was a model for most revolutions to follow even in South America.<br /> <br /> To see it put in the same breath as the America conquests, the Opium War and the World Wars is a bit jarring.<br /> <br /> How would American feel if the War of Independance was presented as a Tarrarom?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I think they should have specified la Terreur, and not the revolution itself.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12678-monkeydjie","name":"Monkeydjie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"47"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-03T07:41:09-07:00","id":1087145,"title":"","content":"My apologies for the poor word choice. The mention of the French Revolution was intended to reference the situation leading up to it and the Reign of Terror, not the final outcome.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Charlie Cantrell</b><br /> Onyx Path Freelancer <hr />Changeling: The Dreaming 20th Anniversary Edition, Conquering Heroes, Book of Freeholds, Guide to the Night, C20 Players Guide","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/648-pookaknight","name":"PookaKnight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar648_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"690"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-03T08:08:29-07:00","id":1087166,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1086863-it-s-out?p=1086987#post1086987\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Also, gladeling mannikins. Ironically, my first thought about how that would pan out years ago was with mandrake roots, yet, the name mandragora ended up with the thallain ghille-dhu...</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yeah, wouldn't technically ALL Mannikins be Krofted? I can't think of a &quot;natural&quot; statue for a mannkin that wouldn't be covered by one of the other empires.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3071-magusrogue","name":"MagusRogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3071_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"53"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-03T08:12:18-07:00","id":1087168,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ganonso</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1086863-it-s-out?p=1087127#post1087127\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Kithbook Redcap describe them as &quot;Dreams of Hunger&quot; and puts them as coming from Nightmares. I must reread Shadow Court but I seem to remember they didn't have a Thallain counterpart.</div> </div> </div> </div>They do now. Them and Sidhe now have Thallian counterparts, so most if not all the kiths are covered by Fomorian variations now.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3071-magusrogue","name":"MagusRogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3071_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"53"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-03T08:24:43-07:00","id":1087175,"title":"","content":"Janet, Ms. Jackson if you're a thallain satyr.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MagusRogue</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1086863-it-s-out?p=1087166#post1087166\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Yeah, wouldn't technically ALL Mannikins be Krofted? I can't think of a &quot;natural&quot; statue for a mannkin that wouldn't be covered by one of the other empires.</div> </div> </div> </div>Technically, most krofted mannikins would be under other empires as well, since they're made of materials like wood or stone. How it seems to work is that shape is important, though it also leads into funny jokes about human faces in toast.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-03T08:31:04-07:00","id":1087178,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PookaKnight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1086863-it-s-out?p=1087145#post1087145\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My apologies for the poor word choice. The mention of the French Revolution was intended to reference the situation leading up to it and the Reign of Terror, not the final outcome.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's an interesting one. Was Citizen Robespierre's fanatical devotion to virtue and terror banal, through the murders of thousands of so-called decadent bourgeoisie?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#000080\">Matthew Dawkins</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000080\">In-House Developer for Onyx Path Publishing</span></b><br /> <br /> <i><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b><span style=\"color:#008080\">Website: </span><a href=\"http://www.matthewdawkins.com\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.matthewdawkins.com</span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#008080\">Patreon: </span><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins</span></a></b></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/152-the-gentleman-gamer","name":"The Gentleman Gamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar152_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-03T08:46:11-07:00","id":1087184,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Gentleman Gamer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1086863-it-s-out?p=1087178#post1087178\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's an interesting one. Was Citizen Robespierre's fanatical devotion to virtue and terror banal, through the murders of thousands of so-called decadent bourgeoisie?</div> </div> </div> </div>Would you cover this topic in one of your videos, <i>perhaps</i>?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5211-firkraag","name":"Firkraag","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5211_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-03T09:33:43-07:00","id":1087201,"title":"","content":"I am sad that House Scathach has lost its official non-aligned status. I'd have been happy with both House Daanan and Scathach being un-aligned to keep the numbers even, but having them part of the Courts and then saying &quot;Yeah, but they aren't REALLY a part of them&quot; in the text seems awkward. (I generally really dislike House Daanan's existence in the core book, but c'est la vie. *grumble grumble* darned Dice *grumble grumble*)<br /> <br /> I'm also a bit frustrated that House Scathach lost its &quot;We were the only ones to stay on Earth during the Interregnum&quot; bit and was hoping this edition would emphasize it rather than gloss it over. House Liam's tragedy of being the exiled nobles who no one trusts and prefer humans to their fellow Sidhe is a lot less powerful if most of the House had been staying on Earth all along. (I mean, yes, there's the reconciliation of &quot;We're the ones who love humans, yet we also kick them out of their bodies&quot; bit, but there's story potential there. I think House Liam has enough cool narrative potential without also taking the cool bits from Scathach away. <br /> <br /> I'm also wary of the House Liam and Scathach try to negotiate peace during the Accordance War bits. Liam are Oathbreakers. No one listens to them because of their reputation. And Scathach's negotiations made more sense when they weren't aligned to either Seelie or Unseelie courts. <br /> <br /> Now, in this edition did all of the Arcadian houses arrive at once? That probably seems for the best, simplifies things and the book doesn't get into the awkward politics of &quot;Okay, first it was five Seelie houses and House Scathach, then it turned out that three Unseelie houses also showed up at the moon landing but were in hiding for a while until their first supplement came out, then four more showed up to make the numbers even. And then when the world ended we discovered a fourteenth house.&quot; If that's the case, great. And some of the writing strongly implies this. But then there's a section that refers to Dougal as one of the five original houses, and that doesn't seem to make sense. <br /> <br /> I'm still delving through the book, and there's a lot I love, but there's a few things that are frustrating.<br /> <br /> The resolution to the High King David metaplot is disappointing. Now, the status quo of &quot;High King David is gone, Concordia is at the brink of war&quot; was a fantastic place for the line, full of storytelling potential and intrigue. &quot;Oh, he returned, no one is going to talk about it, and now he's kinda going senile I guess?&quot; is less so. A status quo that created interesting story potential was replaced with one that was less so. <br /> <br /> To end on a positive note, I thoroughly enjoy the Chimerical Qualities and Intent systems. They REALLY fix a lot of the problems about Chimerical reality. There's a stronger tone and it feels much more like a viable game to run. I think much of the Dark Ages Fae elements that have crept in are beneficial. Unleashing is superb. <br /> <br /> I'm just nitpicky about the Sidhe I suppose.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4250-petersvensson","name":"PeterSvensson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4250_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-03T10:39:25-07:00","id":1087222,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Gentleman Gamer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1086863-it-s-out?p=1087178#post1087178\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's an interesting one. Was Citizen Robespierre's fanatical devotion to virtue and terror banal, through the murders of thousands of so-called decadent bourgeoisie?</div> </div> </div> </div>I didn't intend it as banal. The Thallain require Glamour just like the Kithain do. The difference is their preferred Glamour has a horrific, primal aspect to it that serves the Fomorian Dream. Nightmare Glamour, if you will <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Charlie Cantrell</b><br /> Onyx Path Freelancer <hr />Changeling: The Dreaming 20th Anniversary Edition, Conquering Heroes, Book of Freeholds, Guide to the Night, C20 Players Guide","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/648-pookaknight","name":"PookaKnight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar648_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"690"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-03T11:01:40-07:00","id":1087232,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Demigod Beast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1086863-it-s-out?p=1086891#post1086891\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is David still on the throne</div> </div> </div> </div>He's back, but he sure is acting strange.... almost like he could be a totally different person!<br /> <br /> Dun dun DUUUNNN!<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Charlie Cantrell</b><br /> Onyx Path Freelancer <hr />Changeling: The Dreaming 20th Anniversary Edition, Conquering Heroes, Book of Freeholds, Guide to the Night, C20 Players Guide","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/648-pookaknight","name":"PookaKnight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar648_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"690"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-03T11:30:27-07:00","id":1087247,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PookaKnight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1086863-it-s-out?p=1087222#post1087222\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I didn't intend it as banal. The Thallain require Glamour just like the Kithain do. The difference is their preferred Glamour has a horrific, primal aspect to it that serves the Fomorian Dream. Nightmare Glamour, if you will <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, of course! I contributed to this book and I forgot about that <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> <br /> <br /> Well France was definitely a nightmare for enemies of the revolution.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#000080\">Matthew Dawkins</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000080\">In-House Developer for Onyx Path Publishing</span></b><br /> <br /> <i><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b><span style=\"color:#008080\">Website: </span><a href=\"http://www.matthewdawkins.com\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.matthewdawkins.com</span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#008080\">Patreon: </span><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins</span></a></b></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/152-the-gentleman-gamer","name":"The Gentleman Gamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar152_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-03T11:32:57-07:00","id":1087250,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Firkraag</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1086863-it-s-out?p=1087184#post1087184\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Would you cover this topic in one of your videos, <i>perhaps</i>?</div> </div> </div> </div>Changeling: The French Revolution... I like the idea! I'll consider it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#000080\">Matthew Dawkins</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000080\">In-House Developer for Onyx Path Publishing</span></b><br /> <br /> <i><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b><span style=\"color:#008080\">Website: </span><a href=\"http://www.matthewdawkins.com\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.matthewdawkins.com</span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#008080\">Patreon: </span><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins</span></a></b></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/152-the-gentleman-gamer","name":"The Gentleman Gamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar152_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-03T11:35:49-07:00","id":1087251,"title":"","content":"Are prodigals still treated as mortals for purposes of the Mists? The mage description for example seemed to assume if the &quot;paradigm&quot; matched you were good.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-03T12:09:27-07:00","id":1087274,"title":"","content":"Does preordering the PDF on the Backer Kit get you the PDF right away, or just earlier than it'll be available on DriveThruRPG?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1885-crackedman","name":"CrackedMan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1885_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"254"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-03T12:12:30-07:00","id":1087276,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CrackedMan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1086863-it-s-out?p=1087274#post1087274\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does preordering the PDF on the Backer Kit get you the PDF right away, or just earlier than it'll be available on DriveThruRPG?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The latter, I think. I'm in the same boat. When I've gone to check my link, it indicates that it's not available yet. I should have read more carefully.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2430-kalinara","name":"kalinara","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2430_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"582"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-03T12:13:57-07:00","id":1087277,"title":"","content":"That's what I was afraid of. I was sadly broker than broke when the Kickstarter happened and wasn't able to get involved then. I guess I'm waiting until fall then.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1885-crackedman","name":"CrackedMan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1885_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"254"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-03T12:16:25-07:00","id":1087279,"title":"","content":"I like the fact that the Thallain are now distinguished from the Kithain, not by having two Unseelie Legacies (which wouldn't make sense now that Unseelie\u2260EVIL) but by having their own, corrupted Nightmare Legacies. So the difference between a Redcap and a Ghast is that as bloody as the Redcap is, he's not fundamentally malicious; the Ghast <i>is</i>.<br /> <br /> It's a surprisingly\u200b Black-and-Dark-Gray presentation, not unlike Mage's Nephandi.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-03T12:47:57-07:00","id":1087293,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1086863-it-s-out?p=1087251#post1087251\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are prodigals still treated as mortals for purposes of the Mists? The mage description for example seemed to assume if the &amp;quot;paradigm&amp;quot; matched you were good.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think there's a blanket rule for it. I figure that, e.g., Toreador vampires are subject to the Mists, but Kiasyd vampires aren't; and Ravnos probably are (just looking at the three sample vampires in the book). Heck, the Kiasyd entry explicitly says that they perceive the Dreaming (and also that they have a fae mien; IDK about them as Vampire has never been one of my interests).<br /> <br /> My rule of thumb would be that as a whole, Prodigals probably are subject to the Mists; but that there exist exceptions to this role, like the Kiasyd or mages with fae-compatible paradigms.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-03T13:06:51-07:00","id":1087307,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1086863-it-s-out?p=1087293#post1087293\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think there's a blanket rule for it. I figure that, e.g., Toreador vampires are subject to the Mists, but Kiasyd vampires aren't; and Ravnos probably are (just looking at the three sample vampires in the book). Heck, the Kiasyd entry explicitly says that they perceive the Dreaming (and also that they have a fae mien; IDK about them as Vampire has never been one of my interests).</div> </div> </div> </div>In Vampire, the Kiasyd have Faerie Sight, the level 2 power of their signature Discipline Mytherceria, which allows them to see all things fae. The faerie mien is new with C20.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-03T13:51:56-07:00","id":1087328,"title":"","content":"It's a gorgeous book and I'm loving a lot of what I'm seeing, I'm just supremely disappointed that the ridiculous pooka frailty remained as written. Guess pooka are not meant to have jobs, bank accounts, or access the internet without burning through their willpower. Wow. How utterly stupid. Ugh. First house rule of many, I'm sure. Great work otherwise...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11658-rabbit-pooka","name":"Rabbit Pooka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11658_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"65"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-03T15:00:58-07:00","id":1087346,"title":"","content":"I'm curious what people think of the overhauled Arts and Realms. We fucked with them a <i>lot</i>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/84-holden","name":"Holden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar84_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"673"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-03T15:27:08-07:00","id":1087357,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Holden</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1086863-it-s-out?p=1087346#post1087346\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm curious what people think of the overhauled Arts and Realms. We fucked with them a <i>lot</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Honestly they look awesome but I'm going to have no real comparison until I see them in serious action","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-03T15:49:26-07:00","id":1087369,"title":"","content":"The problem with the pooka frailty is that it's simply the single harshest and most unworkable frailty in the game as written. Even the other kith with willpower based frailties aren't required to spend a willpower point...yet pooka are. <br /> <br /> A betrayed troll simply has to make a willpower roll not to go aggro on whomever betrayed them, no willpower point cost. A boggan simply has to make a willpower check to refuse helping someone in need, no willpower point cost. Yet if asked what his name is a pooka has to pass a willpower check <u><i><b>and</b></i></u> cough up a willpower point. So things like job interviews, setting up a bank account, getting into college...nope. You better have 10 willpower and be willing to burn through most of them simply to get a job a McDonalds.<br /> <br /> Did the writer of the pooka kith want to make sure they wouldn't ever show up at a gaming table? That's likely the result, without house ruling out that willpower point cost. <br /> <br /> I'd suggest it's worthy of being errata'ed out, but I get the feeling it's very much intended as written.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11658-rabbit-pooka","name":"Rabbit Pooka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11658_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"65"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-03T15:53:14-07:00","id":1087370,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Holden</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1086863-it-s-out?p=1087346#post1087346\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm curious what people think of the overhauled Arts and Realms. We fucked with them a <i>lot</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Am nervous, on Soothsay, the power to reward or punish, with a blessing or curse, used to be very accessible, now...<br /> <br /> What can a Kinain Social worker, who has 2 or 3 dots in soothsay, do to use her Fae power to augment her ability to watch and protect children. (have one in the game im running right now)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":1153,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","user":"Prince of the Night","date":". 05-03-2017, 07:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-03T16:22:34-07:00","id":1087385,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Holden</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1086863-it-s-out?p=1087346#post1087346\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm curious what people think of the overhauled Arts and Realms. We fucked with them a <i>lot</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The new version of the Time realm is awesome. It's a thousand times better than the original.<br /> <br /> Personally, I love a lot of the changes to the Arts. There were so many Cantrips that felt like they were in the wrong Arts before, and they've pretty much all found better homes. Dragon's Ire as an Art is a neat idea, and I'm really digging it on first impressions. Ruin is super cool; I'm glad the Dauntain have a unique Art now.<br /> <br /> I'm not sad that Aphrodesia was left out; that's a good call, in my opinion. I am curious why Infusion, Talecraft, the Adhene Arts, and the Shadow Court Arts weren't included, though. Was it just an issue of space?<br /> <br /> It's also a little odd that Oneiromancy isn't taboo and mostly found among the Adhene anymore, and that Naming doesn't seem to make any mention of being restricted and regulated by the Crystal Circle. (Actually, what happened to the Crystal Circle? There's no mention of them at all, at least that I've found.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5910-csschulz","name":"CSSchulz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5910_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-03T16:24:38-07:00","id":1087386,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rabbit Pooka</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1086863-it-s-out?p=1087369#post1087369\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd suggest it's worthy of being errata'ed out, but I get the feeling it's very much intended as written.</div> </div> </div> </div>Eh, you might as well give it a shot and plug it into the errata thread.<br /> <br /> Having if pookas be the only ones that have to do a Willpower roll AND a Willpower point which the other Kiths don't have? Yeah, I'd say put it up, on the grounds of being inconsistent with the other Kiths.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4418,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","user":"tasti man LH","date":". 05-03-2017, 07:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-03T16:35:43-07:00","id":1087390,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CSSchulz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1086863-it-s-out?p=1087385#post1087385\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">and that Naming doesn't seem to make any mention of being restricted and regulated by the Crystal Circle</div> </div> </div> </div>Naming Art and exclusivity doesn't mesh very well, considering, that Saining is a single most important ritual of changeling after... nothing. Without it, all changelings would've gone into Bedlam or Dauntain, and you needed Naming cantrip Saining to avoid that. Or at least, it was that way. I'm not sure, whether it changed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5211-firkraag","name":"Firkraag","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5211_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-03T17:13:16-07:00","id":1087401,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Firkraag</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1086863-it-s-out?p=1087390#post1087390\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Naming Art and exclusivity doesn't mesh very well, considering, that Saining is a single most important ritual of changeling after... nothing. Without it, all changelings would've gone into Bedlam or Dauntain, and you needed Naming cantrip Saining to avoid that. Or at least, it was that way. I'm not sure, whether it changed.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Having a court Seer/Namer proficient enough to do the Saining was important, and that Seer/Namer held a special position because it was supposed to be a rare and difficult Art to learn. And in the old books, the Sidhe were trying to restrict it, but they definitely weren't a hundred percent successful, and obviously at least some commoners were practicing it while the Sidhe were away. I get wanting to make it more accessible, but I liked the idea that it was a difficult Art to master and that the Sidhe were trying to restrict it as a political power move. I like the way Chronos makes mention of the fact that it used to be considered the province of the Sidhe, while opening it up to all kithain in the modern setting. I would've preferred that approach for Naming, as well, personally.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5910-csschulz","name":"CSSchulz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5910_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-03T17:31:05-07:00","id":1087404,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CSSchulz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1086863-it-s-out?p=1087385#post1087385\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> The new version of the Time realm is awesome. It's a thousand times better than the original.<br /> <br /> Personally, I love a lot of the changes to the Arts. There were so many Cantrips that felt like they were in the wrong Arts before, and they've pretty much all found better homes. Dragon's Ire as an Art is a neat idea, and I'm really digging it on first impressions. Ruin is super cool; I'm glad the Dauntain have a unique Art now.<br /> <br /> I'm not sad that Aphrodesia was left out; that's a good call, in my opinion. I am curious why Infusion, Talecraft, the Adhene Arts, and the Shadow Court Arts weren't included, though. Was it just an issue of space?<br /> <br /> It's also a little odd that Oneiromancy isn't taboo and mostly found among the Adhene anymore, and that Naming doesn't seem to make any mention of being restricted and regulated by the Crystal Circle. (Actually, what happened to the Crystal Circle? There's no mention of them at all, at least that I've found.)</div> </div> </div> </div>As a general thing, we didn't want to do faction or kith-exclusive Arts, feeling that if a power was signature to a kith, it should be part of their birthright/frailty package, or maybe a Merit. A lot of other Arts we discarded as largely redundant with existing Arts, or just dumb (like that one that was nothing but anti-Sovereign), or structurally built so that they were almost impossible to make gel with the Realms system. One thing we were very adamant on while writing the Arts was that all Arts should be usable with all Realms, and that there shouldn't be Arts that could basically only be used with a single Realm. There used to be a -lot- of those. The Realm &quot;aiming&quot; system is a <i>lot</i> of fun and we felt C20 should prominently showcase it, rather than just kind of fumbling around it like it was an obstacle to writing Disciplines.<br /> <br /> The Adhene Arts didn't make it in because they were outside the scope of the chapter. It sure wasn't for lack of interest, the Adhene are my favorite thing in Changeling. Maybe they'll show up in a supplement? That's up to Matt.<br /> <br /> The Shadow Court Arts went the way of the dodo both due to the trend toward anti-exclusivity in the Arts chapter, and because they were kinda stinky conceptually-- &quot;fuck you Sovereign, you're not the boss of me&quot; and &quot;the roofie Art&quot; weren't adding a ton to the game, especially since there were already like three other more generalized arts for fucking with people's heads that could easily cover what Aphrodisia did. So Aphrodisia got demoted from a full Art to a single cantrip to replicate the pine cone comic from Oglaf.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/84-holden","name":"Holden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar84_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"673"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-03T18:06:13-07:00","id":1087433,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Holden</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1086863-it-s-out?p=1087404#post1087404\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> As a general thing, we didn't want to do faction or kith-exclusive Arts, feeling that if a power was signature to a kith, it should be part of their birthright/frailty package, or maybe a Merit. A lot of other Arts we discarded as largely redundant with existing Arts, or just dumb (like that one that was nothing but anti-Sovereign), or structurally built so that they were almost impossible to make gel with the Realms system. One thing we were very adamant on while writing the Arts was that all Arts should be usable with all Realms, and that there shouldn't be Arts that could basically only be used with a single Realm. There used to be a -lot- of those. The Realm &quot;aiming&quot; system is a <i>lot</i> of fun and we felt C20 should prominently showcase it, rather than just kind of fumbling around it like it was an obstacle to writing Disciplines.<br /> <br /> The Adhene Arts didn't make it in because they were outside the scope of the chapter. It sure wasn't for lack of interest, the Adhene are my favorite thing in Changeling. Maybe they'll show up in a supplement? That's up to Matt.<br /> <br /> The Shadow Court Arts went the way of the dodo both due to the trend toward anti-exclusivity in the Arts chapter, and because they were kinda stinky conceptually-- &quot;fuck you Sovereign, you're not the boss of me&quot; and &quot;the roofie Art&quot; weren't adding a ton to the game, especially since there were already like three other more generalized arts for fucking with people's heads that could easily cover what Aphrodisia did. So Aphrodisia got demoted from a full Art to a single cantrip to replicate the pine cone comic from Oglaf.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> You dont think &quot;Fuck you!&quot; is an appropiate sentiment for the Shadow court?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-03T18:15:46-07:00","id":1087435,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1086863-it-s-out?p=1087433#post1087433\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> You dont think &quot;Fuck you!&quot; is an appropiate sentiment for the Shadow court?</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think it's a good design basis for a power. As a general thing, &quot;kill Bob&quot; powers don't tend to be a lot of fun. (What's a Kill Bob power? It's a power that specifically kills Bob.)<br /> <br /> It was incoherent with the Realm system.<br /> <br /> It's not fun to buy a power, roll 4 successes, and then not have it work because someone bought &quot;Edgy Rebel&quot; and &quot;Edgy Rebel&quot; auto-trumps Lofty Noble.<br /> <br /> Edgy Rebel auto-trumping the authority of the Nobility also ran against the general grain of how the Dreaming behaves, so the very existence of that Art kinda undermined itself.<br /> <br /> There are plenty of ways to go &quot;fuck you!&quot; with Legerdemain, Chicanery, Autumn, etc, without just doing an anti-Art.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/84-holden","name":"Holden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar84_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"673"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-03T18:19:17-07:00","id":1087437,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Holden</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1086863-it-s-out?p=1087435#post1087435\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't think it's a good design basis for a power. As a general thing, &quot;kill Bob&quot; powers don't tend to be a lot of fun. (What's a Kill Bob power? It's a power that specifically kills Bob.)<br /> <br /> It was incoherent with the Realm system.<br /> <br /> It's not fun to buy a power, roll 4 successes, and then not have it work because someone bought &quot;Edgy Rebel&quot; and &quot;Edgy Rebel&quot; auto-trumps Lofty Noble.<br /> <br /> Edgy Rebel auto-trumping the authority of the Nobility also ran against the general grain of how the Dreaming behaves, so the very existence of that Art kinda undermined itself.<br /> <br /> There are plenty of ways to go &quot;fuck you!&quot; with Legerdemain, Chicanery, Autumn, etc, without just doing an anti-Art.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I have to agree, contempt was a bit Redundant, but one of the other Shadow Court Arts... created a new quest...<br /> <br /> <br /> (also loved how quests were all given a Mechanical component)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-03T19:21:01-07:00","id":1087464,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CSSchulz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1086863-it-s-out?p=1087385#post1087385\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ruin is super cool; I'm glad the Dauntain have a unique Art now.</div> </div> </div> </div>^_^<br /> <br /> Night made.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Luka Carroll</b><br /> Onyx Path Freelancer &amp; Developer<br /> <i>Working On: </i>C20 Player's Guide, Lunars<br /> <i>Worked On: </i>V20 TMR, Demon STG, C20, Book of Freeholds, Conquering Heroes, Building A Legend, Dragon-Blooded, The Realm","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3785-luka-c","name":"Luka C","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3785_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"175"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-03T20:17:57-07:00","id":1087485,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Holden</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1086863-it-s-out?p=1087404#post1087404\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> As a general thing, we didn't want to do faction or kith-exclusive Arts, feeling that if a power was signature to a kith, it should be part of their birthright/frailty package, or maybe a Merit. A lot of other Arts we discarded as largely redundant with existing Arts, or just dumb (like that one that was nothing but anti-Sovereign), or structurally built so that they were almost impossible to make gel with the Realms system. One thing we were very adamant on while writing the Arts was that all Arts should be usable with all Realms, and that there shouldn't be Arts that could basically only be used with a single Realm. There used to be a -lot- of those. The Realm &quot;aiming&quot; system is a <i>lot</i> of fun and we felt C20 should prominently showcase it, rather than just kind of fumbling around it like it was an obstacle to writing Disciplines.<br /> <br /> The Adhene Arts didn't make it in because they were outside the scope of the chapter. It sure wasn't for lack of interest, the Adhene are my favorite thing in Changeling. Maybe they'll show up in a supplement? That's up to Matt.<br /> <br /> The Shadow Court Arts went the way of the dodo both due to the trend toward anti-exclusivity in the Arts chapter, and because they were kinda stinky conceptually-- &quot;fuck you Sovereign, you're not the boss of me&quot; and &quot;the roofie Art&quot; weren't adding a ton to the game, especially since there were already like three other more generalized arts for fucking with people's heads that could easily cover what Aphrodisia did. So Aphrodisia got demoted from a full Art to a single cantrip to replicate the pine cone comic from Oglaf.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks for the answer! Your reasoning is pretty solid; I'm sold.<br /> <br /> I'd love for the Adhene to get more love in future supplements. After reading all the new Thallain (which are great), I was kind of hoping to get some new Adhene (maybe the Aslynthi).<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">I actually liked Contempt, because I felt an anti-Sovereign was logical to maintain a secret society that opposed Sovereign's wielders. However, Sovereign has been changed significantly in this edition and all for the better, in my opinion. With Sovereign being slightly less overpowering, available to all, and not being completely useless against those with higher titles, means it's no longer necessary to have an anti-Sovereign for the Shadow Court. I really love the bit about Sovereign being dependent on context and environment. The nobles might be all-powerful at court, but don't try to pull rank on a Nocker in her workshop! </span></span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5910-csschulz","name":"CSSchulz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5910_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-03T21:14:53-07:00","id":1087501,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1086863-it-s-out?p=1086980#post1086980\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Everything was incredibly cut down, kind of like the Fera were in the W20 core. Expanding upon them is going to be the work of several books. At least the Mannikins have listed birthrights and frailties in this version! (^VVVVVV^)<br /> <br /> On that note, I see that in this cut-down version, the Hsien had their Yin and Yang tempers changed to a 1-5 scale. The one thing I think one might absolutely need to re-evaluate, though, is the name of the metal kamuii, before it gets worked in again as something fixed. I stand by my assumption that chu-ih-yu is a highly mangled form of Ch'ih-yu (Chiyou in Hanyu Pinyin), based on the presence of other notable legendary emperor and divine names in the ranks (Chu-jung being Zhurong and Hou-chi being Houji, Lord of Millet) and... creative misspelling like the Dragon Tear Discipline from KotE, which is so off that I can't even bear to type out right now, or the Mokole floating Gift (ditto). Also, if you are using Wade-Giles Romanization of Mandarin as the Chinese kith names seem to be, each syllable is separated by a dash (i.e. Fu-hsi instead of Fu Hsi).</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Keep in mind the celtic spellings are rather archaic (and I think sometimes just wrong) as well. For instance, the modern spelling of &quot;sidhe&quot; is &quot;s\u00ed&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10243-zenten","name":"zenten","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10243_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"488"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-03T21:19:41-07:00","id":1087503,"title":"","content":"The Denizens arts : you have Discord which I can't see a need for with Dragon's Ire becoming a full art(they even have the same backstory), I would readily accept something like Mythbane as a reasonable unleashing for Dragon's ire. Oneriormancy which got taken, and Autumn way which would get confusing Autumn Contract and should probably be an innate power like how Nunnhei got spirit Link made innate, Zeitgeist could be maybe added to something else and Reality's Horror is &quot;Here's Chimestry 5 from Vampire.. because reasons&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-03T21:46:39-07:00","id":1087510,"title":"","content":"I don't see mine in my Email BOX!!!! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-03T22:19:19-07:00","id":1087517,"title":"","content":"Found it! Nifty!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-03T22:56:24-07:00","id":1087526,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>zenten</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1086863-it-s-out?p=1087501#post1087501\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Keep in mind the celtic spellings are rather archaic (and I think sometimes just wrong) as well. For instance, the modern spelling of &quot;sidhe&quot; is &quot;s\u00ed&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Wade-Giles is already quite archaic, since it replaced the even-older Legge form and had to undergo a change in notation because certain Mandarin sounds changed back in the mid-19th century (it's why we call Beijing, well, by that name instead of Beiking, or Peiking if you're going by Wade-Giles and Peking for Legge). What's more, even if the Gaelic, Welsh and such are horribly mangled doesn't mean that it's a necessity to repeat it for all the other names. It means that you take the time to correct them. And (cringe) Chi'iu Muh, if any new KotE material happens (It should be Ch'ih-mu or Chimu, depending on which Romanization you're using).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-03T23:26:04-07:00","id":1087536,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1086863-it-s-out?p=1087526#post1087526\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Wade-Giles is already quite archaic, since it replaced the even-older Legge form and had to undergo a change in notation because certain Mandarin sounds changed back in the mid-19th century (it's why we call Beijing, well, by that name instead of Beiking, or Peiking if you're going by Wade-Giles and Peking for Legge). What's more, even if the Gaelic, Welsh and such are horribly mangled doesn't mean that it's a necessity to repeat it for all the other names. It means that you take the time to correct them. And (cringe) Chi'iu Muh, if any new KotE material happens (It should be Ch'ih-mu or Chimu, depending on which Romanization you're using).</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> or Dragon Tears to match all the other soul Arts like Obligation, Tapestry, etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-03T23:28:02-07:00","id":1087540,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1086863-it-s-out?p=1087536#post1087536\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> or Dragon Tears to match all the other soul Arts like Obligation, Tapestry, etc.</div> </div> </div> </div>Also a viable option, and what its name was in Blood and Silk, I think.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-04T01:32:39-07:00","id":1087571,"title":"","content":"wrong subject<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2809,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2809-batro","user":"batro","date":". 05-04-2017, 06:30 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2809-batro","name":"batro","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"24"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-04T02:04:07-07:00","id":1087578,"title":"","content":"The Goblins cannot fix anything they did not build themselves seems...intense...to not be a frailty.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-04T11:21:44-07:00","id":1087815,"title":"","content":"Got mine Tuesday night. On my second read through.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Onyx Path Kickstarters I back.<br /> W20, MtC, CB20, DtD, MtAs20, BotW20, Wraith 20th.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1442-paladindemo","name":"PaladinDemo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1442_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"622"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-04T11:30:26-07:00","id":1087822,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1086863-it-s-out?p=1087090#post1087090\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like the new write-ups for the Legacies; I can actually see myself playing an Unseelie protagonist now.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yay, I'm glad they're working as intended! The Legacies were the first thing I wrote, so I was still hesitant to change things too much. I still tried to write them more from an individualist slant instead of the hardcore evil they sometimes read as in second edition. It worked out pretty well when I was given the Courts stretch goal to write and could incorporate that into the Unseelie Code <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Also, because I saw someone complaining that the Players Guide Legacies aren't in there, I *really* wanted to include them! I tried several times to make them fit, but I just didn't have the word count to make it happen.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Charlie Cantrell</b><br /> Onyx Path Freelancer <hr />Changeling: The Dreaming 20th Anniversary Edition, Conquering Heroes, Book of Freeholds, Guide to the Night, C20 Players Guide","edited":{"userid":648,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/648-pookaknight","user":"PookaKnight","date":". 05-04-2017, 02:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/648-pookaknight","name":"PookaKnight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar648_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"690"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-04T11:49:52-07:00","id":1087831,"title":"","content":"Also, I have a request about Wallpaper. It looks awesome, but regretfully very, very busy to actually use like one. I can barely see my Desktop icons.<br /> <br /> Could you, folks, whoever responsible for that, make two more versions of it? One without Kith figures and the other one without Kith-emblems?<br /> <br /> It would'be been perfect if you made several versions with free-four Kiths cluttered to the left side or in the center...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>...","edited":{"userid":5211,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5211-firkraag","user":"Firkraag","date":". 05-04-2017, 03:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5211-firkraag","name":"Firkraag","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5211_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-04T12:06:20-07:00","id":1087838,"title":"","content":"I don't want to clutter up the errata thread, but since I wrote the wolpertinger, I wanted to respond to this.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dfunkmale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1086773-c20-backer-pdf-errata-thread?p=1087832#post1087832\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also note that some of the items listed in the &quot;Revelry&quot; sections for various Kith seem to have more to do with interacting with others than finding glamour in oneself. See [/B][/SIZE][/FONT][B]Autumn Sidhe (109) and Wolpertinger (452) for examples that might need clarification.</div> </div> </div> </div>Revelry is an action the changeling can take that resonates with her kith's dream that produces Glamour. For some kiths, that can be an action taken completely alone. For others, such as the wolpertinger, it requires interacting with others.<br /> <br /> The path to finding Glamour within oneself is Rapture <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Charlie Cantrell</b><br /> Onyx Path Freelancer <hr />Changeling: The Dreaming 20th Anniversary Edition, Conquering Heroes, Book of Freeholds, Guide to the Night, C20 Players Guide","edited":{"userid":648,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/648-pookaknight","user":"PookaKnight","date":". 05-04-2017, 03:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/648-pookaknight","name":"PookaKnight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar648_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"690"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-04T12:57:40-07:00","id":1087870,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baroness Nerak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1086863-it-s-out?p=1087578#post1087578\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Goblins cannot fix anything they did not build themselves seems...intense...to not be a frailty.</div> </div> </div> </div>They don't want to fix other people's things. They want to break everything and maim everyone they can. Because of this absolute malice, their Birthright of being able to explode virtually anything in the most catastrophic way imaginable has this drawback, because they simply don't care about fixing things.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Luka Carroll</b><br /> Onyx Path Freelancer &amp; Developer<br /> <i>Working On: </i>C20 Player's Guide, Lunars<br /> <i>Worked On: </i>V20 TMR, Demon STG, C20, Book of Freeholds, Conquering Heroes, Building A Legend, Dragon-Blooded, The Realm","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3785-luka-c","name":"Luka C","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3785_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"175"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-04T13:03:40-07:00","id":1087875,"title":"","content":"Echoing Maggie. While there are certainly enough rules to play a Thallain as a PC if people really want to, they're Changeling's equivalent of Black Spiral Dancers and Nephandi. Thallain don't build things up. They exist solely to tear down.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Charlie Cantrell</b><br /> Onyx Path Freelancer <hr />Changeling: The Dreaming 20th Anniversary Edition, Conquering Heroes, Book of Freeholds, Guide to the Night, C20 Players Guide","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/648-pookaknight","name":"PookaKnight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar648_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"690"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-04T13:04:36-07:00","id":1087877,"title":"","content":"I just have a player who has been playing her Goblin off and on for 20 years who is a weaponsmith, so trying to compensate. One of the handful in my spontaneous game. Regardless, thanks for answerin