ay a Thallain as a PC if people really want to, they're Changeling's equivalent of Black Spiral Dancers and Nephandi. Thallain don't build things up. They exist solely to tear down.</div> </div> </div> </div>BSDs, sure. But not Nephandi. There's a different equivalent for that now. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar56_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"56\" data-vbnamecard=\"56\">Baroness Nerak</a>: What works for your table works for your table. I just wanted to clarify, and absolutely do what you (and she) feel will work best for your playstyles. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Luka Carroll</b><br /> Onyx Path Freelancer &amp; Developer<br /> <i>Working On: </i>C20 Player's Guide, Lunars<br /> <i>Worked On: </i>V20 TMR, Demon STG, C20, Book of Freeholds, Conquering Heroes, Building A Legend, Dragon-Blooded, The Realm","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3785-luka-c","name":"Luka C","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3785_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"175"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-04T13:41:59-07:00","id":1087897,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maggie C</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1086863-it-s-out?p=1087894#post1087894\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">BSDs, sure. But not Nephandi. There's a different equivalent for that now. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Hahahaha! I suppose that's true! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <b>Edit to channel his inner pooka:</b> Or maybe we have *twice* the Nephandi of other game lines! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Charlie Cantrell</b><br /> Onyx Path Freelancer <hr />Changeling: The Dreaming 20th Anniversary Edition, Conquering Heroes, Book of Freeholds, Guide to the Night, C20 Players Guide","edited":{"userid":648,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/648-pookaknight","user":"PookaKnight","date":". 05-04-2017, 04:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/648-pookaknight","name":"PookaKnight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar648_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"690"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-04T13:52:11-07:00","id":1087904,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#222222\">I think Nephandi is a pretty cool guy. Eh kills nioccents and doesnt afraid of anything.<br /> <br /> All they need is a hug.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5211-firkraag","name":"Firkraag","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5211_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-04T14:38:05-07:00","id":1087920,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rabbit Pooka</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1086863-it-s-out?p=1087328#post1087328\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's a gorgeous book and I'm loving a lot of what I'm seeing, I'm just supremely disappointed that the ridiculous pooka frailty remained as written. Guess pooka are not meant to have jobs, bank accounts, or access the internet without burning through their willpower. Wow. How utterly stupid. Ugh. First house rule of many, I'm sure. Great work otherwise...</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That should be <i>or</i> spend a point of Willpower, yes. Maybe put it in the errata thread?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13-blackhatmatt","name":"blackhatmatt","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"464"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-04T16:35:36-07:00","id":1087984,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>blackhatmatt</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1086863-it-s-out?p=1087920#post1087920\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> That should be <i>or</i> spend a point of Willpower, yes. Maybe put it in the errata thread?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> But you can always spend a point of willpower to succeed on Willpower rolls.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10243-zenten","name":"zenten","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10243_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"488"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-04T16:36:41-07:00","id":1087986,"title":"","content":"So, can more glamour be given to the lasting enchanted? If not it seems like it wouldn't be very lasting, due to Banality, and so given that you can never enchant them again it doesn't really make sense to ever use it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10243-zenten","name":"zenten","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10243_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"488"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-04T17:44:24-07:00","id":1088017,"title":"","content":"So, why Infusion was taken out?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5211-firkraag","name":"Firkraag","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5211_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-04T19:15:29-07:00","id":1088051,"title":"","content":"Ideas how an Unseelie Grump can &quot;Interpret&quot; &quot;Provide neccesitys for those in their care&quot; <br /> <br /> The Grump immunity seems to allow them to work as social workers or teachers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-04T20:10:44-07:00","id":1088078,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1086863-it-s-out?p=1088051#post1088051\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ideas how an Unseelie Grump can &amp;quot;Interpret&amp;quot; &amp;quot;Provide neccesitys for those in their care&amp;quot; <br /> <br /> The Grump immunity seems to allow them to work as social workers or teachers.</div> </div> </div> </div>Tough love: It's what's for dinner! Also, bad students.<br /> <br /> On a more general note, the book is fantastic, and I'm thrilled. Some of the weirder inconsistencies are gone from the setting info - no &quot;science is bad&quot; in sight - and the rules got a much-needed tune-up. The Arts are pretty much what I wanted; the Fae actually feel powerful, and suddenly every other splat in the World of Darkness saying &quot;Dear god, don't aggravate the fairies&quot; makes sense (plus, y'know, half the word count in the Arts chapter isn't dedicated to explaining what you CAN'T do with a given Cantrip). The chapter on the Dreaming, while obviously cut down from Dreams and Nightmares for space reasons, was one of my favorites, with some excellent story fodder in every example.<br /> <br /> So, bravo and thank you to everyone responsible! CtD was always one of my favorite RPGs in total, &quot;warts and all.&quot; Now, there's far fewer warts, and a lot more all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4732-drazosh","name":"Drazosh","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"50"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-04T22:45:45-07:00","id":1088111,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PookaKnight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1086863-it-s-out?p=1087875#post1087875\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Echoing Maggie. While there are certainly enough rules to play a Thallain as a PC if people really want to, they're Changeling's equivalent of Black Spiral Dancers and Nephandi. Thallain don't build things up. They exist solely to tear down.</div> </div> </div> </div>Having played an Ogre, a Goblin, a Beastie, and a Bogart at various times I don't really see where that reading on Thallain is coming from. They're definitely more &quot;at home&quot; in the WoD than Kithain, but putting them in a category with BSDs and Nephandi just doesn't track.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-05T02:10:45-07:00","id":1088156,"title":"","content":"Well this version seems to elevate them as setting antagonists somewhat.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-05T03:30:26-07:00","id":1088177,"title":"","content":"Yeah, they've changed a bit for C20. Now they're one of the big bads of the setting. They're not merely double Unseelie. They have a Nightmare Legacy that is permanently primary.<br /> <br /> The Thallain are actively trying to destroy human civilization to return people to a more primal, animalistic state. They want to completely eliminate the Tuathan Dream so their Fomorian masters can hold sway over the Dreaming once more.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Charlie Cantrell</b><br /> Onyx Path Freelancer <hr />Changeling: The Dreaming 20th Anniversary Edition, Conquering Heroes, Book of Freeholds, Guide to the Night, C20 Players Guide","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/648-pookaknight","name":"PookaKnight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar648_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"690"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-05T05:49:24-07:00","id":1088224,"title":"","content":"Considering what you've said about Dark Ages, anyone who perpetuates pointless conflict is bad guy in this.<br /> <br /> Thallain, Kithain; Seelie, Unseelie; Thuatha, Fomorian.<br /> <br /> Dreaming plays no favorites.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>...","edited":{"userid":5211,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5211-firkraag","user":"Firkraag","date":". 05-05-2017, 12:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5211-firkraag","name":"Firkraag","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5211_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-05T06:26:11-07:00","id":1088244,"title":"","content":"Yep, the Dreaming doesn't play favorites. It took a lot of hard work and sacrifice to make humanity ascendant and establish the Tuathan Dream as the dominant view of the Dreaming. The Kithain in a lot of ways seem hell bent on pissing all that away. There's no one waiting in the wings to come in at the last minute to save them. The Dreaming is just as happy with Fomorian rulers as it was with the Tuatha. If some other type of dream arises and becomes dominant, it'll be just as happy with that one. The only people who can save the Kithain are themselves.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Charlie Cantrell</b><br /> Onyx Path Freelancer <hr />Changeling: The Dreaming 20th Anniversary Edition, Conquering Heroes, Book of Freeholds, Guide to the Night, C20 Players Guide","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/648-pookaknight","name":"PookaKnight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar648_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"690"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-05T08:47:46-07:00","id":1088313,"title":"","content":"On the whole I love it. I'm also not a fan of the development of High King David, and I preferred my Liam oathbreakers to the new Liam Scathach-Lite. Keeping the Scathach unaligned was also something I liked and will keep.<br /> <br /> I love the idea of the Evanescence, although I'd probably still tie it into the Week of Nightmares (I kinda wish the M20 Future Fates had been borrowed for C20 too). It does make me think of that early 00s rock band, of course...<br /> <br /> I like the ties to DA:F. I'm not sold on the addition of seasonal Arts, as most of them overlap, particularly with the Arts that already had a lot of overlap (Primal/Pyretics/Skycraft, all of which are kind of Nature the Art). But I'm glad that there are fewer of them in general.<br /> <br /> The Thallain are much improved and the Dauntain finally make sense--and WOW! They're amazing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-05T08:49:32-07:00","id":1088314,"title":"","content":"Oh, I'm also not liking how the Adhene are basically just called the Dark-Kin now. Adhene only gets used a couple of times in the whole book.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-05T09:24:41-07:00","id":1088328,"title":"","content":"So I've been doing a few read-throughs of the book, to the point that I posted an actual review somewhere else (not going to inflict it on people twice). I'm ultimately finding C20 to be something of a pretty mixed bag for me.<br /> <br /> There's a bunch of stuff I really, really like (crafting, the new take on seemings, ways to deal with banality, the great art, curses and frailties being cleaned up and playable, a lot of other stuff). There's things I dislike but can live with (still no siochain guidelines or exploration of what it does, Dice being the head of house Danaan and or existing at all, Dragon's Ire being objectively terrible and useless at most levels, magic being harder to use from how it reads, various other things).<br /> <br /> But there are a few things I just can't bring myself past. The metaplot is one of the big ones. I'm not a fan of High King David as broken compromised nonentity, and I'm super not a fan of the whole 99.999% of the nobility in Concordia have become awful hoarder d-bags letting the fae outside their holds die (barring Liam and Scathach I guess). I liked that a lot of the conflicts in changeling didn't have an objectively &quot;right&quot; side (and there was vs the Fomorians/Thallain to balance that out as far as being more clear by contrast), but that seems to have been entirely abandoned as far as the commoner/nobility thing, to the point that the latter read as the default setting villains barring the Fomorians/Thallain.<br /> <br /> The other thing is Unleashing. I don't know, it just feels too good? Like to the point that any significant combat or other plot resolution scene may as well boil down to who manages to get an Unleashing off first. There aren't a lot of guidelines or sense of limitations to it, with examples of buildings being thrown around, time travel, and what seem like insta kill effects. I would have really appreciated a firmer sense of how to adjudicate that stuff other than &quot;narratively wing it&quot;. It just otherwise feels like one of those things that can be a path to ST/player acrimony on what any given Unleashing manages to do (yes, less likely say with in person table top, where you know people and are interacting directly, but for instance in online gaming where people are often entirely strangers to each other, whole different bag).<br /> <br /> I suppose it helps that in going through the book, you can honestly feel the love of the game motivating the writing and the ideas, which is a major plus. It makes me want to try and work past this stuff, but, I don't know. Like I say, mixed bag. <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12141-markk","name":"MarkK","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-05T09:30:53-07:00","id":1088330,"title":"","content":"Metaplot is easily changed or ignored.<br /> <br /> My understanding of the Unleashing is it lets you do just about anything within the context of an Art, not just limit yourself to the pre-set powers. Kind of like dipping into Mage a bit. I don't have all the info, but perhaps there is a way to make it harder or more costly, so it's a once a story thing, rather than who can do it first.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1885-crackedman","name":"CrackedMan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1885_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"254"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-05T09:36:03-07:00","id":1088336,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adambeyoncelowe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1086863-it-s-out?p=1088313#post1088313\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The Thallain are much improved and the Dauntain finally make sense--and WOW! They're amazing.</div> </div> </div> </div><img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />DD<br /> <br /> I've loved Dauntain since 1e, but they werent exactly easy to properly reconcile, and they always felt off theme. I still can't quite convince myself that it's not homebrew, but I've been waiting to see what people thought, so thanks! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Luka Carroll</b><br /> Onyx Path Freelancer &amp; Developer<br /> <i>Working On: </i>C20 Player's Guide, Lunars<br /> <i>Worked On: </i>V20 TMR, Demon STG, C20, Book of Freeholds, Conquering Heroes, Building A Legend, Dragon-Blooded, The Realm","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3785-luka-c","name":"Luka C","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3785_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"175"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-05T09:36:35-07:00","id":1088337,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MarkK</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1086863-it-s-out?p=1088328#post1088328\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The other thing is Unleashing. I don't know, it just feels too good? Like to the point that any significant combat or other plot resolution scene may as well boil down to who manages to get an Unleashing off first. There aren't a lot of guidelines or sense of limitations to it, with examples of buildings being thrown around, time travel, and what seem like insta kill effects. I would have really appreciated a firmer sense of how to adjudicate that stuff other than &quot;narratively wing it&quot;. It just otherwise feels like one of those things that can be a path to ST/player acrimony on what any given Unleashing manages to do (yes, less likely say with in person table top, where you know people and are interacting directly, but for instance in online gaming where people are often entirely strangers to each other, whole different bag).</div> </div> </div> </div>I suggest you to take a look at Dungeon World and similar games (also known as PbtA). There's the game mechanics you could steal, that might work very well for Unleashing. You know, as an underlying principle.<br /> <br /> Doing the Unleashing is always risky and comes with the inherent cost of Nightmare rating rising up. When changelings screw up with their magic they screw up big time. It's like &quot;too good&quot;, but for ST instead. Though, a good player enjoys big failures as much, as big victories.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>...","edited":{"userid":5211,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5211-firkraag","user":"Firkraag","date":". 05-05-2017, 08:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5211-firkraag","name":"Firkraag","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5211_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-05T09:41:14-07:00","id":1088340,"title":"","content":"The thing about &quot;metaplot can be easily changed or ignored&quot;, well again, less so in online gaming for example (which is most of my gaming these days), where often for sake of simplicity and common ground, people roll ahead with as close to the book as possible. The other thing is, with that being the metaplot, that's going to be the metaplot in any future books for C20, or, since this would have had to get white wolf approval, whatever theoretical Changeling things they do. And when I feel frozen out by it, it puts me in a bit of a &quot;do I even want to get these other books then&quot;, which is a crummy place to be. I really, really want to be on board with this edition, y'know?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12141-markk","name":"MarkK","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-05T09:43:41-07:00","id":1088341,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I suggest you to take a look at Dungeon World and similar games (also known as PbtA). There'smechanics you could steal, that might work very well for Unleashing. You know, as an underlying principle. </div> </div> </div>Thanks, I'll take a look at it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Doing the Unleashing is always risky and comes with the inherent cost of Nightmare rating rising up. When changelings crew up with their magic they screw up big time. It's like &quot;too good&quot;, but for ST instead. Though, a good player enjoys big failures as much, as big victories. </div> </div> </div>Yeah, but that's just acrimony in the other direction really. It's one thing to talk about good players enjoying big failures, but especially when it's a matter of near pure narrative, there's a lot of ways for that to go wrong. And there's certainly &quot;well don't use it in your games then&quot;, but it's a big new cool thing, and it's a pretty easy way to put people off by proclaiming &quot;nope to all of it.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12141,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12141-markk","user":"MarkK","date":".  thing I was replying to was edited 05-05-2017, 12:52 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12141-markk","name":"MarkK","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-05T09:50:01-07:00","id":1088342,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CrackedMan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1086863-it-s-out?p=1088330#post1088330\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My understanding of the Unleashing is it lets you do just about anything within the context of an Art, not just limit yourself to the pre-set powers. Kind of like dipping into Mage a bit. I don't have all the info, but perhaps there is a way to make it harder or more costly, so it's a once a story thing, rather than who can do it first.</div> </div> </div> </div>Unleashing is nowhere near the &quot;I win button&quot; some people seem to think. The only result where you come out mostly ahead is if you happen to roll equal to or fewer successes than you have dots in the Art you're Unleashing. Botch, failing the roll, and rolling more successes than you have dots in the Art you're Unleashing all have rather drastic downsides. Hell, even a successful result reveals your fae mien for a few rounds up to the whole scene. Depending on the circumstance (and your kith) that could be disastrous in and of itself.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11658-rabbit-pooka","name":"Rabbit Pooka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11658_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"65"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-05T09:55:54-07:00","id":1088345,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MarkK</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1086863-it-s-out?p=1088340#post1088340\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The thing about &quot;metaplot can be easily changed or ignored&quot;, well again, less so in online gaming for example (which is most of my gaming these days), where often for sake of simplicity and common ground, people roll ahead with as close to the book as possible. The other thing is, with that being the metaplot, that's going to be the metaplot in any future books for C20, or, since this would have had to get white wolf approval, whatever theoretical Changeling things they do. And when I feel frozen out by it, it puts me in a bit of a &quot;do I even want to get these other books then&quot;, which is a crummy place to be. I really, really want to be on board with this edition, y'know?</div> </div> </div> </div>I get that, I guess I just have always considered metaplot stuff background noise to whatever the PCs are doing. What happens to HKD is of little concern to my story and your nobles could be part of the 1% who are different. I rarely ever consider the metaplot and that's rarely made it an issue for me to decide if a given book is something I want to buy. I'm not trying to tell you that your concerns aren't valid, just that as far as problems with this edition go, it's a pretty minor one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1885-crackedman","name":"CrackedMan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1885_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"254"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-05T09:57:20-07:00","id":1088347,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rabbit Pooka</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1086863-it-s-out?p=1088342#post1088342\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Unleashing is nowhere near the &quot;I win button&quot; some people seem to think. The only result where you come out mostly ahead is if you happen to roll equal to or fewer successes than you have dots in the Art you're Unleashing. Botch, failing the roll, and rolling more successes than you have dots in the Art you're Unleashing all have rather drastic downsides. Hell, even a successful result reveals your fae mien for a few rounds up to the whole scene. Depending on the circumstance (and your kith) that could be disastrous in and of itself.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sadly I don't have the book, so I was just going off what MarkK said. It sounds like a neat new option.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1885-crackedman","name":"CrackedMan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1885_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"254"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-05T09:58:54-07:00","id":1088349,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rabbit Pooka</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1086863-it-s-out?p=1088342#post1088342\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Unleashing is nowhere near the &quot;I win button&quot; some people seem to think. The only result where you come out mostly ahead is if you happen to roll equal to or fewer successes than you have dots in the Art you're Unleashing. Botch, failing the roll, and rolling more successes than you have dots in the Art you're Unleashing all have rather drastic downsides. Hell, even a successful result reveals your fae mien for a few rounds up to the whole scene. Depending on the circumstance (and your kith) that could be disastrous in and of itself.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would say to that though, look at the examples given for when you do manage to come out ahead, that's a pretty big pile of &quot;I win/resolve my problem&quot; to take the risk for. Even with a &quot;succeed, but there are consequences&quot; result.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12141-markk","name":"MarkK","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-05T10:36:19-07:00","id":1088377,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MarkK</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1086863-it-s-out?p=1088349#post1088349\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would say to that though, look at the examples given for when you do manage to come out ahead, that's a pretty big pile of &quot;I win/resolve my problem&quot; to take the risk for. Even with a &quot;succeed, but there are consequences&quot; result.</div> </div> </div> </div>Unleashing really comes in two varieties: mechanical and narrative. Most of the mechanical ones either replicate existing levels of Arts, like &quot;go back in time&quot; (Chronos 4), or simply cause or prevent damage. Using the fairly standard one success = one damage isn't out of line, nor is simply cribbing the duration charts from other levels or other Arts to determine how long something lasts. For the ones that replicate existing Art effects, like go back in time (Chronos 4 already does it), just look at those effects for guidance. <br /> <br /> Then there's the narrative ones. Like Chronos' &quot;suffer eternally&quot; or Chicanery's &quot;the world forgets this day&quot;. For those, it's all about the narrative rather than the mechanics. So it comes down to what you want to allow as the GM. Just because a player Unleashes Chronos with one success you're going to give them something like &quot;suffer eternally&quot; by what...making the target's wounds never heal. Well, sure, but that's arguably a terrible call. Far better to inflict something like a reverse of the merit Increased Pain Threshold. Granted, it takes a bit of work on the GM's side, but it's worth it. Just don't be ridiculous with it. And never forget the consequences. One of your PCs just knocked down a building? Someone's going to be pissed and come after whoever did that. <br /> <br /> Short of that you likely have a problem player on your hand and/or an overly permissive GM. If you're willing to let one roll destroy the campaign, that's more about you and your table than the rules not giving enough guidance. &quot;But it doesn't say I <u><i><b>can't</b></i></u> do that!&quot; Well, that's on you and your table and I'd guess that nothing short of a phone book with computer code level precision is going to be enough to satisfy. Just use a bit of imagination.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11658-rabbit-pooka","name":"Rabbit Pooka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11658_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"65"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-05T10:40:10-07:00","id":1088379,"title":"","content":"The context for Unleashing, such as it is, doesn't really come off as &quot;just duplicates an existing effect&quot;, is I guess what I'm saying there.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Short of that you likely have a problem player on your hand and/or an overly permissive GM. If you're willing to let one roll destroy the campaign, that's more about you and your table than the rules not giving enough guidance. &quot;But it doesn't say I <u><i><b>can't</b></i></u> do that!&quot; Well, that's on you and your table and I'd guess that nothing short of a phone book with computer code level precision is going to be enough to satisfy. Just use a bit of imagination. </div> </div> </div>That's.. really insulting dude. Thanks anyway for your advice.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12141-markk","name":"MarkK","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-05T10:46:59-07:00","id":1088381,"title":"","content":"I have mitigated feelings about the book.<br /> <br /> I really like some of the new Arts and Cantrips, the new versions of Seemings are great, Unleashing is an awesome thing to have in Changeling, the crafting rules for chimera and treasures are simple and being able to play a gallain is really nice.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, Nightmare dices look like they're going to complicate gameplay, the rare kiths' writeups feel minimalistic, Obas and River Hags still feel like they're not made to be used by players (try and play the toy box campaign with them!), Merfolk lost their Houses' distinct Boons and Flaws.<br /> <br /> I'm also concerned with the Thallain dominated Shadow Court being associated with Black Lives Matter, the Arab Spring and the Occupy Movement. A sensitivity reader or two would perhaps not have been superfluous. Chief Greyhhawk of House Gwydion &quot;going native&quot; is as problematic now as it was then, almost everything about the Fiefs of Bright Paradise made me cringe, Africa is still a mystery in spite of all the far travelling, storytelling changelings coming from it. Speaking of which, the art for the Kiths has the stereotypically subservient and violent kiths as black people, while the one kith supposed to come from Africa or southern Asia is a really pale causasian man, which is clumsy at best.<br /> <br /> C20 is a good core book, and I'm really happy to get a updated version of one of White Wolf's best games, but there's still some elements that need work.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>When will you rage?","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1405-anteros","name":"Anteros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1405_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-05T10:55:23-07:00","id":1088384,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MarkK</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1086863-it-s-out?p=1088379#post1088379\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The context for Unleashing, such as it is, doesn't really come off as &quot;just duplicates an existing effect&quot;, is I guess what I'm saying there.<br /> <br /> That's.. really insulting dude. Thanks anyway for your advice.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry if my comments seem harsh. I'm just having trouble wrapping my head around the complaint. It's a game about unfettered imagination and the Unleashing mechanic is specifically about letting players pour their unfettered imagination into the game world...and your complaint is that there's not enough guidelines for how to handle that as a GM...whose sole job is to bring their unfettered imagination to bear on constructing and running a fictitious game world filled with creatures of pure imagination.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11658-rabbit-pooka","name":"Rabbit Pooka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11658_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"65"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-05T11:00:57-07:00","id":1088386,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Anteros</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1086863-it-s-out?p=1088381#post1088381\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have mitigated feelings about the book.<br /> <br /> I really like some of the new Arts and Cantrips, the new versions of Seemings are great, Unleashing is an awesome thing to have in Changeling, the crafting rules for chimera and treasures are simple and being able to play a gallain is really nice.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, Nightmare dices look like they're going to complicate gameplay, the rare kiths' writeups feel minimalistic, Obas and River Hags still feel like they're not made to be used by players (try and play the toy box campaign with them!), Merfolk lost their Houses' distinct Boons and Flaws.<br /> <br /> I'm also concerned with the Thallain dominated Shadow Court being associated with Black Lives Matter, the Arab Spring and the Occupy Movement. A sensitivity reader or two would perhaps not have been superfluous. Chief Greyhhawk of House Gwydion &quot;going native&quot; is as problematic now as it was then, almost everything about the Fiefs of Bright Paradise made me cringe, Africa is still a mystery in spite of all the far travelling, storytelling changelings coming from it. Speaking of which, the art for the Kiths has the stereotypically subservient and violent kiths as black people, while the one kith supposed to come from Africa or southern Asia is a really pale causasian man, which is clumsy at best.<br /> <br /> C20 is a good core book, and I'm really happy to get a updated version of one of White Wolf's best games, but there's still some elements that need work.</div> </div> </div> </div>That one of the pre-release gameplay samples was about how gentrification is good also gave me pause. Most of it's easily ignored, but that it's present does give one pause. I noticed the Irish stereotype of loud-mouth drunk brawler is alive and well. But yeah, I was kind of shocked about the boggan, eshu, and redcap depictions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11658-rabbit-pooka","name":"Rabbit Pooka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11658_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"65"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-05T11:04:16-07:00","id":1088387,"title":"","content":"As a big fan of generalist, freeform use of magic that greatly appreciated the DA:F system, I welcome C20 Unleashing as a serious step in the right direction in comparison to the terribly messy and static 2e way of doing things. Besides adding a much-welcome dose of Mage-style flexibility in supposed-to-be-dynamic fae magic, it makes investment in low-rating scores in multiple Arts much more sensible and valuable, since it opens up those Arts to possible Unleashing use. Provided you are willing to accept significant side effects and consequences for your feats of wild magic, rolling more successes than you have dots in the Art you're Unleashing *works* at solving the problem you are facing. This way, a generalist, dynamic fae sorcerer character build of a few dots in a half-dozen-plus Arts becomes a valid high-risk, high-reward approach for a jack-of-all-trades, freeform, reckless magic playstyle. Playing against specializations and tried-and-true spell-list magic effects now becomes a somewhat viable if risky option. Strict comparisons of power levels aside, it becomes rather more feasible to play modern fae characters the way you could do it in DA.F. And I'much thankful for it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1949,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1949-irioth","user":"Irioth","date":". 05-05-2017, 02:52 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1949-irioth","name":"Irioth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"566"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-05T11:10:13-07:00","id":1088390,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rabbit Pooka</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1086863-it-s-out?p=1088384#post1088384\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Sorry if my comments seem harsh. I'm just having trouble wrapping my head around the complaint. It's a game about unfettered imagination and the Unleashing mechanic is specifically about letting players pour their unfettered imagination into the game world...and your complaint is that there's not enough guidelines for how to handle that as a GM...whose sole job is to bring their unfettered imagination to bear on constructing and running a fictitious game world filled with creatures of pure imagination.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think when the discussion turns to various takes on &quot;then your table is bad and you're probably a terrible GM who doesn't understand Changeling&quot; is where it stops having any productive value.<br /> <br /> I will just note that gaming online is not the same thing as gaming over a table and leave it there. Again, thanks for the advice.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12141-markk","name":"MarkK","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-05T11:11:37-07:00","id":1088391,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rabbit Pooka</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1086863-it-s-out?p=1088386#post1088386\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That one of the pre-release gameplay samples was about how gentrification is good also gave me pause. Most of it's easily ignored, but that it's present does give one pause. I noticed the Irish stereotype of loud-mouth drunk brawler is alive and well. But yeah, I was kind of shocked about the boggan, eshu, and redcap depictions.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah,the Clurichauns' depiction isn't exactly subltle about where it takes its inspiration.<br /> I hope they do something about all this.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>When will you rage?","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1405-anteros","name":"Anteros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1405_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-05T11:22:18-07:00","id":1088393,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Anteros</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1086863-it-s-out?p=1088391#post1088391\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah,the Clurichauns' depiction isn't exactly subltle about where it takes its inspiration.<br /> I hope they do something about all this.</div> </div> </div> </div>Then there's the rapist fantasy that is the Satyr birthright Gift of Pan. Nothing's perfect, sure, but there's a fair amount of problematic stuff in here.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11658-rabbit-pooka","name":"Rabbit Pooka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11658_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"65"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-05T11:27:18-07:00","id":1088394,"title":"","content":"If it's anything, mentioned Gift of Pan in the errata thread, owing to how it almost came close to finally not being a creep festival, then epically refused to stick the landing:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1086773-c20-backer-pdf-errata-thread?p=1088359#post1088359\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/filedata/fetch?filedataid=1074\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1086773-c20-backer-pdf-errata-thread?p=1088359#post1088359\"> C20 Backer PDF errata thread - Onyx Path Forums </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1086773-c20-backer-pdf-errata-thread?p=1088359#post1088359\"> http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1086773-c20-backer-pdf-errata-thread?p=1088359#post1088359 </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> The C20 backer PDF will be sent out soon! Please use this thread to report typos and visual glitches. Please also keep discussion of setting, rules, and other content to other threads. </div> </div> </div><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12141-markk","name":"MarkK","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-05T12:07:10-07:00","id":1088406,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13-blackhatmatt\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar13_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"13\" data-vbnamecard=\"13\">blackhatmatt</a> and all the writers: I wanted to let y'all know that recently I've been utterly consumed with depression, really low, and near a dangerous precipice.<br /> <br /> You'll not believe the positive effect this book has had on me. It's not just the receiving the PDF. It's the quality of the writing, the message in the book's stories, the wonderful art, the love that's gone into every page....It makes me come alive again. This is a game I needed and most importantly, words I needed to read.<br /> <br /> I've never been a massive Changeling fan. You've made me a fan of Changeling, and a fan of all of your work. Thank you. You've made a difference to me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3241-stannis","name":"Stannis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3241_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"115"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-05T12:20:13-07:00","id":1088414,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Anteros</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1086863-it-s-out?p=1088381#post1088381\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have mitigated feelings about the book.<br /> <br /> I really like some of the new Arts and Cantrips, the new versions of Seemings are great, Unleashing is an awesome thing to have in Changeling, the crafting rules for chimera and treasures are simple and being able to play a gallain is really nice.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, Nightmare dices look like they're going to complicate gameplay, the rare kiths' writeups feel minimalistic, Obas and River Hags still feel like they're not made to be used by players (try and play the toy box campaign with them!), Merfolk lost their Houses' distinct Boons and Flaws.<br /> <br /> I'm also concerned with the Thallain dominated Shadow Court being associated with Black Lives Matter, the Arab Spring and the Occupy Movement. A sensitivity reader or two would perhaps not have been superfluous. Chief Greyhhawk of House Gwydion &amp;quot;going native&amp;quot; is as problematic now as it was then, almost everything about the Fiefs of Bright Paradise made me cringe, Africa is still a mystery in spite of all the far travelling, storytelling changelings coming from it. Speaking of which, the art for the Kiths has the stereotypically subservient and violent kiths as black people, while the one kith supposed to come from Africa or southern Asia is a really pale causasian man, which is clumsy at best.<br /> <br /> C20 is a good core book, and I'm really happy to get a updated version of one of White Wolf's best games, but there's still some elements that need work.</div> </div> </div> </div>This all over. I also thought it tried a bit too hard to shoehorn in contemporary fears about people like Trump and the 2% ignoring the 'common' person. I get it, and it's a valid reflection of contemporary culture, but it feels...cheap, maybe? Underdeveloped? I'm undecided.<br /> <br /> The eshu's face is right next to the words where it says they're usually POC. I think that the art notes probably tried to steer away from presenting eshu as the token POC kith (which was a problem), but the text still calls it out. I guess it's that juxtaposition that threw me. I'm not sure what the right answer there is. But I agree that things like making the domestic faerie and the thug faerie black, and the Irish faerie a ginger alcoholic, while making the eshu white, suggests a bit of cognitive dissonance... It makes me question other things when I just wanted to enjoy the magic. I guess that's the weight of the Autumn World creeping in!<br /> <br /> The Caribbean setting fluff was stereotypical, but then Changeling trades in archetypes. It's a tricky path to tread. There's some scary stuff about duppies, lagahoo, soucouyants, etc, in Caribbean myth that Changeling really should look into sometime. Plus, Oba would make more sense being tied to the Caribbean and South America than India and the Middle East, since Yoruba traditions appear in Vodu, Candomble, Santeria, etc. A good friend of mine is a Bajan Yoruba priestess--why wouldn't someone like that inherit an eshu noble soul?<br /> <br /> I still plan to houserule the Actor Realm, too. I just don't think a Dire Enemy would be Actor 4, when someone you know by face alone is Actor 3. I make it my business to know my enemies. But that's my rant over. I promise I do love the book and I'm not trying to be overly negative here. :P<br /> <br /> Onto more things I do love: Unleashing. I'm surprised not to see coaxing and commanding, but I get it. It needs to be more than an easy win button. I may keep those options as a house rule, though. I'm also very glad there's a better system for Bedlam, although I didn't expect it to be tied solely to Nightmare. I feel like getting too Glamour-imbalanced is negative in its own right, without Nightmare entering the picture. Nightmare, in my view, leads to something else...<br /> <br /> I like the new Legacies, and the Nightmare Legacies. I like the crafting rules. I love what's happened with the Enchanted and Autumn People (although some plays really are awful, you know <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />). I really love Brands for Dauntain. So much. They're genuinely kinda disturbing. Ruin is very appropriate too. Love, love, love it.<br /> <br /> I love the art. I love the clarity around the Fomorians now. I love that the kithain history section now incorporates important elements from later supplements up front. And did I mention the art?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-05T12:29:11-07:00","id":1088421,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MarkK</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1086863-it-s-out?p=1088394#post1088394\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If it's anything, mentioned Gift of Pan in the errata thread, owing to how it almost came close to finally not being a creep festival, then epically refused to stick the landing:<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1086773-c20-backer-pdf-errata-thread?p=1088359#post1088359\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...59#post1088359</a></div> </div> </div> </div>To be fair, the C20 writeup of the Gift of Pan explictly states it does not create any new and extraneous compulsion in the subject's psyche, it just awakens and gives a big boost to the person's own dormant urges. Even the failure at the resistance roll that still seems to disturb you is explictly explained as the lusty/passionate/gluttonous side of the subject's psyche winning the inner battle with the prudish/shy/temperate side. It is not really different from being exposed to a concentrated dose of really good porn, revelry-inducing music, or food and failing to resist the urge to indulge then and there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1949,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1949-irioth","user":"Irioth","date":". 05-05-2017, 03:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1949-irioth","name":"Irioth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"566"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-05T12:49:53-07:00","id":1088430,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adambeyoncelowe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1086863-it-s-out?p=1088414#post1088414\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The Caribbean setting fluff was stereotypical, but then Changeling trades in archetypes. It's a tricky path to tread. There's some scary stuff about duppies, lagahoo, soucouyants, etc, in Caribbean myth that Changeling really should look into sometime. Plus, Oba would make more sense being tied to the Caribbean and South America than India and the Middle East, since Yoruba traditions appear in Vodu, Candomble, Santeria, etc. A good friend of mine is a Bajan Yoruba priestess--why wouldn't someone like that inherit an eshu noble soul?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>What bothhered me with thhe Fiefs of Brighht Paradse is that it was written with a European/North American perspective in mind. The whole &quot;pirate of the caribbean&quot; is mostly an European/American fantasy, not a Caribbean one. It's basically saying that Caribbean Changelings were shaped by the fantasies of Americans and Europeans, not those of their own people. Turning an entire region into a tourist stereotype is really creepy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>When will you rage?","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1405-anteros","name":"Anteros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1405_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-05T12:50:45-07:00","id":1088432,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Anteros</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1086863-it-s-out?p=1088381#post1088381\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm also concerned with the Thallain dominated Shadow Court being associated with Black Lives Matter, the Arab Spring and the Occupy Movement...</div> </div> </div> </div>It is really weird, isn't it. The book largely is presented as from the point of view of the commoners and that they're largely right, yet when it comes to the corresponding real-world movements they're presented as corrupted and co-opted by the bad guys. So the fictional commoners are right, but the real-world commoners are corrupted and co-opted. Such a bizarre position to take. Fighting for fictional equality is good, but fighting for real-world equality somehow serves the death of imagination and creativity...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11658-rabbit-pooka","name":"Rabbit Pooka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11658_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"65"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-05T13:11:22-07:00","id":1088444,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Irioth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1086863-it-s-out?p=1088421#post1088421\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> To be fair, the C20 writeup of the Gift of Pan explictly states it does not create any new and extraneous compulsion in the subject's psyche, it just awakens and gives a big boost to the person's own dormant urges. Even the failure at the resistance roll that still seems to disturb you is explictly explained as the lusty/passionate/gluttonous side of the subject's psyche winning the inner battle with the prudish/shy/temperate side. It is not really different from being exposed to a concentrated dose of really good porn, revelry-inducing music, or food and failing to resist the urge to indulge then and there.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> It also says it doesn't force you to do anything. Like, it literally says that. It uses those words. &quot;The Gift of Pan doesn't force anyone to partake in sex or any other activity&quot; is what it says. Apparently that's ambiguous, so please listen to me: <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\">AS DEVELOPER, I OFFICIALLY STATE THAT GIFT OF PAN DOES NOT FORCE ANY CHARACTER TO DO SOMETHING THEY DON'T WANT TO DO. FURTHER, IF YOU'RE PLAYING IN A GAME AND THE STORYTELLER SAYS &quot;THIS SATYR ROLLED A BUNCH OF SUCCESSES AND YOU FAILED YOUR WILLPOWER ROLL SO NOW YOU HAVE TO FUCK SOMEONE,&quot; THAT STORYTELLER IS TERRIBLE AND YOU SHOULD STOP PLAYING WITH THEM.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\">Is that clearer?</span></span> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":11}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13-blackhatmatt","name":"blackhatmatt","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"464"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-05T13:25:37-07:00","id":1088455,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>blackhatmatt</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1086863-it-s-out?p=1088444#post1088444\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It also says it doesn't force you to do anything. Like, it literally says that. It uses those words. &quot;The Gift of Pan doesn't force anyone to partake in sex or any other activity&quot; is what it says. Apparently that's ambiguous, so please listen to me:<br /> <br /> AS DEVELOPER, I OFFICIALLY STATE THAT GIFT OF PAN DOES NOT FORCE ANY CHARACTER TO DO SOMETHING THEY DON'T WANT TO DO. FURTHER, IF YOU'RE PLAYING IN A GAME AND THE STORYTELLER SAYS &quot;THIS SATYR ROLLED A BUNCH OF SUCCESSES AND YOU FAILED YOUR WILLPOWER ROLL SO NOW YOU HAVE TO FUCK SOMEONE,&quot; THAT STORYTELLER IS TERRIBLE AND YOU SHOULD STOP PLAYING WITH THEM.<br /> <br /> Is that clearer?</div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Respectfully, that's not where the ambiguity is. The ambiguity is here:<br /> <br /> &quot;The Gift of Pan doesn\u2019t force anyone to partake in sex or any other activity, but <u><i><b>removes inhibitions</b></i></u> that might normally keep someone from indulging. Rather than creating a new passion, the Gift of Pan <i><u><b>removes the barriers of social convention</b></u></i> that might otherwise prevent someone from being able to completely surrender to an action of passion or revelry...</span><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Those failing a Banality or Willpower roll (difficulty 8) find themselves <u><i><b>helpless to resist indulging their secret desires</b></i></u>.&quot;<br /> <br /> Secret desires are a funny thing. They're secret. They're not discussed. They're not widely known outside the head of the person, and could quite honestly be repressed and therefore largely secret to the person themselves. So who determines what someone's secret desires are in an RPG? The GM for the NPCs and likely the player for PCs...but maybe not. <br /> <br /> You don't think it's a problem, that's clear. That's fine. As someone who plays in games not run by the lead developer, let me tell you, it's going to be a problem. Your </span></span></span>admonition is great and all, but that basically tells me not to game with the vast majority of GMs and players in the community. Give an inch and they take a mile. You're giving an inch and saying it's not a problem. It's all covered by &quot;removes inhibitions&quot; and &quot;removes the barriers of social convention&quot; and &quot;secret desires&quot;. <br /> <br /> It's not mind-control...it's subtler and ambiguous, and therefore worse.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11658-rabbit-pooka","name":"Rabbit Pooka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11658_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"65"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-05T13:29:50-07:00","id":1088457,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rabbit Pooka</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1086863-it-s-out?p=1088455#post1088455\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Respectfully, that's not where the ambiguity is. The ambiguity is here:<br /> <br /> &amp;quot;The Gift of Pan doesn\u2019t force anyone to partake in sex or any other activity, but <u><i><b>removes inhibitions</b></i></u> that might normally keep someone from indulging. Rather than creating a new passion, the Gift of Pan <i><u><b>removes the barriers of social convention</b></u></i> that might otherwise prevent someone from being able to completely surrender to an action of passion or revelry...</span><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Those failing a Banality or Willpower roll (difficulty 8) find themselves <u><i><b>helpless to resist indulging their secret desires</b></i></u>.&amp;quot;<br /> <br /> Secret desires are a funny thing. They're secret. They're not discussed. They're not widely known outside the head of the person, and could quite honestly be repressed and therefore largely secret to the person themselves. So who determines what someone's secret desires are in an RPG? The GM for the NPCs and likely the player for PCs...but maybe not. <br /> <br /> You don't think it's a problem, that's clear. That's fine. As someone who plays in games not run by the lead developer, let me tell you, it's going to be a problem. Your </span></span></span>admonition is great and all, but that basically tells me not to game with the vast majority of GMs and players in the community. Give an inch and they take a mile. You're giving an inch and saying it's not a problem. It's all covered by &amp;quot;removes inhibitions&amp;quot; and &amp;quot;removes the barriers of social convention&amp;quot; and &amp;quot;secret desires&amp;quot;. <br /> <br /> It's not mind-control...it's subtler and ambiguous, and therefore worse.</div> </div> </div> </div>My interpretation is that if you really want to do something, but you think you shouldn't because of insecurity or a fear of how silly you'll look doing it, or if you're like me and sometimes paralyzed with all the nebulous what ifs, it nullifies that and frees them to do what they really want to do. <br /> <br /> If it's going to be decided that violations of a person's comfort zone is okay, that is not a problem with the game, but with the group, and the vast majority of the community simply isn't like that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Luka Carroll</b><br /> Onyx Path Freelancer &amp; Developer<br /> <i>Working On: </i>C20 Player's Guide, Lunars<br /> <i>Worked On: </i>V20 TMR, Demon STG, C20, Book of Freeholds, Conquering Heroes, Building A Legend, Dragon-Blooded, The Realm","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3785-luka-c","name":"Luka C","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3785_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"175"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-05T13:39:58-07:00","id":1088464,"title":"","content":"For me it just boils down to that the &quot;helpless to indulge their secret desires&quot; part reads as contradicting the stuff before it about &quot;cannot force you to etc.&quot;<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12141-markk","name":"MarkK","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-05T13:40:01-07:00","id":1088465,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rabbit Pooka</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1086863-it-s-out?p=1088455#post1088455\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> You don't think it's a problem, that's clear. That's fine. As someone who plays in games not run by the lead developer, let me tell you, it's going to be a problem. Your [/SIZE][/SIZE][/FONT]admonition is great and all, but that basically tells me not to game with the vast majority of GMs and players in the community. Give an inch and they take a mile. You're giving an inch and saying it's not a problem. It's all covered by &quot;removes inhibitions&quot; and &quot;removes the barriers of social convention&quot; and &quot;secret desires&quot;.<br /> <br /> It's not mind-control...it's subtler and ambiguous, and therefore worse.</div> </div> </div> </div>Then you're playing with the wrong people. <br /> <br /> I'm not being coy or naive, here, because I have seen this argument before, as applied to the <b>turn someone on</b> move in <b>Monsterhearts</b> and in various other areas. Anything that remotely approaches mind control has this problem, though not every power gets the same outcry. It seems like it's just powers that make people more amenable to consensual sex, maybe? I don't know.<br /> <br /> All I can say is: I do not think that any reasonable read of Gift of Pan allows for rape. And, if you're playing at a game where sex is at all a possibility, then probably you should have a discussion ahead of time about what is acceptable (maybe use an X card?) so that if something comes up in play that's going to be problematic, there's something in place that allows you to put the brakes on. But I do not accept this argument that because some people might be assholes, I need to write every game system as though only assholes will use it. Instead, I charge the players thusly: Don't be assholes, and don't play with assholes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13-blackhatmatt","name":"blackhatmatt","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"464"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-05T13:40:13-07:00","id":1088466,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maggie C</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1086863-it-s-out?p=1088457#post1088457\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><u><i><b>My interpretation</b></i></u> is...</div> </div> </div> </div>And others exist. And will be seen at the table.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If it's going to be decided that violations of a person's comfort zone is okay, that is not a problem with the game, but with the group, and the vast majority of the community simply isn't like that. </div> </div> </div>Your experience is vastly different than mine. Mine happens to include harassment and unwelcome sexual advances at conventions, conventions covering up harassment and sexual assault, and protecting harassers, up to and including defending harassers when the entire roster of big name guests refuse to attend because the harasser is being protected, and game companies putting out briefs about how long-standing and well-documented harassment from a newly hired freelancer are bullshit. These are just the stuff that gets reported and goes viral. To say nothing about all the unreported stuff, or stuff that doesn't go viral.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11658-rabbit-pooka","name":"Rabbit Pooka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11658_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"65"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-05T13:43:27-07:00","id":1088471,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I'm not being coy or naive, here, because I have seen this argument before, as applied to the <b>turn someone on</b> move in <b>Monsterhearts</b> and in various other areas. Anything that remotely approaches mind control has this problem, though not every power gets the same outcry. It seems like it's just powers that make people more amenable to consensual sex, maybe? I don't know. </div> </div> </div>In this case, at least in my purely anecdotal experience to be sure, some of the reaction (my own anyway) is helped by that Gift of Pan has just had an awful, awful history to it in play. Yes, it's a great signpost for &quot;don't game with these people&quot; when that kind of disasterpiece occurs, but it's still been awful.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12141-markk","name":"MarkK","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-05T13:43:59-07:00","id":1088472,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MarkK</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1086863-it-s-out?p=1088464#post1088464\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For me it just boils down to that the &quot;helpless to indulge their secret desires&quot; part reads as contradicting the stuff before it about &quot;cannot force you to etc.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I would argue that &quot;secret desire&quot; requires the desire to be there in the first place. If the Storyteller says &quot;you are helpless to indulge your secret desire&quot; and your response is &quot;cool, but character's secret desire doesn't have anything to do with ol' hairylegs over there,&quot; then I don't see the problem.<br /> <br /> But <b>AGAIN</b>, this is all predicated on players being willfully disrespectful to each other and taking an uncharitable, childishly literal read of the game over what it's actually saying. Don't do that. If you're running a game and you find yourself saying &quot;no, your character totally fucks that guy because you failed a Willpower roll,&quot; you're being a terrible person and you sure as hell shouldn't need me to explain that.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13-blackhatmatt","name":"blackhatmatt","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"464"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-05T13:45:18-07:00","id":1088473,"title":"","content":"*insert unrelated brief amusement at the tides of the internet on being in accord with a person I was just otherwise arguing game stuff with a moment ago*<br /> <br /> I need some silver lining here.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12141,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12141-markk","user":"MarkK","date":". 05-05-2017, 05:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12141-markk","name":"MarkK","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-05T13:47:00-07:00","id":1088476,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>blackhatmatt</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1086863-it-s-out?p=1088472#post1088472\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I would argue that &quot;secret desire&quot; requires the desire to be there in the first place. If the Storyteller says &quot;you are helpless to indulge your secret desire&quot; and your response is &quot;cool, but character's secret desire doesn't have anything to do with ol' hairylegs over there,&quot; then I don't see the problem.<br /> <br /> But <b>AGAIN</b>, this is all predicated on players being willfully disrespectful to each other and taking an uncharitable, childishly literal read of the game over what it's actually saying. Don't do that. If you're running a game and you find yourself saying &quot;no, your character totally fucks that guy because you failed a Willpower roll,&quot; you're being a terrible person and you sure as hell shouldn't need me to explain that.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Whenever I run a game I just houserule the living crap out of Gift of Pan honestly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12141-markk","name":"MarkK","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-05T13:53:19-07:00","id":1088477,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rabbit Pooka</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1086863-it-s-out?p=1088466#post1088466\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Your experience is vastly different than mine. Mine happens to include harassment and unwelcome sexual advances at conventions, conventions covering up harassment and sexual assault, and protecting harassers, up to and including defending harassers when the entire roster of big name guests refuse to attend because the harasser is being protected, and game companies putting out briefs about how long-standing and well-documented harassment from a newly hired freelancer are bullshit. These are just the stuff that gets reported and goes viral. To say nothing about all the unreported stuff, or stuff that doesn't go viral.</div> </div> </div> </div>My experience is not vastly different than yours. I've been a gamer in possession of boobs and a vagina since the late 90s in male-dominated groups. There are problems and humongous ones, but it is not everyone and it is not even close to a &quot;vast majority&quot;. Thanks for assuming I've been a sheltered princess, tho.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Luka Carroll</b><br /> Onyx Path Freelancer &amp; Developer<br /> <i>Working On: </i>C20 Player's Guide, Lunars<br /> <i>Worked On: </i>V20 TMR, Demon STG, C20, Book of Freeholds, Conquering Heroes, Building A Legend, Dragon-Blooded, The Realm","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3785-luka-c","name":"Luka C","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3785_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"175"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-05T13:56:53-07:00","id":1088478,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MarkK</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1086863-it-s-out?p=1088476#post1088476\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Whenever I run a game I just houserule the living crap out of Gift of Pan honestly.</div> </div> </div> </div>In such a case, I suppose the most honest thing to do would be to houserule kiths such as satyrs, sidhes, and aonides entirely out of existence, rather than erasing or crippling their signature abilities. Because I don't think their powers could be reasonably done much less potentially abusable than the way Gift of Pan has been written in this edition. And the whole point of these archetypes is to be charming, seductive social gods that are very, very good at leading/influencing people into passion or obedience. Even so, if you ban or cripple social-god kiths you are simply kicking the can down the street, since there are other ways bad players could abuse social gods character concepts, either by using mind-influence Arts, high social stats, or both.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1949,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1949-irioth","user":"Irioth","date":". 05-05-2017, 05:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1949-irioth","name":"Irioth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"566"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-05T14:36:42-07:00","id":1088497,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Irioth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1086863-it-s-out?p=1088478#post1088478\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> In such a case, I suppose the most honest thing to do would be to houserule kiths such as satyrs, sidhes, and aonides entirely out of existence, rather than erasing or crippling their signature abilities. Because I don't think their powers could be reasonably done much less potentially abusable than the way Gift of Pan has been written in this edition. And the whole point of these archetypes is to be charming, seductive social gods that are very, very good at leading/influencing people into passion or obedience. Even so, if you ban or cripple social-god kiths you are simply kicking the can down the street, since there are other ways bad players could abuse social gods character concepts, either by using mind-influence Arts, high social stats, or both.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why? none of them can basically magic people into being drunk. Being charming and altering someone consciousness to make them act a certain way are different.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>When will you rage?","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1405-anteros","name":"Anteros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1405_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-05T14:50:50-07:00","id":1088501,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Anteros</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1086863-it-s-out?p=1088497#post1088497\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Why? none of them can basically magic people into being drunk. Being charming and altering someone consciousness to make them act a certain way are different.</div> </div> </div> </div>The way I read the c20 version of Gift of Pan, and the statements about it of the writer, it looks to me much less like magic people into being drunk/drugged, and much more like magic them into exposure to concentrated amounts of really, really good porn, wine, food, music, drugs, or whatever may represent a proper sensual temptation. As in, shoving the stuff under their nose. If there isn't any potential interest at all for the stuff lurking in their minds, they won't be affected. If there is any, an inner battle is going to take place between the passionate and temperate sides of their psyches, and the outcome means the subject falling into temptation and indulging or resisting and not being affected. Since the stuff is really, really good, the lusty/passionate/gluttonous side is usually going to have the advantage in the psychic battle unless the chaste/temperate side is overwhelmingly stronger. Which to me seems not really that different from the effects of a super-charming/seductive social god with 5+ in all social stats putting a move on the subject.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1949,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1949-irioth","user":"Irioth","date":". 05-05-2017, 06:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1949-irioth","name":"Irioth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"566"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-05T14:56:58-07:00","id":1088503,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rabbit Pooka</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1086863-it-s-out?p=1088432#post1088432\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It is really weird, isn't it. The book largely is presented as from the point of view of the commoners and that they're largely right, yet when it comes to the corresponding real-world movements they're presented as corrupted and co-opted by the bad guys. So the fictional commoners are right, but the real-world commoners are corrupted and co-opted. Such a bizarre position to take. Fighting for fictional equality is good, but fighting for real-world equality somehow serves the death of imagination and creativity...</div> </div> </div> </div>I just got finished driving for 6 hours and haven't had a chance read the rest the thread leading up to this yet, but I've gotta say, what? I have no idea where that's coming from.<br /> <br /> The Shadow Court is secretly infiltrated by the Black Court. It's so secret the vast majority of Shadow Courtiers have no idea.<br /> <br /> Occupy, Black Lives Matter, and all the other mortal protest movements have zero to do with the Black Court.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Charlie Cantrell</b><br /> Onyx Path Freelancer <hr />Changeling: The Dreaming 20th Anniversary Edition, Conquering Heroes, Book of Freeholds, Guide to the Night, C20 Players Guide","edited":{"userid":648,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/648-pookaknight","user":"PookaKnight","date":". 05-05-2017, 06:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/648-pookaknight","name":"PookaKnight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar648_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"690"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-05T15:30:55-07:00","id":1088519,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PookaKnight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1086863-it-s-out?p=1088503#post1088503\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I just got finished driving for 6 hours and haven't had a chance read the rest the thread leading up to this yet, but I've gotta say, what? I have no idea where that's coming from.<br /> <br /> The Shadow Court is secretly infiltrated by the Black Court. It's so secret the vast majority of Shadow Courtiers have no idea.<br /> <br /> Occupy, Black Lives Matter, and all the other mortal protest movements have zero to do with the Black Court.</div> </div> </div> </div>Happy to read it. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> It could perhaps be clarified, because when the text says that the Shadow Court is inspired by and inspire those movements in turn, then a few lines further it says that the Black Court fractures Kithain society from their place atop the Shadow Court, it brings to mind infortunate implications.<br /> Thanks for putting this concern to rest!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>When will you rage?","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1405-anteros","name":"Anteros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1405_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-05T15:39:15-07:00","id":1088526,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Irioth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1086863-it-s-out?p=1088501#post1088501\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The way I read the c20 version of Gift of Pan, and the statements about it of the writer, it looks to me much less like magic people into being drunk/drugged, and much more like magic them into exposure to concentrated amounts of really, really good porn, wine, food, music, drugs, or whatever may represent a proper sensual temptation. As in, shoving the stuff under their nose. If there isn't any potential interest at all for the stuff lurking in their minds, they won't be affected. If there are, an inner battle is going to take place between the passionate and temperate sides of their psyches, and the outcome means the subject falling into temptation and indulging or resisting and not being affected. Which to me seems not really that different from the effects of a super-charming/seductive social god with 5+ in all social stats putting a move on the subject.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know about that, the text seems to state that the Gift of Pan remove someone's inhibition into joining into whatever passionate activity the Satyr is indulging in at the moment, so that's clearly mind alteration since it's basically shutting down part of someone's normal reasoning ability.<br /> Being really pretty doesn't do that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>When will you rage?","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1405-anteros","name":"Anteros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1405_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-05T15:39:46-07:00","id":1088527,"title":"","content":"I intended that to mean the protest movements are good candidates for dreamers, and that the Shadow Court adopted their tactics.<br /> <br /> Edit to add: But yeah, while the rank and file Shadow Court members have legit grievances and good intentions, they're totally being used to further the Back Court's goals.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Charlie Cantrell</b><br /> Onyx Path Freelancer <hr />Changeling: The Dreaming 20th Anniversary Edition, Conquering Heroes, Book of Freeholds, Guide to the Night, C20 Players Guide","edited":{"userid":648,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/648-pookaknight","user":"PookaKnight","date":". 05-05-2017, 06:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/648-pookaknight","name":"PookaKnight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar648_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"690"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-05T15:47:11-07:00","id":1088529,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PookaKnight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1086863-it-s-out?p=1088527#post1088527\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I intended that to mean the protest movements are good candidates for dreamers, and that the Shadow Court adopted their tactics.</div> </div> </div> </div>I get it, but then perhaps the bit about inspiring the movements in turn is unnecessary? It's just 4 words, but they do leave place for some ambiguity.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>When will you rage?","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1405-anteros","name":"Anteros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1405_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-05T15:50:19-07:00","id":1088531,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Anteros</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1086863-it-s-out?p=1088526#post1088526\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't know about that, the text seems to state that the Gift of Pan remove someone's inhibition into joining into whatever passionate activity the Satyr is indulging in at the moment, so that's clearly mind alteration since it's basically shutting down part of someone's normal reasoning ability.<br /> Being really pretty doesn't do that.</div> </div> </div> </div>As human psychology goes, the inhibitions being shut down here usually have little to do with reasoning ability, and much more with shyness, insecurity, internalized social expectations of restraint, second-guessing, and the like. Prudishness and social anxiety =/= rationality.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1949,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1949-irioth","user":"Irioth","date":". 05-05-2017, 06:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1949-irioth","name":"Irioth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"566"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-05T15:54:07-07:00","id":1088533,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Irioth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1086863-it-s-out?p=1088531#post1088531\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> As human psychology goes, the inhibitions being shut down here quite often have very little to do with reasoning ability, and much more with shyness, insecurity, internalized social expectations of restraint, second-guessing, and the like. Prudishness =/= rationality.</div> </div> </div> </div>I probably expressed myself badly, sorry. I meant the Gift of Pan changes the way someone ususally think, not that it diminishes someone's cognitive functions.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>When will you rage?","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1405-anteros","name":"Anteros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1405_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-05T16:34:13-07:00","id":1088546,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maggie C</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1086863-it-s-out?p=1088477#post1088477\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thanks for assuming I've been a sheltered princess, tho.</div> </div> </div> </div>No such assumption was made. But thanks for proving it's pointless trying to discuss it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11658-rabbit-pooka","name":"Rabbit Pooka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11658_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"65"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-05T16:40:10-07:00","id":1088548,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PookaKnight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1086863-it-s-out?p=1088527#post1088527\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I intended that to mean the protest movements are good candidates for dreamers, and that the Shadow Court adopted their tactics.<br /> <br /> Edit to add: But yeah, while the rank and file Shadow Court members have legit grievances and good intentions, they're totally being used to further the Back Court's goals.</div> </div> </div> </div>And since the Shadow Court <b><i>inspires and is inspired by</i></b> Black Lives Matter, etc, the direct implication being the human movements are also co-opted by the Black Court. At least with the wording at present. If that's not the intent, great. But it should be revised. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11658-rabbit-pooka","name":"Rabbit Pooka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11658_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"65"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-05T16:55:21-07:00","id":1088555,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Anteros</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1086863-it-s-out?p=1088430#post1088430\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What bothhered me with thhe Fiefs of Brighht Paradse is that it was written with a European/North American perspective in mind. The whole &quot;pirate of the caribbean&quot; is mostly an European/American fantasy, not a Caribbean one. It's basically saying that Caribbean Changelings were shaped by the fantasies of Americans and Europeans, not those of their own people. Turning an entire region into a tourist stereotype is really creepy.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Strangely I had the opposite opinion when I read the Fiefs of Bright Paradise section. When I read that Puerto Rico was ruled by a Liam listening to plight of the commoners, declared independence from Concordia, and continues to champion for the needs of his commoners citizens I cheered out loud. I felt an incredible sense of pride, and excitement to run a game set in my native land.<br /> <br /> Now mind you I have a strong dual cultural identity as I have lived in both the states and on the island on and off my whole life. So it could be possible I have assimilated so much into US culture I am missing the imperialist tone entirely. I will make an effort to reread that section with your critique in mind. however for now I must say as a Puerto Rican, I am simply not seeing what you are talking about. :/","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>May you live in interesting times...</i><br /> <br /> Storyteller of <b><a href=\"https://sunforgedoath.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Sun Forged Oath</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1998-keichiokami","name":"Keichiokami","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1998_4.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"303"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-05T17:05:00-07:00","id":1088558,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1086863-it-s-out?p=1087056#post1087056\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So is it just me, or did C20's history change it so that there are now two Houses that took the Changeling Way during the Shattering, but still only one according to the character creation rules?</div> </div> </div> </div>Two houses remained and turned into the &quot;original&quot; Autumn sidhe, and in doing so, lost a lot of credebility with the Arcadian sidhe. Many viewed them as traitors, others as exiles, but at the end of the day, they're sidhe so allowances must be given. <br /> <br /> Not sure about chapter two's text, though. Mention it in the errata.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Krister M. Michl</b> <hr /><b>Freelance writer</b> <hr /><a href=\"http://whitewolf.wikia.com/wiki/Krister_M._Michl\" target=\"_blank\">Entry on White Wolf Wikipedia</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2494-rigistrade","name":"Rigistrade","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2494_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"37"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-05T17:18:35-07:00","id":1088561,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rabbit Pooka</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1086863-it-s-out?p=1088548#post1088548\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And since the Shadow Court <b><i>inspires and is inspired by</i></b> Black Lives Matter, etc, the direct implication being the human movements are also co-opted by the Black Court. At least with the wording at present. If that's not the intent, great. But it should be revised. </div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know, they're changelings. The gain glamour from inspiring people. It's a glamorous feedback loop - rebels inspiring rebels. I don't see how that immediately means human protest groups are puppets of the Black Court.<br /> <br /> (But that being said, if someone wants to run it that way in their game, I'm certainly not gonna stop them.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Charlie Cantrell</b><br /> Onyx Path Freelancer <hr />Changeling: The Dreaming 20th Anniversary Edition, Conquering Heroes, Book of Freeholds, Guide to the Night, C20 Players Guide","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/648-pookaknight","name":"PookaKnight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar648_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"690"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-05T18:58:14-07:00","id":1088587,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Keichiokami</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1086863-it-s-out?p=1088555#post1088555\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Strangely I had the opposite opinion when I read the Fiefs of Bright Paradise section. When I read that Puerto Rico was ruled by a Liam listening to plight of the commoners, declared independence from Concordia, and continues to champion for the needs of his commoners citizens I cheered out loud. I felt an incredible sense of pride, and excitement to run a game set in my native land.<br /> <br /> Now mind you I have a strong dual cultural identity as I have lived in both the states and on the island on and off my whole life. So it could be possible I have assimilated so much into US culture I am missing the imperialist tone entirely. I will make an effort to reread that section with your critique in mind. however for now I must say as a Puerto Rican, I am simply not seeing what you are talking about. :/</div> </div> </div> </div>I'll readily admit I know next to nothing about Puerto Rico in particular, but still, do you feel that the pirate realm happily ruled by a foreign rebel duke sounds like a Puerto Rican tale?<br /> It doesn't even mention a single Puerto Rican person, just a foreign Sidhe who was part of a colonizing force and whom the local commoners are glad to have leading them and taking care of them. It feels like a bad case of white saviorism, though to be fair, we don't know that the duke is actually white.<br /> <br /> I, for one, live on one of the smaller islands the book mention, and the idea of a &quot;pirate republic&quot; sounds completely alien, as does the notion of sailing away to raid distant lands. But that's what Changelings do aroud here appearently, even though piracy around here was a european business, and not a part of our culture and folklore.<br /> <br /> That's all I'm saying in fact. The Fiefs of Bright Paradise are a european fantasy situated in the Caribbean, while no actual Caribbean narratives are mentioned.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>When will you rage?","edited":{"userid":1405,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1405-anteros","user":"Anteros","date":".  Typos 05-06-2017, 09:40 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1405-anteros","name":"Anteros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1405_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-05T19:29:56-07:00","id":1088595,"title":"","content":"I'm the only one here, who thought that Gift of Pan was about street or stage performances? Like rock concerts and such. Noble art of meistersingers and all that.<br /> <br /> What happens afterwards between two adult consenting people is their business. Some drink, others dance, some talk, others bone. Gamble, play, swim, run, stand in the corner shyly, whatever ticks their tock.<br /> <br /> And I know it might sound incredibly naive from me, who's not very forthcoming with strangers on convents, generally tactless and socially abrasive, not a frequent party visitor nor a great proponent or user of violence, but I think it all comes to intent and articulation.<br /> When other player or GM seemingly violates a sacred trust between players, you just say &quot;Full-stop!&quot; and slowly, clearly ask them to explain what they, as a player and character what they want from your character, and why. Based on how stupid (or reasonable, dunno - miscommunications happen) their response is, you either agree with their suggested course of action, mediate to reconsider, leave immediately or get their faces acquainted with sufficient amount of force applied through pressure of your upper appendages until their.. uhm.. cognitive processes readjust to the new cultural paradigm - then one or both of you leave this gaming table for necessary self-medication purposes (ice cream.. or just ice).<br /> <br /> It's all a matter of right argumentation and supplemental reasoning tools. Use figures and metaphors. Zen koans and pain grips also help you to grasp others' attention - irrational at heart, but very hard to ignore.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>...","edited":{"userid":5211,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5211-firkraag","user":"Firkraag","date":". 05-06-2017, 11:12 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5211-firkraag","name":"Firkraag","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5211_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-05T19:36:28-07:00","id":1088597,"title":"","content":"That's a good point. The Gift of Pan will only ever lead someone to having sex (which is the issue at hand here) if they're already watching the Satyr using it having sex at the time, and it certainly seems like you could walk away if you wanted to without even having to roll. This seems like a very narrow set of circumstances that are unlikely to come up in a game unless you want it to.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10243-zenten","name":"zenten","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10243_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"488"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-05T19:52:52-07:00","id":1088602,"title":"","content":"I really like the Sevartal ability to turn unawakened Changelings. That's a good story hook directly integrated into the kith!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>When will you rage?","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1405-anteros","name":"Anteros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1405_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-06T03:22:09-07:00","id":1088676,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Anteros</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1086863-it-s-out?p=1088587#post1088587\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'll readily admit I know next to nothing about Puerto Rico in particular, but still, do you feel that the pirate realm happily ruled by a foreign rebel duke sounds like a Puerto Rican tale?<br /> It doesn't even mention a single Puerto Rican person, just a foreign Sidhe who was part of a colonizing force and whom the local commoners are glad to have leading them and taking care of them. t feels like a bad case of white saviorism, though to be fair, we don't know that the duke is actually white.<br /> <br /> I, for one, live on one of the smaller isalnds the book mention, and the idea of a &quot;pirate republic&quot; sounds completely alien, as does the notion of sailing away to raid distant lands. But that's what Changelings do aroud here appearently, even though piratery around here was a european business, and not a part of our culture and folklore.<br /> <br /> That's all I'm saying in fact. The Fiefs of Bright Paradise are a european fantasy situated in the Caribbean, while no actual Caribbean narratives are mentioned.<br /> <br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>That's all true. Piracy doesn't really reflect everyday life in the Caribbean. It is a Western fantasy. Swashbuckling absolutely would be fun, but probably more for an historical setting or Dreaming realm.<br /> <br /> The Caribbean has a really interesting blend of indigenous, European, African, Indian and Chinese culture, further distinguished linguistically by English, French, Dutch, Spanish and Portuguese, plus various creoles and patois from island to island. Pirates and colonist leaders don't quite capture the depth of the Caribbean dream.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-06T13:11:40-07:00","id":1088827,"title":"","content":"The information outside the US for Changeling tended to be somewhat odd. This has pretty much kept which was established about the setting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-06T15:24:46-07:00","id":1088877,"title":"","content":"Just for the sake of some positivity, I'm really, really happy with the Contract art the more I read over it. It's not just something it's always felt like the fae should be able to do, the art itself is really nice as a launch point for stories (fae making a pledge to do a thing, someone sensing an oath having been broken, even mortals finding themselves having accidentally sworn to do something as a result of casual contract). It both makes sense giving the setting and nicely brings to life some folklore aspects of faeries and oaths.<br /> <br /> I find a lot of the things I really like about the book have the feeling to them of &quot;man, I feel like this should have been here the whole time&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12141-markk","name":"MarkK","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-06T17:10:26-07:00","id":1088909,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Anteros</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1086863-it-s-out?p=1088533#post1088533\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I probably expressed myself badly, sorry. I meant the Gift of Pan changes the way someone ususally think, not that it diminishes someone's cognitive functions.</div> </div> </div> </div>So does being faced with an incredibly charming/seductive person putting the moves on you. I think the consent problem certain people have with this power is because they apply the IMO wrong analogy to it, of being made drunk/drugged. I prefer to apply the analogy of being presented with the opportunity to indulge in an extremely tempting sensual stimulus. .","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1949-irioth","name":"Irioth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"566"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-06T17:17:41-07:00","id":1088911,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Irioth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1086863-it-s-out?p=1088909#post1088909\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So does being faced with an incredibly charming/seductive person putting the moves on you. .</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm sorry, would you care to explain, because I don't think I get your meaning.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>When will you rage?","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1405-anteros","name":"Anteros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1405_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-06T17:37:24-07:00","id":1088919,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Irioth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1086863-it-s-out?p=1088909#post1088909\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So does being faced with an incredibly charming/seductive person putting the moves on you. I think the consent problem certain people have with this power is because they apply the IMO wrong analogy to it, of being made drunk/drugged. I prefer to apply the analogy of being presented with the opportunity to indulge in an extremely tempting sensual stimulus. .</div> </div> </div> </div>I just realized why it isn't as bad al alcohol. When someone's drunk they might do something they didn't want to do because they were confused, or easily manipulated, or whatnot. The gift of pan doesn't do that. At the very least it's something you wanted to do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10243-zenten","name":"zenten","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10243_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"488"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-06T17:44:37-07:00","id":1088922,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Anteros</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1086863-it-s-out?p=1088911#post1088911\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm sorry, would you care to explain, because I don't think I get your meaning.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean being offered the sudden opportunity to indulge in something sensual very appealing to you, such as an extremely charming and sexy person of your preferred gender trying to seduce or fascinate you, would change the way someone usually thinks/acts, since it would make the person less willing and able to deny the opportunity than usual, yet it wouldn't diminish the person's free will.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1949-irioth","name":"Irioth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"566"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-06T17:52:10-07:00","id":1088925,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Irioth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1086863-it-s-out?p=1088922#post1088922\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I mean being offered the sudden opportunity to indulge in something sensual very appealing to you, such as an extremely charming and sexy person of your preferred gender trying to seduce or fascinate you, would change the way someone usually thinks/acts, since it would make the person less willing and able to deny the opportunity than usual, yet it wouldn't diminish the person's free will.</div> </div> </div> </div>I... don't think so? From personal experience, being offered something very appealing doesn't make me forget why society wouldn't allow me to take it. Perhaps other people don't function that way, but I rather doubt it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>When will you rage?","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1405-anteros","name":"Anteros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1405_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-06T19:16:05-07:00","id":1088953,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MarkK</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1086863-it-s-out?p=1088877#post1088877\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just for the sake of some positivity, I'm really, really happy with the Contract art the more I read over it. It's not just something it's always felt like the fae should be able to do, the art itself is really nice as a launch point for stories (fae making a pledge to do a thing, someone sensing an oath having been broken, even mortals finding themselves having accidentally sworn to do something as a result of casual contract). It both makes sense giving the setting and nicely brings to life some folklore aspects of faeries and oaths.<br /> <br /> I find a lot of the things I really like about the book have the feeling to them of &quot;man, I feel like this should have been here the whole time&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>Awesome, that is exactly what we were going for with Contract. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/84-holden","name":"Holden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar84_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"673"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-07T00:05:48-07:00","id":1089026,"title":"","content":"I was very surprised by what I am seeing with what is added with Arts and Realms! I really like how a lot of the cool stuff from Lost, like themeing arts on the 4 seasons, as well as Contracts, are added! They are very welcome additions! Also brilliant making Dragon's Ire an Art!<br /> <br /> This totally makes up for not getting a Changeling Revised! This is in my top 3 of the 20th anniversary editions! Probably the most beautiful of them too!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-07T00:16:34-07:00","id":1089028,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Anteros</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1086863-it-s-out?p=1088587#post1088587\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'll readily admit I know next to nothing about Puerto Rico in particular, but still, do you feel that the pirate realm happily ruled by a foreign rebel duke sounds like a Puerto Rican tale?<br /> It doesn't even mention a single Puerto Rican person, just a foreign Sidhe who was part of a colonizing force and whom the local commoners are glad to have leading them and taking care of them. It feels like a bad case of white saviorism, though to be fair, we don't know that the duke is actually white.<br /> <br /> I, for one, live on one of the smaller islands the book mention, and the idea of a &quot;pirate republic&quot; sounds completely alien, as does the notion of sailing away to raid distant lands. But that's what Changelings do aroud here appearently, even though piracy around here was a european business, and not a part of our culture and folklore.<br /> <br /> That's all I'm saying in fact. The Fiefs of Bright Paradise are a european fantasy situated in the Caribbean, while no actual Caribbean narratives are mentioned.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> So here is the thing about Puerto Rico. Our culture and ethnicity is a mixture of Spanish European, Indigenous Tanio, and African. Puerto Rico, since the landing of Columbus, has been a colonized territory. The natives the Tanios were driven to extiniction through diesase, slavery, genocide, and breeding. Studies have shown that many Puerto Ricans carry the genes of Tanio peoples, but not &quot;pure&quot; Tanios exist anymore. <br /> <br /> Puerto Rican culture is a spanish culture, especially among the upper classes whom have a more direct lineage from Spanish colonists. <br /> The concept of a Pirate realm definately feels distinictly Puerto Rican to me. I grew up with stories of hidden pirate treasure, and brave sea battles as child from my family. Puerto Rican are lovers of history and stories from the pirate era, especially since Old San Juan still stands and we can point to solid remants from those times. <br /> The idea of a Foriegn rebel Duke happily ruling? Sounds like a Puerto Rican fantasy! Puerto Rico started as a colony of Spain, and after we gained our independence from Spain, we became a colony of the United States, which we still are to this day. The idea of a leader who decided to listen to the plight of common people and break the island free of colonial yoke and make it truly independant, is a dream that burns in the heart of many Puerto Ricans. It resonated with me very deeply. <br /> <br /> Because of my understanding of my home, I did not read Duke Danon as a &quot;forigen Duke&quot;, he is most like a wealthy young man from an influential puerto rican family from San Juan. Puerto Ricans span a vast spectrum of skin tone, ethnicites, political leanings, and socio-economic backgrounds. Yet at the end of the day we all aknowledge one another as Puerto Ricans. <br /> <br /> I felt that The Island of Riches was well written, and that is my Puerto Rican Changeling two-cents.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>May you live in interesting times...</i><br /> <br /> Storyteller of <b><a href=\"https://sunforgedoath.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Sun Forged Oath</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1998-keichiokami","name":"Keichiokami","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1998_4.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"303"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-07T04:03:47-07:00","id":1089067,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1086863-it-s-out?p=1089026#post1089026\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was very surprised by what I am seeing with what is added with Arts and Realms! I really like how a lot of the cool stuff from Lost, like themeing arts on the 4 seasons, as well as Contracts, are added! They are very welcome additions! Also brilliant making Dragon's Ire an Art!<br /> <br /> This totally makes up for not getting a Changeling Revised! This is in my top 3 of the 20th anniversary editions! Probably the most beautiful of them too!</div> </div> </div> </div>I LOVE Contracts. Oneiromancy, too, since these are things changelings should have been able to do from day one.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-07T04:07:54-07:00","id":1089068,"title":"","content":"Except for fifth dot, Oneiromancy is okay.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5211-firkraag","name":"Firkraag","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5211_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-07T04:36:23-07:00","id":1089071,"title":"","content":"I was curious to see if the runic magic system promised in the Book of Glamour was going to appear. It sounded like a new way of casting magic other than cantrips. But Naming is now a non-exclusive Art, as it should have been, so that Art can cover runic magician concepts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-07T04:48:36-07:00","id":1089076,"title":"","content":"Argh! Apologies, I didn't realise there was also a Gift of Pan debate on this thread - I went and derailed the errata thread instead. I won't repeat myself on that point, then. <br /> <br /> I will say that I quite like the new setup of the Shadow Court and the Black Court. I found the relationship between the two very clear and didn't think it was delegitimising the concerns of the Kithain involved (or the human protest movements that inspired their tactics). It reminded me of the recent reporting that Russia attempted to manipulate Sanders' supporters into voting for Trump by targeting them for anti-Clinton spam. A grassroots movement grounded in ethical concerns about justice and fairness manipulated (well, attempted anyway) by the clandestine and powerful. I think it's an interesting dynamic.<br /> <br /> I also don't think it's inherently inappropriate to reference Black Lives Matter, Occupy Wall Street or the Arab Spring. These are disparate political movements bound more by form than function, and - in keeping with C20's focus on Kithain society mirroring humanity's throughout history - it makes sense that mass grassroots protest would also characterise modern Kithain political conflict. I don't feel it's inappropriately laying claim to the seriousness of, for instance, the murder of young black men. It's more acknowledging that the Dream of protest and political activism is affected by the times - by the dominant imagery on our screens.<br /> <br /> I can see why it might be seen that way, but then, does the Week of Nightmares retcon - now associated with September 11 - trivialise those deaths? Is it in poor taste to tie the Accordance War to the Vietnam War, and all its attendant atrocities? If not, is it a matter of time? Is it too soon? That's a serious question. But it does raise another - when has it been long enough? How should a game set in a version of our contemporary world deal with current events? <br /> <br /> On the other hand I think the kith art is definitely questionable. I understand wanting to avoid tokenistic eshu but as others have noted, doing so by giving the only major kith associated with a non-Western myth white representation while portraying the violent and domestic fae as black is a very poor choice. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/187-beccatoria","name":"beccatoria","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar187_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"85"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-07T05:10:58-07:00","id":1089078,"title":"","content":"I think it's the part where the Shadow Court inspires those movements in turn. If the Shadow Court is merely inspired by them, that's another thing. I feel uncomfortable with fae inspiring 9/11 as much as Black Lives Matter. But being inspired by those things is fine.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-07T05:30:58-07:00","id":1089081,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Keichiokami</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1086863-it-s-out?p=1089028#post1089028\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> So here is the thing about Puerto Rico. Our culture and ethnicity is a mixture of Spanish European, Indigenous Tanio, and African. Puerto Rico, since the landing of Columbus, has been a colonized territory. The natives the Tanios were driven to extiniction through diesase, slavery, genocide, and breeding. Studies have shown that many Puerto Ricans carry the genes of Tanio peoples, but not &quot;pure&quot; Tanios exist anymore.<br /> <br /> Puerto Rican culture is a spanish culture, especially among the upper classes whom have a more direct lineage from Spanish colonists.<br /> The concept of a Pirate realm definately feels distinictly Puerto Rican to me. I grew up with stories of hidden pirate treasure, and brave sea battles as child from my family. Puerto Rican are lovers of history and stories from the pirate era, especially since Old San Juan still stands and we can point to solid remants from those times.<br /> The idea of a Foriegn rebel Duke happily ruling? Sounds like a Puerto Rican fantasy! Puerto Rico started as a colony of Spain, and after we gained our independence from Spain, we became a colony of the United States, which we still are to this day. The idea of a leader who decided to listen to the plight of common people and break the island free of colonial yoke and make it truly independant, is a dream that burns in the heart of many Puerto Ricans. It resonated with me very deeply.<br /> <br /> Because of my understanding of my home, I did not read Duke Danon as a &quot;forigen Duke&quot;, he is most like a wealthy young man from an influential puerto rican family from San Juan. Puerto Ricans span a vast spectrum of skin tone, ethnicites, political leanings, and socio-economic backgrounds. Yet at the end of the day we all aknowledge one another as Puerto Ricans.<br /> <br /> I felt that The Island of Riches was well written, and that is my Puerto Rican Changeling two-cents.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, I guess it does change things in that case. I totally read the mention of the duke ruling the Island of Riches as a colony of Concordia, then not having any intention of going back, meant he was originally from Concordia.<br /> Thanks for explaining!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>When will you rage?","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1405-anteros","name":"Anteros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1405_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-07T05:56:57-07:00","id":1089091,"title":"","content":"I can see that point. I guess the truth is that I just didn't read it that way around. Rereading it now it says the Kithain &quot;take inspiration [from], and inspire in turn&quot; which does suggest reciprocity. But I don't think the text intends to give the Kithain <i>credit</i> for BLM or to imply a direct inspirational relationship, as a fae musing on a mortal artist (which I agree would be icky). I believe the intention was to imply a broad synchronicity - art imitates life, but art also inspires the life it is imitating. The ways this works aren't always direct or clear. <br /> <br /> Saying that changelings secretly organised and founded BLM is gross. Saying that changelings participating in Shadow Court protests strengthens the Dream of such movements, which in turn, and indirectly, bolsters humans engaged in similar activities? I don't think that's gross? <br /> <br /> I am willing to be persuaded I've not thought about it coherently, though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/187-beccatoria","name":"beccatoria","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar187_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"85"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-07T06:29:13-07:00","id":1089098,"title":"","content":"Fae musing a mortal artist can't take credit for the mortals work though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10243-zenten","name":"zenten","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10243_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"488"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-07T06:46:10-07:00","id":1089108,"title":"","content":"zenten - I agree, I was trying to list taking credit and direct inspiration as separate things. <br /> <br /> To make it clearer, in case it wasn't, I think that if you implied, say, Maya Angelou's work is really only as good and beautiful and effective as it is because someone else was directly mentoring and inspiring her - refining and improving her raw material - that could be read as very paternalistic. That old &quot;this type of person couldn't possible have done this type of thing, so who was secretly responsible,&quot; stereotype. The one that attributes the accomplishments of women to the men in their lives, and the accomplishments of ethnic minorities to white people. <br /> <br /> I'm not saying that's how musing always works or should be read at all. I'm just saying that in certain circumstances it <i>could</i> come across that way and I think this would be one of them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/187-beccatoria","name":"beccatoria","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar187_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"85"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-07T06:52:32-07:00","id":1089117,"title":"","content":"Ah, OK. Yeah, I don't think that's ever a description of musing.<br /> Rhapsody on the other hand...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10243-zenten","name":"zenten","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10243_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"488"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-07T07:41:03-07:00","id":1089145,"title":"","content":"Love the book so far, especially the changes to Chimerical reality (that is not reality anymore if I got things right), and banality. That Voldemort Sluagh rustled my jimmies though!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11321-sinister-spider","name":"Sinister Spider","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"36"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-07T07:50:41-07:00","id":1089149,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Firkraag</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1086863-it-s-out?p=1087107#post1087107\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Reign_of_Terror\" target=\"_blank\">https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Reign_of_Terror</a><br /> <br /> All I want to say is that France had a long, rocky path to &quot;Libert\u00e9, \u00e9galit\u00e9, fraternit\u00e9!&quot;<br /> <br /> Revolutions, while at some points of history may be a necessary and inevitable conclusion of an interests conflict, are an indication, that formal leadership of the state and the leaders of public opinion have failed to communicate and achieve a consensus. Revolutions are built on blood and bones of people, who are often called heroes or villains based on the side they nominally supported when they died, not who they were in their lives. And France had seen their heroes turned rotten, violent and oppressive. And there are more peoples I can recall, that did as well.<br /> <br /> It depends on who you ask, how much that person knows about the issue, what she believes, how much she's benefiting from that, etc. etc. and even then - different factors might mean more or less to different people.<br /> <br /> Like, what would a Native North American think about War of Independence? It most likely depends.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, okay, certainly, everything depends on one's point of view... But, the French Revolution was the defining moment when the idea of republicanism became to mean also democracy, sovereignty for the people (which was not even true until then even in the US). It was the first moment in history when suddenly everything became possible. People were so elated that they thought they could declare universal peace (1790), the end of all wars, and the enthusiasm was such that many people from all over the Atlantic world came to Paris to celebrate how the French had overthrown the oldest monarchy in the world (or so they believe, since Europe was basically the world in the mindset of the time).<br /> <br /> That the so-called &quot;Terror&quot; was a terrible moment is not questioned (though I wonder why a &quot;terror&quot; of two years is always remembered but not the terror that monarchies have inflicted on their subjects for hundreds if not thousands of years), but historians agree that it was the moment that changed history and moved it from the pre-modern period to the modern or contemporary period. What does that mean? Well, it means that now people know that *they* can make and change history and they believed in a better future instead of a fantasy past (see Reinhard Kosseleck and his &quot;horizon of expectation&quot;).<br /> <br /> So labelling the Feench Revolution *as a whole* as a moment of despair is so wrong -- unless we consider that the Autumn People have won the way we look at history.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3747,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3747-mattboggan","user":"mattboggan","date":". 05-07-2017, 11:20 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3747-mattboggan","name":"mattboggan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"110"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-07T07:52:06-07:00","id":1089152,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mattboggan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1086773-c20-backer-pdf-errata-thread?p=1089130#post1089130\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Finally, a last question: you seem to have had the rights to use the kiths from the Monde des T\u00e9n\u00e8bres: France book, so why not use the duchies and counties and kingdoms from it too?</div> </div> </div> </div>Replying here so I don't clutter the errata thread.<br /> <br /> Even though I have a copy of the Fance book, I had to rely on terrible Google translations of the korred and morganed. Those plus the very little and super rusty French I remember from grade school let me muddle by to get the gist of what the two kiths are about and their birthrights and frailties.<br /> <br /> While I agree it would be best to have C20's France information sync up with the actual French book, I'm not sure if it would have feasible for that section given our resources.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Charlie Cantrell</b><br /> Onyx Path Freelancer <hr />Changeling: The Dreaming 20th Anniversary Edition, Conquering Heroes, Book of Freeholds, Guide to the Night, C20 Players Guide","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/648-pookaknight","name":"PookaKnight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar648_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"690"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-07T08:00:13-07:00","id":1089155,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PookaKnight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1086863-it-s-out?p=1087145#post1087145\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My apologies for the poor word choice. The mention of the French Revolution was intended to reference the situation leading up to it and the Reign of Terror, not the final outcome.</div> </div> </div> </div>PookaKnight,<br /> <br /> The &quot;Reign of Terror&quot; is an expression which was first coined by very conservative historians who wanted to discredit Robespierre by saying that he had &quot;reigned&quot; over France, which is very, very wrong. Robespierre, as many historians have now shown convincingly, was a rather centrist-like figure who eliminated opponents from the left (Hebertists) and right (Dantonists) because he felt that they both threatened the stability of the newly-established French Republic.<br /> <br /> Also, Robespierre never reigned over France. He was just one of the twelve members of the Comity of Public Safety who constantly fought among themselves, and who were accountable to the National Convention and its 700+ elected members (elected with universal suffrage for the first time in history!). France was surely a dictatorship at this moment (suppression of liberties) in order to fight almost all of Europe in order to survive, but it was a legislative dictatorship, not an executive one.<br /> <br /> The war in the Vend\u00e9e was most certainly a moment of Dark Glamour.<br /> <br /> Finally, the immediate outcome of the French Revolution was bleak: Napol\u00e9on Bonaparte took power with a coup on 9 November 1799 and then set up an executive dictatorship to prepare for his conquest of almost the whole of Europe. This conquest and the Napoleonic Wars were certainly also a moment of Dark Glamour, though it is very ambiguous: many peoples resisted against Napol\u00e9on in the name of the very ideals of the French Revolution that he claimed to bring to them. And for some (the Irish for instance), Napol\u00e9on was a liberator.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3747-mattboggan","name":"mattboggan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"110"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-07T08:18:49-07:00","id":1089163,"title":"","content":"How exactly historians have shown convincingly?..","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5211-firkraag","name":"Firkraag","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5211_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-07T08:20:19-07:00","id":1089166,"title":"","content":"In the US, the term French Revolution brings to mind both the dark times during the Revolution and the misery leading up to it. My word choice was poor, reflecting an American-centric shorthand. I should have thought about that when I wrote it and clarified things more.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Charlie Cantrell</b><br /> Onyx Path Freelancer <hr />Changeling: The Dreaming 20th Anniversary Edition, Conquering Heroes, Book of Freeholds, Guide to the Night, C20 Players Guide","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/648-pookaknight","name":"PookaKnight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar648_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"690"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-07T08:27:08-07:00","id":1089168,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Firkraag</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1086863-it-s-out?p=1089163#post1089163\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How exactly historians have shown convincingly?..</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, because they have done their jobs and have been honest about it: they have quoted their sources, they have been very open about why they interpret them the way they do, and, perhaps more importantly, they have reached now a pretty agreed-on consensus on who was Robespierre.<br /> <br /> The perception of Robespierre that has endured was forged immediately his fall and execution by those who were very close to him and who used him as a scapegoat in order to wash themselves of the crimes they had participated in. And since the enemies of the Revolution were using Robespierre as their scapegoat to sell to their own people their war against a democratic republican France, the two discourses coalesced and took hold on many, many minds. Then, it was used by very conservative historians (like Thomas Carlyle) who in turn were used by conservative novelists (Charles Dickens's Tale of Two Cities comes to mind) who then inspired many movies (the French Revolution was the historical topic most used in cinema after the Vietnam War until recently -- I'm thinking about Batman: The Dark Knight here, which is a direct evocation of the French Revolution, inspired by a Tale of Two Cities). In other words, when people think about it today, they think about a myth, not about what it really was, and what it did for France (but that's true for many other historic periods, and this is where historians have an important job to do).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3747,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3747-mattboggan","user":"mattboggan","date":". 05-07-2017, 11:34 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3747-mattboggan","name":"mattboggan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"110"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-07T08:27:56-07:00","id":1089170,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Holden</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1086863-it-s-out?p=1088953#post1088953\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Awesome, that is exactly what we were going for with Contract. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, I was sad at no Dreamcraft (which for me would have been a good place to put in something that shields/mitigates fae from the memory loss/personality warping associated with Dreaming travel to make it more viable), or Infusion, and I still think Dragon's Ire fell short of its mark (it's an art for fights that's not really great to use while in fights), but on the whole? The revamped arts and realms is one of the best sections of the book and well worth the entire price of admission alone. They're more evocative, thematic, and even what might seem like little touches made me really happy. The idea to move Will o Wisp to Soothsay was just fantastic. A seer focused character that can divine the location of things! That's seriously great.<br /> <br /> At this point in the big ol C20 discussion I think I'm mostly just looking/hoping for some insight from the creative team on the motivations behind the shift in the nobility/commoners dynamic.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12141-markk","name":"MarkK","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-07T08:31:27-07:00","id":1089171,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mattboggan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1086863-it-s-out?p=1089155#post1089155\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> PookaKnight,<br /> <br /> The &quot;Reign of Terror&quot; is an expression which was first coined by very conservative historians who wanted to discredit Robespierre by saying that he had &quot;reigned&quot; over France, which is very, very wrong. Robespierre, as many historians have now shown convincingly, was a rather centrist-like figure who eliminated opponents from the left (Hebertists) and right (Dantonists) because he felt that they both threatened the stability of the newly-established French Republic.<br /> <br /> Also, Robespierre never reigned over France. He was just one of the twelve members of the Comity of Public Safety who constantly fought among themselves, and who were accountable to the National Convention and its 700+ elected members (elected with universal suffrage for the first time in history!). France was surely a dictatorship at this moment (suppression of liberties) in order to fight almost all of Europe in order to survive, but it was a legislative dictatorship, not an executive one.<br /> <br /> The war in the Vend\u00e9e was most certainly a moment of Dark Glamour.<br /> <br /> Finally, the immediate outcome of the French Revolution was bleak: Napol\u00e9on Bonaparte took power with a coup on 9 November 1799 and then set up an executive dictatorship to prepare for his conquest of almost the whole of Europe. This conquest and the Napoleonic Wars were certainly also a moment of Dark Glamour, though it is very ambiguous: many peoples resisted against Napol\u00e9on in the name of the very ideals of the French Revolution that he claimed to bring to them. And for some (the Irish for instance), Napol\u00e9on was a liberator.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree that the revolution itself was a immense moment of hope, quickly dashed by the successions of dictatorships that followed. For a moment people thought they were going to be free, that they could attempt to make the ideals of the Lumi\u00e8res a reality. The tyranny of the nobility and the Church ended, slavery was abolished, women involved themselves in the struggle just as hard and prominently as men. And then those hopes were betrayed, dissenters were brutally eliminated, women lost whatever influence they'd gained during the revolution, many prominent female revolutionaries being executed, Napol\u00e9on became emperor and reinstated slavery. The Reign of Terror, which was just a prelude to more horror, was perhaps not quite what it's commonly thought to be but it still deserved its name.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>When will you rage?","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1405-anteros","name":"Anteros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1405_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-07T08:33:25-07:00","id":1089172,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PookaKnight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1086863-it-s-out?p=1089166#post1089166\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In the US, the term French Revolution brings to mind both the dark times during the Revolution and the misery leading up to it. My word choice was poor, reflecting an American-centric shorthand. I should have thought about that when I wrote it and clarified things more.</div> </div> </div> </div>You are right that indeed the French Revolution was a period filled with dark moments. Indeed, I do believe that redcaps, ogres and boggarts could enjoy the executions during the &quot;Terror&quot; (as did the redcap Shadow Court character in the said book). The war in the Vend\u00e9e was certainly something that sparked Dark Glamour.<br /> <br /> But the French Revolution was also a wonderful period of hope, of human progress when people really believed that now things could changed and be for the better, that now peoples were in charge, and so could bring forth a new future.<br /> <br /> But like anything in a game of fiction, the French Revolution is too big to be interpreted in a single way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3747-mattboggan","name":"mattboggan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"110"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-07T08:42:25-07:00","id":1089182,"title":"","content":"Ok so, according to the book, chimera can't interact with the mundane world under normal circumstances, right? Does that mean a changeling being chased by a chimera can simply enter some room and close the door behind them and stay completely safe?<br /> <br /> Also, do changelings caught by mundanes doing things like riding a chimerical flying carpet or something similar get kicked into the Dreaming like in 2nd edition?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11321-sinister-spider","name":"Sinister Spider","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"36"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-07T08:50:15-07:00","id":1089188,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MarkK</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1086863-it-s-out?p=1089170#post1089170\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">At this point in the big ol C20 discussion I think I'm mostly just looking/hoping for some insight from the creative team on the motivations behind the shift in the nobility/commoners dynamic.</div> </div> </div> </div>From my point of view, it's not the nobility as a whole who've holed up and cut the commoners off from Glamour. It's really just the 1% hoarding their resources. They have theirs and they're terrified of losing it. Instead of using their resources to foster opportunities for Kithain to generate Glamour, they're retreated into their freeholds. The force that used to keep them in check, High King David, has withdrawn and doesn't make them do their duty anymore. Commoners aren't the only ones feeling the pain - I'd imagine landless nobles and anyone without access to a major freehold or significant stores of dross are feeling the pain too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Charlie Cantrell</b><br /> Onyx Path Freelancer <hr />Changeling: The Dreaming 20th Anniversary Edition, Conquering Heroes, Book of Freeholds, Guide to the Night, C20 Players Guide","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/648-pookaknight","name":"PookaKnight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar648_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"690"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-07T08:56:29-07:00","id":1089193,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PookaKnight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1086863-it-s-out?p=1089188#post1089188\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> From my point of view, it's not the nobility as a whole who've holed up and cut the commoners off from Glamour. It's really just the 1% hoarding their resources. They have theirs and they're terrified of losing it. Instead of using their resources to foster opportunities for Kithain to generate Glamour, they're retreated into their freeholds. The force that used to keep them in check, High King David, has withdrawn and doesn't make them do their duty anymore. Commoners aren't the only ones feeling the pain - I'd imagine landless nobles and anyone without access to a major freehold or significant stores of dross are feeling the pain too.</div> </div> </div> </div>From the way the section talking about it reads, it mostly came off as the considerable majority of Concordia's nobility acting that way. I was just sort of surprised to see the desirous of overthrow set given a sense of objective rightness they previous lacked in a more murky state of affairs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12141-markk","name":"MarkK","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-07T08:57:18-07:00","id":1089194,"title":"","content":"Page 55 suggests chimera can now interact with the mortal world as long as no mortals are looking. I haven't read the later sections on Chimera or the Dreaming, but assuming there's no contradiction, I'd say the door trick you describe would work if there was a mortal present. However by deliberately relying on banality to suppress a creature of the Dreaming, the changeling would likely gain banality.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/187-beccatoria","name":"beccatoria","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar187_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"85"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-07T09:03:25-07:00","id":1089196,"title":"","content":"I hardly see how French Revolution would not bring Dark Glamour into the World. I mean, the event was caused by a massive economic crisis (due to the wars leaded by Louis XIV) and resulted in a Reign of Terror, wars, and an Empire some years later (with more wars).<br /> In reading Wikipedia, I even see something from Fran\u00e7ois Furet stating that a moderate crushing would have been enough.<br /> <br /> Of course, I can see some hope in it but it looks like romanticized vision of history to me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12595-nitenshi","name":"Nitenshi","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"110"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-07T09:06:47-07:00","id":1089197,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PookaKnight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1086863-it-s-out?p=1089188#post1089188\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> From my point of view, it's not the nobility as a whole who've holed up and cut the commoners off from Glamour. It's really just the 1% hoarding their resources. They have theirs and they're terrified of losing it. Instead of using their resources to foster opportunities for Kithain to generate Glamour, they're retreated into their freeholds. The force that used to keep them in check, High King David, has withdrawn and doesn't make them do their duty anymore. Commoners aren't the only ones feeling the pain - I'd imagine landless nobles and anyone without access to a major freehold or significant stores of dross are feeling the pain too.</div> </div> </div> </div>Seems like history repeating itself to me... Interesting...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12595-nitenshi","name":"Nitenshi","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"110"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-07T09:08:38-07:00","id":1089199,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>beccatoria</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1086863-it-s-out?p=1089194#post1089194\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Page 55 suggests chimera can now interact with the mortal world as long as no mortals are looking. I haven't read the later sections on Chimera or the Dreaming, but assuming there's no contradiction, I'd say the door trick you describe would work if there was a mortal present. However by deliberately relying on banality to suppress a creature of the Dreaming, the changeling would likely gain banality.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you! I was looking everywhere for more info but couldn't find it. It was the case for 2nd edition too but since so much has changed, I wasn't so sure it was still true.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11321-sinister-spider","name":"Sinister Spider","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"36"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-07T09:23:32-07:00","id":1089204,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MarkK</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1086863-it-s-out?p=1089193#post1089193\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> From the way the section talking about it reads, it mostly came off as the considerable majority of Concordia's nobility acting that way. I was just sort of surprised to see the desirous of overthrow set given a sense of objective rightness they previous lacked in a more murky state of affairs.</div> </div> </div> </div>In my opinion, part of it came from the split of the sidhe into Autumn and Arcadian.<br /> <br /> Commoners tend to take a better view of the Autumn sidhe, because those are the nobles that stuck around to live or die with their vassals. To many, <i>they've</i> earned their right to rule because they showed they were as loyal to their people as their people were to them. So it's not them. It's the other ones. It's these fairyland fuckers coming back, taking over, thinking they can just slide right back into leadership roles like they have divine mandate.<br /> <br /> It might have been fifty years, but in those fifty years, what was a thriving, functioning society got upheaved and shaken hard. A lot of commoners lost their freeholds to nobles, who brought certain Treasures back with them that allowed them to claim them. It isn't just a grudge or &quot;overthrow the system&quot;. It's legitimately &quot;we had a system, and it worked, and it was good. And then there's these assholes, acting like they're entitled to be bossing us around, and now resources are getting tighter and Lord Poncypants wants us to tighten our belts while he hoards the balefire he <i>stole </i>from us to himself? Fuck him, and the Glimmer he ponced in on.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Luka Carroll</b><br /> Onyx Path Freelancer &amp; Developer<br /> <i>Working On: </i>C20 Player's Guide, Lunars<br /> <i>Worked On: </i>V20 TMR, Demon STG, C20, Book of Freeholds, Conquering Heroes, Building A Legend, Dragon-Blooded, The Realm","edited":{"userid":3785,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3785-luka-c","user":"Luka C","date":". 05-07-2017, 12:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3785-luka-c","name":"Luka C","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3785_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"175"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-07T09:33:31-07:00","id":1089209,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nitenshi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1086863-it-s-out?p=1089196#post1089196\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I hardly see how French Revolution would not bring Dark Glamour into the World. I mean, the event was caused by a massive economic crisis (due to the wars leaded by Louis XIV) and resulted in a Reign of Terror, wars, and an Empire some years later (with more wars).<br /> In reading Wikipedia, I even see something from Fran\u00e7ois Furet stating that a moderate crushing would have been enough.<br /> <br /> Of course, I can see some hope in it but it looks like romanticized vision of history to me.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fran\u00e7ois Furet was a liberal historian who hated the French Revolution and equated it with totalitarianism. He wanted to prove that the Revolution had not meaning in contemporary France, as he, along other conservative historians, thought that the apex of political felicity was the liberal democracy and capitalism.<br /> <br /> No, the French Revolution was not caused by an economic crisis due to the wars of Louis XIV (which were about 120 years before!).<br /> <br /> There was economic crisis in 1788, but not worse than any one before. Revolutions are not only the products of economic crisis, though economic crisis help spark them, sure.<br /> <br /> Also, the Revolution would be dark because it sparked wars. What about the hundreds of wards sparked by monarchies before? That's not dark? Because they are waged for crowned heads, they're bright? And consider that the Revolution sparked war... because all other countries (ruled by monarchs) could not stand to have a country getting rid of the absolute power of its king; it threatened their own rule. (Granted, the leading faction at the moment in April 1792, the Girondins, led by Brissot welcomed the opportunity and declared war in order to cement the French people around their revolution... because Brissot wanted to emulate the example set forth by... the American war of Independence.)<br /> <br /> As I already wrote above: sure the Revolution saw some moments of Dark Glamour, but it was also (and mainly!) a moment of hope of levels never reached before. This is why it should be labelled as only a moment of Dark Glamour.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3747,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3747-mattboggan","user":"mattboggan","date":". 05-07-2017, 01:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3747-mattboggan","name":"mattboggan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"110"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-07T09:35:04-07:00","id":1089211,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PookaKnight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1086863-it-s-out?p=1089188#post1089188\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> From my point of view, it's not the nobility as a whole who've holed up and cut the commoners off from Glamour. It's really just the 1% hoarding their resources. They have theirs and they're terrified of losing it. Instead of using their resources to foster opportunities for Kithain to generate Glamour, they're retreated into their freeholds. The force that used to keep them in check, High King David, has withdrawn and doesn't make them do their duty anymore. Commoners aren't the only ones feeling the pain - I'd imagine landless nobles and anyone without access to a major freehold or significant stores of dross are feeling the pain too.</div> </div> </div> </div>Are all Sidhes still nobles? I don't recall seeing them having to take a tilte dot or getting one for free.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>When will you rage?","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1405-anteros","name":"Anteros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1405_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-07T09:37:47-07:00","id":1089215,"title":"","content":"For me it boils down to that when the Autumn Sidhe are mostly written as Liam or Scathach with handfuls of others (to the point that there was a fellow in the errata thread searching for references to other houses that had been noted as having chunks of them staying behind previously), I suppose it just sort of feels like it gives the sidhe (and whatever titled commoners have freeholds as related) a sense of objective wrongness/default villainy to them. And again, given previous involved internet arguments I've seen on that very thing well before C20, I'm sure there are people that groove on that just fine, but it was previously just that, something that could be argued. Here it's well more stark. Concordia's nobility are near en masse letting all the other kithain slowly die of lack of glamour basically (and there doesn't seem to be an &quot;any of them that are Autumn Sidhe aren't doing that&quot; exemption really). That's outright clear cut villain stuff. It caught me off guard as a change.<br /> <br /> I dunno, even the Ventrue aren't actively starving the other Camarilla clans of blood, y'know?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12141-markk","name":"MarkK","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-07T09:39:57-07:00","id":1089217,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Anteros</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1086863-it-s-out?p=1089211#post1089211\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Are all Sidhes still nobles? I don't recall seeing them having to take a tilte dot or getting one for free.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd say yes, they are. Sidhe without the Title Background, however, are on the outermost edges of noble society and, despite being nominally part that House, gain absolutely no benefits, magically or politically, from it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-07T09:54:49-07:00","id":1089224,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MarkK</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1086863-it-s-out?p=1089215#post1089215\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For me it boils down to that when the Autumn Sidhe are mostly written as Liam or Scathach with handfuls of others (to the point that there was a fellow in the errata thread searching for references to other houses that had been noted as having chunks of them staying behind previously), I suppose it just sort of feels like it gives the sidhe (and whatever titled commoners have freeholds as related) a sense of objective wrongness/default villainy to them. And again, given previous involved internet arguments I've seen on that very thing well before C20, I'm sure there are people that groove on that just fine, but it was previously just that, something that could be argued. Here it's well more stark. Concordia's nobility are near en masse letting all the other kithain slowly die of lack of glamour basically (and there doesn't seem to be an &quot;any of them that are Autumn Sidhe aren't doing that&quot; exemption really). That's outright clear cut villain stuff. It caught me off guard as a change.<br /> <br /> I dunno, even the Ventrue aren't actively starving the other Camarilla clans of blood, y'know?</div> </div> </div> </div>Would you say that C20 became an &quot;anti-Sidhe/anti-nobles&quot; edition, even more so than the former ones?<br /> <br /> Also, aside from the powers itself (which seems to be quite good from most of the posts), glamour was always a very harsh resource, which curbed Changeling's power level. Was it changed in C20?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","name":"PM\u00e1rk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-07T09:55:40-07:00","id":1089225,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Demigod Beast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1086863-it-s-out?p=1089217#post1089217\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'd say yes, they are. Sidhe without the Title Background, however, are on the outermost edges of noble society and, despite being nominally part that House, gain absolutely no benefits, magically or politically, from it.</div> </div> </div> </div>And what book says?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5211-firkraag","name":"Firkraag","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5211_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-07T09:56:30-07:00","id":1089228,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Firkraag</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1086863-it-s-out?p=1089225#post1089225\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's a direct quote?</div> </div> </div> </div>Nope! 'Tis my own interpretation, it 'tis.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-07T10:03:06-07:00","id":1089230,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PM\u00e1rk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1086863-it-s-out?p=1089224#post1089224\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Would you say that C20 became an &quot;anti-Sidhe/anti-nobles&quot; edition, even more so than the former ones?<br /> <br /> Also, aside from the powers itself (which seems to be quite good from most of the posts), glamour was always a very harsh resource, which curbed Changeling's power level. Was it changed in C20?</div> </div> </div> </div>On the one hand, rules wise, it's actually more defined and thus somewhat easier to harvest glamour via musing/rapture/that kind of thing (it requires a lot of successes at the attempt, but if managed, you can gain glamour within the span of a day for instance, which is very welcome and a good idea). On the other hand, the glamour pool is still very small, yes. On the other, other hand, setting wise it notes that glamour and freeholds are even more scarce (the latter for being even more tightly controlled amongst other things). So.. mixed bag?<br /> <br /> And yeah, at least from my own read, C20 does feel very &quot;the nobles are the setting villains here, barring the Fomorians/Thallain&quot;, which 2nd ed kept more in the air, and even Nobles: the Shining Host gave some nuance in 1e.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12141-markk","name":"MarkK","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-07T10:09:16-07:00","id":1089235,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MarkK</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1086863-it-s-out?p=1089230#post1089230\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> On the one hand, rules wise, it's actually more defined and thus somewhat easier to harvest glamour via musing/rapture/that kind of thing (it requires a lot of successes at the attempt, but if managed, you can gain glamour within the span of a day for instance, which is very welcome and a good idea). On the other hand, the glamour pool is still very small, yes. On the other, other hand, setting wise it notes that glamour and freeholds are even more scarce (the latter for being even more tightly controlled amongst other things). So.. mixed bag?.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's an optional rule further along that allows for a Storyteller to permit dross (solid Glamour equivalent to one point) to be used for cantrips, crafting and other kinds of Glamour expenditures. There are also optional rules for harvesting dross from creatures of the Dreaming. You can mitigate it as you need to.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Luka Carroll</b><br /> Onyx Path Freelancer &amp; Developer<br /> <i>Working On: </i>C20 Player's Guide, Lunars<br /> <i>Worked On: </i>V20 TMR, Demon STG, C20, Book of Freeholds, Conquering Heroes, Building A Legend, Dragon-Blooded, The Realm","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3785-luka-c","name":"Luka C","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3785_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"175"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-07T10:17:51-07:00","id":1089239,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PM\u00e1rk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1086863-it-s-out?p=1089224#post1089224\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Would you say that C20 became an &quot;anti-Sidhe/anti-nobles&quot; edition, even more so than the former ones?<br /> <br /> Also, aside from the powers itself (which seems to be quite good from most of the posts), glamour was always a very harsh resource, which curbed Changeling's power level. Was it changed in C20?</div> </div> </div> </div>I wouldn't say, C20 is anti-Sidhe. Rather, the Arcadian Sidhe's conquests after their return were a villainous act, as were their body-snatching ways, their usurpation of power and spoliation of commoners' possessions. As such they find themselves in the roles of tyrants and oppressors but it's not new. The novelty is the greater role of the Autumn Sidhe who provide a contrast and can claim a measure of moral superiority and legitimacy, plus the fact that the Shadow Court is not under the control of scheming and murderous Unseelie Sidhes anymore. Instead, the Sidhes are depicted as merely aloof and blind to the commoners' plight. As such, I'd see C20 as more pro-Sidhe than ever, or at least at giving better reasons why the Sidhe are not actually the villains of the game.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>When will you rage?","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1405-anteros","name":"Anteros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1405_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-07T10:21:45-07:00","id":1089242,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maggie C</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1086863-it-s-out?p=1089235#post1089235\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> There's an optional rule further along that allows for a Storyteller to permit dross (solid Glamour equivalent to one point) to be used for cantrips, crafting and other kinds of Glamour expenditures. There are also optional rules for harvesting dross from creatures of the Dreaming. You can mitigate it as you need to.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, whenever I run Changeling, even previously, I tended to dip pretty heavily into finding ways for my players to accumulate dross, yeah (the background from Enchanted, rewards for deeds performed, etc. etc.). Just noting as far as non optional stuff. I'm probably a broken record on this by now, but I do find online play doesn't truck as willingly in optional rules though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12141-markk","name":"MarkK","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-07T10:25:21-07:00","id":1089243,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Anteros</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1086863-it-s-out?p=1089239#post1089239\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I wouldn't say, C20 is anti-Sidhe. Rather, the Arcadian Sidhe's conquests after their return were a villainous act, as were their body-snatching ways, their usurpation of power and spoliation of commoners' possessions. As such they find themselves in the roles of tyrants and oppressors but it's not new. The novelty is the greater role of the Autumn Sidhe who provide a contrast and can claim a measure of moral superiority and legitimacy, plus the fact that the Shadow Court is not under the control of scheming and murderous Unseelie Sidhes anymore. Instead, the Sidhes are depicted as merely aloof and blind to the commoners' plight. As such, I'd see C20 as more pro-Sidhe than ever, or at least at giving better reasons why the Sidhe are not actually the villains of the game.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>The Autumn Sidhe boil down to two houses out of 13 and some bits and bobs of the other ones though, is the thing there. They're also not really noted as exempt from the nobility's general shift to closing off freeholds in the discussion of the state of Concordia. And said aloofness is glamour starving commoners to the point of undoing, so..","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12141-markk","name":"MarkK","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-07T10:31:47-07:00","id":1089245,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Anteros</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1086863-it-s-out?p=1089239#post1089239\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wouldn't say, C20 is anti-Sidhe. Rather, the Arcadian Sidhe's conquests after their return were a villainous act, as were their body-snatching ways, their usurpation of power and spoliation of commoners' possessions. As such they find themselves in the roles of tyrants and oppressors but it's not new. The novelty is the greater role of the Autumn Sidhe who provide a contrast and can claim a measure of moral superiority and legitimacy, plus the fact that the Shadow Court is not under the control of scheming and murderous Unseelie Sidhes anymore. Instead, the Sidhes are depicted as merely aloof and blind to the commoners' plight. As such, I'd see C20 as more pro-Sidhe than ever, or at least at giving better reasons why the Sidhe are not actually the villains of the game.</div> </div> </div> </div>It makes me really happy to read this. That's what I was going for in the Courts write-up \ud83d\ude0a","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Charlie Cantrell</b><br /> Onyx Path Freelancer <hr />Changeling: The Dreaming 20th Anniversary Edition, Conquering Heroes, Book of Freeholds, Guide to the Night, C20 Players Guide","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/648-pookaknight","name":"PookaKnight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar648_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"690"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-07T10:40:10-07:00","id":1089252,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Anteros</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1086863-it-s-out?p=1089239#post1089239\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Instead, the Sidhes are depicted as merely aloof and blind to the commoners' plight.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure, whether it makes it &quot;pro-Sidhe&quot; and Sidhe - not villains. In fact, there's a concept of criminal inaction, they fit into rather well.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\"><i><span style=\"font-family:georgia\">- &quot;I just happen to stand exactly right on your neck, coincidentally, but it's not like I'm at all touched by your suffering or anything. Live and let live others and all that. Have a nice day!&quot;</span></i></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>...","edited":{"userid":5211,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5211-firkraag","user":"Firkraag","date":". 05-07-2017, 01:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5211-firkraag","name":"Firkraag","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5211_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-07T10:41:22-07:00","id":1089255,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MarkK</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1086863-it-s-out?p=1089243#post1089243\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The Autumn Sidhe boil down to two houses out of 13 and some bits and bobs of the other ones though, is the thing there. They're also not really noted as exempt from the nobility's general shift to closing off freeholds in the discussion of the state of Concordia. And said aloofness is glamour starving commoners to the point of undoing, so..</div> </div> </div> </div>Both Liam and Scathach are said to hold few lands and are well seen by commoners, so they're less likely to be the guys hoarding the glamour. Liam is said to be the more widespread House, while Scathachs are often travellers, so coupled with the fact that they stayed during the Interregnum, they're the Sidhes the commoners are likely to be the most familiar with.<br /> As for the Arcadians, at least they're not fomenting war and assasinating people willy-nilly anymore. They're still bad, but more cowardly and selfish, instead of malicious mustache twirling villains.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>When will you rage?","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1405-anteros","name":"Anteros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1405_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-07T10:45:19-07:00","id":1089259,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Anteros</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1086863-it-s-out?p=1089255#post1089255\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Both Liam and Scathach are said to hold few lands and are well seen by commoners, so they're less likely to be the guys hoarding the glamour. Liam is said to be the more widespread House, while Scathachs are often travellers, so coupled with the fact that they stayed during the Interregnum, they're the Sidhes the commoners are likely to be the most familiar with.<br /> As for the Arcadians, at least they're not fomenting war and assasinating people willy-nilly anymore. They're still bad, but more cowardly and selfish, instead of malicious mustache twirling villains.</div> </div> </div> </div>That doesn't really.. disagree with anything I said? I guess I'm not thrilled with that the best that can be said of the kith and Concordian nobility in general is barring two houses out of a huge pile and some handfuls otherwise, they're a bunch of selfish cowards starving faerie society to death. That's malicious just fine.<br /> <br /> Previous editions of CtD had more variety of them than that, even in the Accordance War.<br /> <br /> If the best that can be noted is &quot;hey, at least they're not eating babies&quot;, then they're coming off pretty badly. Again, worse than the Ventrue with regards their own society. At least the Ventrue really do put in a serious effort to keeping the Masquerade up as far as living up to their own nonsense.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12141,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12141-markk","user":"MarkK","date":". 05-07-2017, 01:47 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12141-markk","name":"MarkK","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-07T11:09:01-07:00","id":1089267,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MarkK</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1086863-it-s-out?p=1089259#post1089259\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That doesn't really.. disagree with anything I said? I guess I'm not thrilled with that the best that can be said of the kith and Concordian nobility in general is barring two houses out of a huge pile and some handfuls otherwise, they're a bunch of selfish cowards starving faerie society to death. That's malicious just fine.<br /> <br /> Previous editions of CtD had more variety of them than that, even in the Accordance War.<br /> <br /> If the best that can be noted is &quot;hey, at least they're not eating babies&quot;, then they're coming off pretty badly. Again, worse than the Ventrue with regards their own society. At least the Ventrue really do put in a serious effort to keeping the Masquerade up as far as living up to their own nonsense.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not saying the Sidhe became nice, just that they're less awful as a whole. Not plotting mass death and assassinating people anymore don't make you a good guy, but it's definitely a step up when you actually used to do it. They're still hurting the commoners, but that's callousness more than malice. There's a chance of opening their eyes to the harm they're causing and having them stop, which didn't exist when they were often written as deliberately causing trouble.<br /> Also given the things written about house Balor in the previous edition, i'm not sure that the &quot;eating babies&quot; thing can't apply litterally <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />. The guys hung out with the Black Spiral Dancers!<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>When will you rage?","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1405-anteros","name":"Anteros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1405_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-07T11:32:49-07:00","id":1089275,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Anteros</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1086863-it-s-out?p=1089267#post1089267\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not saying the Sidhe became nice, just that they're less awful as a whole. Not plotting mass death and assassinating people anymore don't make you a good guy, but it's definitely a step up when you actually used to do it. They're still hurting the commoners, but that's callousness more than malice. There's a chance of opening their eyes to the harm they're causing and having them stop, which didn't exist when they were often written as deliberately causing trouble.<br /> <br /> Also given the things written about house Balor in the previous edition, i'm not sure that the &quot;eating babies&quot; thing can't apply litterally <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />. The guys hung out with the Black Spiral Dancers!</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't see that as a hair worth splitting. They're still directly causing a lot of death and suffering. And starving changelings of glamour. Whether they're doing it because they actively want those people dead or they're simply indifferent doesn't really matter. It's really weird to me that the C20 setting has taken this turn. First and second ed were clearly working-class / commoner focused settings, yet this one is more sympathetic to the 1% / nobles, almost painting them as victims instead of the villains they are. &quot;We know you're hurting and starving and drinking poisoned water, but the people withholding the resources you need to live are just misunderstood and don't understand their greed is causing other people to die, which makes it okay.&quot; Combine that with the troublesome depictions of race, non-American countries, and the squick factor of things like Gift of Pan...I'd almost say that getting C20 made was a Pyrrhic victory.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11658-rabbit-pooka","name":"Rabbit Pooka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11658_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"65"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-07T11:41:42-07:00","id":1089282,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Anteros</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1086863-it-s-out?p=1089267#post1089267\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm not saying the Sidhe became nice, just that they're less awful as a whole. Not plotting mass death and assassinating people anymore don't make you a good guy, but it's definitely a step up when you actually used to do it. They're still hurting the commoners, but that's callousness more than malice. There's a chance of opening their eyes to the harm they're causing and having them stop, which didn't exist when they were often written as deliberately causing trouble.<br /> Also given the things written about house Balor in the previous edition, i'm not sure that the &quot;eating babies&quot; thing can't apply litterally <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />. The guys hung out with the Black Spiral Dancers!<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Okay, I guess we disagree then that the sidhe were awful as a whole in previous editions. The whole thing with the iron knives was a house eiluned plot (one house out of a whole lot, as the reverse of the current dynamic), not done by the sidhe as a whole. I found the sidhe/nobility in previous editions to run the gamut as much as any other kith, and there was plenty of material in various books to back that up. If you thought they were all previously baby eating monsters, I can see how you would think that the current setup is actually more nuanced.<br /> <br /> Like I say, the people who viewed the sidhe/nobility as overall kinda garbage monsters anywho I don't imagine have much issue with the current metaplot.<br /> <br /> I suppose I dislike also on a player level &quot;bear in mind if you're making a sidhe, the majority of your kith are monstrous hoarder d-bags letting fae society die&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12141-markk","name":"MarkK","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-07T11:56:56-07:00","id":1089291,"title":"","content":"So, it seems from the differing opinions, that as a whole, the (arcadian) sidhe are depicted as more universally &quot;bad&quot;, but the two non-arcadian houses are more sympathetic. What I get is that the distinction is more acute between the two than it was.<br /> <br /> Indeed, from there it seems that the other authority-focused splats, like the Ventrue and the Hermetics, or the Silver Fangs are more nuanced, although, giving it a second thought, I'm not sure it's not somewhat fitting, since the fae and especially the Sidhe are creatures of extremes, so being a bit more black and white might be okay...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","name":"PM\u00e1rk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-07T11:57:23-07:00","id":1089292,"title":"","content":"Look at it from a commoner's point of view:<br /> <br /> The world basically ended bringing a never-ending age of crushing Banality, wherein every tiny bit of Glamour is a precious commodity---<i>and the sidhe ran like cowards and abandoned their faithful vassals to potential Undoing.</i><br /> <br /> Which is <i>completely accurate.</i> The sidhe saved themselves and let everybody else sink with the ship. Then, centuries later, they return out of nowhere and expect <i>the very people they abandoned to die</i> to just quietly ignore the past and submissively hand over the reigns of power.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-07T12:11:19-07:00","id":1089302,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Demigod Beast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1086863-it-s-out?p=1089292#post1089292\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Look at it from a commoner's point of view:<br /> <br /> The world basically ended bringing a never-ending age of crushing Banality, wherein every tiny bit of Glamour is a precious commodity---<i>and the sidhe ran like cowards and abandoned their faithful vassals to potential Undoing.</i><br /> <br /> Which is <i>completely accurate.</i> The sidhe saved themselves and let everybody else sink with the ship. Then, centuries later, they return out of nowhere and expect <i>the very people they abandoned to die</i> to just quietly ignore the past and submissively hand over the reigns of power.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, previously there were the Dougal who were more caught mid attempted fuller evac to the point that chunks of their own house were left behind and slowly murdered off as time passed, there were the Beaumayn who were imprisoned in Arcadia for a crime they didn't commit, House A Team styles, well before the Shattering, there were the Gwydion, who were bound to obey the High King commanding them to protect and withdraw with him as far as why they left, the Fiona themselves had a mixed response with people like Tamlin the Fiddler instead holding the gates open as long as his powers held out to do so and ended up in the Autumn world that way, the head of house Ailil stayed behind in an effort to keep some part of the Dreaming still anchored to the Autumn World..<br /> <br /> There was variation, is I guess what I'm saying there. The Accordance War itself was a thing of mutual atrocity, and in some cases, some of the returned nobility ruled well and managed to better things around them where they did.<br /> <br /> Here it's just.. but for two houses and some handfuls, the nobility are basically the setting villains in a way various other &quot;authority&quot; groups in other games don't manage to be.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12141-markk","name":"MarkK","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-07T12:11:47-07:00","id":1089303,"title":"","content":"I feel the sidhe come across as more or less the same. Broadly speaking, they're pretty jerky, a fact that is perhaps more apparent now there's more scarcity and noblesse oblige comes with more of a cost, but hardly at odds with the way they were portrayed before. It's easy to be chivalrous when there's no rush for the lifeboats. However, individual sidhe rulers are still described in varying ways in the setting and I don't think anyone would double-take if a game was set in an area with a more egalitarian sidhe noble in charge. If a player is making a sidhe character, the concern is the same as it always was - you're part of a noble social class and that may be a double-edged sword. In this case, however, there's actually more flexibility since a player can choose to play an autumn sidhe. In 2nd ed, the only way to do this was to be part of House Scathach. But an autumn sidhe is entirely decoupled from membership in any particular House (even if it's most common for Liam or Scathach sidhe), so, as I said, more flexibility. <br /> <br /> I'm also confused by Rabbit Pooka's belief that C20 is somehow painting the sidhe as victims. Is that something you feel C20 is doing, or were you just reacting to a previous post? Because I don't see that at all. The attitudes under discussion - while I would disagree that it represents a huge shift from the original game, or that it is presented as some monolithic, unyielding directive for every single sidhe ruler - seem pretty clearly presented as jerktastic to me?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/187-beccatoria","name":"beccatoria","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar187_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"85"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-07T12:20:39-07:00","id":1089309,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MarkK</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1086863-it-s-out?p=1089302#post1089302\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, previously there were the Dougal who were more caught mid attempted fuller evac to the point that chunks of their own house were left behind and slowly murdered off as time passed, there were the Beaumayn who were imprisoned in Arcadia for a crime they didn't commit, House A Team styles, well before the Shattering, there were the Gwydion, who were bound to obey the High King commanding them to protect and withdraw with him as far as why they left, the Fiona themselves had a mixed response with people like Tamlin the Fiddler instead holding the gates open as long as his powers held out to do so and ended up in the Autumn world that way, the head of house Ailil stayed behind in an effort to keep some part of the Dreaming still anchored to the Autumn World..<br /> <br /> There was variation, is I guess what I'm saying there. The Accordance War itself was a thing of mutual atrocity, and in some cases, some of the returned nobility ruled well and managed to better things around them where they did.<br /> <br /> Here it's just.. but for two houses and some handfuls, the nobility are basically the setting villains in a way various other &quot;authority&quot; groups in other games don't manage to be.</div> </div> </div> </div>A lot of this was detailed in further source books, though, and C20 has serious space constraints. It's painting a broad picture - assuming that means there is a sudden uniformity seems counterintuitive. The descriptions of the various rulers around Concordia, for instance, doesn't paint a picture of a bunch of evil villains. Variation still exists. <br /> <br /> I'm also not sure I'd really agree that the Accordance War was a thing of &quot;mutual atrocity&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/187-beccatoria","name":"beccatoria","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar187_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"85"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-07T12:25:35-07:00","id":1089311,"title":"","content":"The commoner side of things had gangs that went around looking for childlings to kill, it wasn't exactly a clean war for either grouping.<br /> <br /> And the picture it paints while broad, is also really stark, and reads like it speaks for the grouping as a whole. When it's that stark, it's not really difficult to read that as a statement.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12141-markk","name":"MarkK","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-07T12:39:52-07:00","id":1089315,"title":"","content":"Why people fret so much about Gift of Pan, but okay with Sovereign (or that Aphrodisia cantrip), which can be chosen to directly order others to do caster's bidding, <i>literally</i>?<br /> <br /> Or what about Appearancen, Charisma and Social Talents, which for some reason never ever manage to affect other player's characters, unless a player is actually charismatic and pretty?<br /> <br /> Or Troll's strength, that allows to physically overpower opponents in arguments?<br /> <br /> Nobody has control over your character's desires - secret or otherwise - unless you're willing to impart others with such power, as part of your social contract. If people does not understand that, you're unlikely to have great gaming experience with them, regardless of what's written in the rule book. <b>They don't have your interests (best or otherwise) in mind.</b>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>...","edited":{"userid":5211,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5211-firkraag","user":"Firkraag","date":". 05-07-2017, 08:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5211-firkraag","name":"Firkraag","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5211_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-07T12:55:06-07:00","id":1089325,"title":"","content":"The attempt to murder sidhe childlings is still in C20. Both sides may have had extremists who did terrible things, but one side was the aggressor and invader - the original setting didn't present the Accordance War as some kind of justified action on the part of the sidhe. Again, I'm just not seeing what you're seeing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/187-beccatoria","name":"beccatoria","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar187_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"85"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-07T13:04:04-07:00","id":1089330,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>beccatoria</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1086863-it-s-out?p=1089325#post1089325\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The attempt to murder sidhe childlings is still in C20. Both sides may have had extremists who did terrible things, but one side was the aggressor and invader - the original setting didn't present the Accordance War as some kind of justified action on the part of the sidhe. Again, I'm just not seeing what you're seeing.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not noting the Accordance War was justified, only that no one exactly came out of it clean, and that afterwards in portrayals, those that came to rule ran a wide gamut of doing good with that to doing horrifically with that. By contrast C20 is mostly a sweeping statement on the majority of the nobility as cowardly hoarders causing wide scale suffering across fae society as a collective entity, which makes anyone noted otherwise come off as handfuls of exceptions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12141-markk","name":"MarkK","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-07T13:14:42-07:00","id":1089336,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PM\u00e1rk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1086863-it-s-out?p=1089291#post1089291\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, it seems from the differing opinions, that as a whole, the (arcadian) sidhe are depicted as more universally &quot;bad&quot;, but the two non-arcadian houses are more sympathetic. What I get is that the distinction is more acute between the two than it was.<br /> <br /> Indeed, from there it seems that the other authority-focused splats, like the Ventrue and the Hermetics, or the Silver Fangs are more nuanced, although, giving it a second thought, I'm not sure it's not somewhat fitting, since the fae and especially the Sidhe are creatures of extremes, so being a bit more black and white might be okay...</div> </div> </div> </div>To be fair, the commoners aren't much better, whatever the Sidhe did to them (conquest, betrayal, theft of freeholds) they did to the Nunnehi first. Nobody has clean hands, here.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>When will you rage?","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1405-anteros","name":"Anteros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1405_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-07T13:41:27-07:00","id":1089349,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Anteros</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1086863-it-s-out?p=1089336#post1089336\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> To be fair, the commoners aren't much better, whatever the Sidhe did to them (conquest, betrayal, theft of freeholds) they did to the Nunnehi first. Nobody has clean hands, here.</div> </div> </div> </div>Chief Greyhawk <i>is</i> a Nunnehi, culturally. Sure, he's sidhe, but he 'went native' a long time ago. I find it hard to believe a sizeable chunk of commoners-turned-nobility in his kingdom <i>aren't</i> Nunnehi...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-07T13:51:24-07:00","id":1089357,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MarkK</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1086863-it-s-out?p=1089302#post1089302\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Here it's just.. but for two houses and some handfuls, the nobility are basically the setting villains in a way various other &amp;quot;authority&amp;quot; groups in other games don't manage to be.</div> </div> </div> </div>Don't forget, there's only about 1000 words or so per house in C20. The idea is to introduce them and give a broad overview that makes players want to play them, not replace entire sourcebooks.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Charlie Cantrell</b><br /> Onyx Path Freelancer <hr />Changeling: The Dreaming 20th Anniversary Edition, Conquering Heroes, Book of Freeholds, Guide to the Night, C20 Players Guide","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/648-pookaknight","name":"PookaKnight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar648_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"690"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-07T13:53:31-07:00","id":1089360,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Demigod Beast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1086863-it-s-out?p=1089349#post1089349\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Chief Greyhawk <i>is</i> a Nunnehi, culturally. Sure, he's sidhe, but he 'went native' a long time ago. I find it hard to believe a sizeable chunk of commoners-turned-nobility in his kingdom <i>aren't</i> Nunnehi...</div> </div> </div> </div>Unless Chief Greyhawk was adopted by a Nunnehi community, he has no claim to being &quot;a Nunnehi, culturally&quot;. The very expression &quot;going native&quot; though commonly used, is often perceived as terribly racist by native americans so seeing it in the book was disturbing. Native Americans fight hard to keep their culture from being erased and commodified by settlers, so the whole Chief Greyhawk thing leave a very bad taste as written.<br /> As for giving titles to Nunnehi, that wouldn't fit with the narrative of Greyhawk adopting the ways of the Nunnehi.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>When will you rage?","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1405-anteros","name":"Anteros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1405_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-07T13:56:55-07:00","id":1089363,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Anteros</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1086863-it-s-out?p=1089360#post1089360\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Unless Chief Greyhawk was adopted by a Nunnehi community, he has no claim to being &amp;quot;a Nunnehi, culturally&amp;quot;. The very expression &amp;quot;going native&amp;quot; though commonly used, is often perceived as terribly racist by native americans so seeing it in the book was disturbing. Native Americans fight hard to keep their culture from being erased and commodified by settlers, so the whole Chief Greyhawk thing leave a very bad taste as written.<br /> As for giving titles to Nunnehi, that wouldn't fit with the narrative of Greyhawk adopting the ways of the Nunnehi.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fair enough.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-07T14:44:04-07:00","id":1089391,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adambeyoncelowe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1086863-it-s-out?p=1089071#post1089071\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was curious to see if the runic magic system promised in the Book of Glamour was going to appear. It sounded like a new way of casting magic other than cantrips. But Naming is now a non-exclusive Art, as it should have been, so that Art can cover runic magician concepts.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm rather surprised that you remember one of my old sections for Book of Glamour, but with the Unleashing added to Changeling, that type of freeform magic would serve no purpose in C20.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Krister M. Michl</b> <hr /><b>Freelance writer</b> <hr /><a href=\"http://whitewolf.wikia.com/wiki/Krister_M._Michl\" target=\"_blank\">Entry on White Wolf Wikipedia</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2494-rigistrade","name":"Rigistrade","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2494_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"37"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-07T15:32:30-07:00","id":1089431,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Anteros</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1086863-it-s-out?p=1089360#post1089360\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Unless Chief Greyhawk was adopted by a Nunnehi community, he has no claim to being &quot;a Nunnehi, culturally&quot;. The very expression &quot;going native&quot; though commonly used, is often perceived as terribly racist by native americans so seeing it in the book was disturbing. Native Americans fight hard to keep their culture from being erased and commodified by settlers, so the whole Chief Greyhawk thing leave a very bad taste as written.<br /> As for giving titles to Nunnehi, that wouldn't fit with the narrative of Greyhawk adopting the ways of the Nunnehi.</div> </div> </div> </div>For all we know, he might've gone into Bedlam. Or established a legitimate embassy among the Nunnehi and <i>was </i>indeed adopted into the culture. Information presented in this chapter is intentionally incomplete. Unless (or until) the relevant sourcebook will be written, you or your Storyteller will have to decide, what happened in </span><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">the Duchy of Copper and how. </span></span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>...","edited":{"userid":5211,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5211-firkraag","user":"Firkraag","date":". 05-07-2017, 06:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5211-firkraag","name":"Firkraag","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5211_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-07T18:31:59-07:00","id":1089511,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PookaKnight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1086863-it-s-out?p=1089357#post1089357\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Don't forget, there's only about 1000 words or so per house in C20. The idea is to introduce them and give a broad overview that makes players want to play them, not replace entire sourcebooks.</div> </div> </div> </div>I get it, I do, but by the same token, it's the corebook that establishes the baseline. Which is what it is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12141-markk","name":"MarkK","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-07T18:51:56-07:00","id":1089519,"title":"","content":"Im glad im not the only one getting the strong Anti-sidhe vibe here, not sure how i feel about it tbh, that said I think the book is pretty lovely","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5533-cameraobscura83","name":"CameraObscura83","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5533_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"151"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-08T01:50:28-07:00","id":1089648,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Against all odds, true Dreamers, from all walks of life, and in every corner of the world, still thrive. They\u2019re not many, but they\u2019re out there, creating beautiful works of art, music, and literature, inventing new and unique technology that revolutionizes the way of life, or teaching generations of children through memorable and inspiring techniques. They infuse the world with Glamour, the stuff of dreams, that wards off the monotony of Banality and keeps the prophesied Long Winter at bay. Dreamers know, on some level, that they aren\u2019t alone, that the magical beings from stories and fables walk among them. They might deny it if someone asks \u2014 after all, who wants to be seen as someone crazy enough to believe in faeries \u2014 but they cross their fingers behind their backs when they do. They know, and the faeries see them.<br /> <br /> C20, chapter 1, opening section, pg. 31-32 </div> </div> </div>Kudos to those who wrote this. It is one of the very best text I have read on what Changeling is. It also focuses on humans. And that is great. I think my next Changeling story will have... humans, not even kinain, characters. I have been contemplating this for a long time now.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3747-mattboggan","name":"mattboggan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"110"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-08T02:15:44-07:00","id":1089660,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mattboggan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1086863-it-s-out?p=1089648#post1089648\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Kudos to those who wrote this. It is one of the very best text I have read on what Changeling is. It also focuses on humans. And that is great. I think my next Changeling story will have... humans, not even kinain, characters. I have been contemplating this for a long time now.</div> </div> </div> </div>That would be me. <br /> <br /> Thank you. I appreciate the kind words.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Krister M. Michl</b> <hr /><b>Freelance writer</b> <hr /><a href=\"http://whitewolf.wikia.com/wiki/Krister_M._Michl\" target=\"_blank\">Entry on White Wolf Wikipedia</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2494-rigistrade","name":"Rigistrade","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2494_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"37"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-08T02:58:04-07:00","id":1089671,"title":"","content":"Krister: congrats. This paragraph is really wonderful.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3747-mattboggan","name":"mattboggan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"110"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-08T12:44:40-07:00","id":1089900,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rigistrade</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1086863-it-s-out?p=1089391#post1089391\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm rather surprised that you remember one of my old sections for Book of Glamour, but with the Unleashing added to Changeling, that type of freeform magic would serve no purpose in C20.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm a superfan. :P I was just curious to see what the system was going to be like. I've played an illegal concept of a roving Scathach who used Vodu-inspired veves as a kind of rune. The only way I could play her was by begging the ST to let me take Naming (an Art which was unfairly reviled) or by having very specific uses of Soothsay. Now I can play her with the RAW.<br /> <br /> I love Unleashing. I'm still just curious how runic magic would have looked. I've saved all the errata, cut material and fan supplements I could find for Changeling. :P","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":5291,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","user":"adambeyoncelowe","date":". 05-08-2017, 03:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-09T02:46:45-07:00","id":1090192,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Daniel Knight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1089244-why-do-you-think-that-dragon-s-ire-is-bad-and-how-would-you-fix-it?p=1089597#post1089597\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Speaking of duration, can you apply multiple levels of Time to the same cantrip with no extra effect after the first one?</div> </div> </div> </div>It may be errata worthy question!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5211-firkraag","name":"Firkraag","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5211_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-09T04:03:03-07:00","id":1090211,"title":"","content":"I'm fine with this edition calling a spade a spade with regards to nobles. There's nothing preventing someone playing a sidhe knight who thinks they're the good guy still. <br /> <br /> Now, the books strong Seelie bias is still a bit irksome, but that's just a tone thing and easily ignored in play.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10243-zenten","name":"zenten","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10243_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"488"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-09T05:59:21-07:00","id":1090255,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>zenten</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1086863-it-s-out?p=1090211#post1090211\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now, the books strong Seelie bias is still a bit irksome, but that's just a tone thing and easily ignored in play.</div> </div> </div> </div>So one of the big goals for the Courts section was to make the Seelie a little less clear cut good guys and the Unseelie more sympathetic so they balance out. Rereading that part after spending some time away from it, I was really afraid I went too far.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Charlie Cantrell</b><br /> Onyx Path Freelancer <hr />Changeling: The Dreaming 20th Anniversary Edition, Conquering Heroes, Book of Freeholds, Guide to the Night, C20 Players Guide","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/648-pookaknight","name":"PookaKnight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar648_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"690"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-09T06:23:32-07:00","id":1090261,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PookaKnight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1086863-it-s-out?p=1090255#post1090255\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So one of the big goals for the Courts section was to make the Seelie a little less clear cut good guys and the Unseelie more sympathetic so they balance out. Rereading that part after spending some time away from it, I was really afraid I went too far.</div> </div> </div> </div>I thought the actual court part was great. It's the other parts of the book that talked about the courts that often had the seelie = good, unseelie = bad stuff.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10243-zenten","name":"zenten","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10243_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"488"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-09T06:46:03-07:00","id":1090270,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PookaKnight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1086863-it-s-out?p=1090255#post1090255\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So one of the big goals for the Courts section was to make the Seelie a little less clear cut good guys and the Unseelie more sympathetic so they balance out. Rereading that part after spending some time away from it, I was really afraid I went too far.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>zenten</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1086863-it-s-out?p=1090261#post1090261\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I thought the actual court part was great. It's the other parts of the book that talked about the courts that often had the seelie = good, unseelie = bad stuff.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I head that complaint as well.<br /> <br /> What was the point of your work if it's completely undermined and contradicted everywhere else in the book?<br /> <br /> And for the record: I'm all for the idea of Unseelie <i><b>not</b></i> being just a bunch of dicks.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>...","edited":{"userid":5211,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5211-firkraag","user":"Firkraag","date":". 05-09-2017, 02:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5211-firkraag","name":"Firkraag","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5211_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-09T07:11:51-07:00","id":1090283,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Firkraag</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1086863-it-s-out?p=1090270#post1090270\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What was the point of your work if it's completely undermined and contradicted everywhere else in the book?</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think it was?<br /> <br /> I mean, I included the Courts' criticisms of each other. How much of it is propaganda against the other Court and how much of it is accurate? The Seelie Court talks a big game about love and inclusivity, but maybe the Unseelie Court has a point about them being a bunch of overbearing, authoritarian tyrants. Likewise, the Unseelie Court claims to be all about self expression and individuality, but at the same time, that one Unseelie over there seems to do nothing but violently sow destruction for no reason other than the lulz.<br /> <br /> How much is the truth and how much is an unfair, nasty stereotype? Each gaming group gets to come up with their own answer to that question.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Charlie Cantrell</b><br /> Onyx Path Freelancer <hr />Changeling: The Dreaming 20th Anniversary Edition, Conquering Heroes, Book of Freeholds, Guide to the Night, C20 Players Guide","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/648-pookaknight","name":"PookaKnight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar648_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"690"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-09T07:25:46-07:00","id":1090288,"title":"","content":"In the end, most of the well-paid historians and tale tellers (in Concordia) are Seelie, so we both know who'll turn out to be a &quot;villain&quot; all along.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>...","edited":{"userid":5211,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5211-firkraag","user":"Firkraag","date":". 05-09-2017, 11:28 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5211-firkraag","name":"Firkraag","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5211_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-09T07:48:41-07:00","id":1090302,"title":"","content":"dammit this whole debate got this song stuck in my head... although that would suit the mood of the game<br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=lyEDDylzq_A\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=lyEDDylzq_A\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=lyEDDylzq_A\" target=\"_blank\"> https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=lyEDDylzq_A </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3729-darkfoxdev","name":"Darkfoxdev","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"161"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-09T11:48:39-07:00","id":1090398,"title":"","content":"For me, it was mostly the Legacies that seemed to enforce the the Unseelie = bad thing. Otherwise, it doesn't seem that bad.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>When will you rage?","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1405-anteros","name":"Anteros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1405_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-09T12:10:41-07:00","id":1090416,"title":"","content":"The Legacies were literally the first thing I wrote for C20. I was still iffy about going too far in changing things. I tried to massage the Unseelie ones into being more individualistic as opposed to flat out evil. I think I mostly succeeded compared to their second edition write-ups, but I can see how their descriptions might not have changed enough for some folks.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Charlie Cantrell</b><br /> Onyx Path Freelancer <hr />Changeling: The Dreaming 20th Anniversary Edition, Conquering Heroes, Book of Freeholds, Guide to the Night, C20 Players Guide","edited":{"userid":648,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/648-pookaknight","user":"PookaKnight","date":".  clarity 05-09-2017, 04:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/648-pookaknight","name":"PookaKnight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar648_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"690"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-09T12:22:24-07:00","id":1090425,"title":"","content":"If you were able to do bigger changes I could see switching the Court on some of them, but I don't have a real problem with them. Fiona and Varich for instance should trade Courts IMO. <br /> <br /> The Courts of some of the houses though, to me those need changing (but again, I get that they can't for a 20th Anniversary edition).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10243-zenten","name":"zenten","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10243_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"488"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-09T13:33:41-07:00","id":1090460,"title":"","content":"see i am not getting the unseelie = bad seelie = good vibe... maybe because im hyper fixated on the Sidhe issue","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5533-cameraobscura83","name":"CameraObscura83","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5533_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"151"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-09T22:04:44-07:00","id":1090593,"title":"","content":"Hey y'all, I couldn't find this: how many pages is C20?<br /> <br /> Search function didn't show anything.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3487-jetstream","name":"Jetstream","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3487_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"572"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-09T22:21:10-07:00","id":1090595,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PookaKnight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1086863-it-s-out?p=1090416#post1090416\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Legacies were literally the first thing I wrote for C20. I was still iffy about going too far in changing things. I tried to massage the Unseelie ones into being more individualistic as opposed to flat out evil. I think I mostly succeeded compared to their second edition write-ups, but I can see how their descriptions might not have changed enough for some folks.</div> </div> </div> </div>They're alright taken individually, but they all seem to promote rather anti-social behavior, so in the end they're all variations on the theme of being nasty.<br /> <br /> I tend to see Unseelie as valueing individuals and personal expression and Seelie valuing groups and social conventions. That way, they both have good and bad points, and we have more of an chaos vs order divide, than a evil vs good one. I'm not sure if the RAW support my view or if it is supposed to be only &quot;Unseelie are selfish and ruthless&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>When will you rage?","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1405-anteros","name":"Anteros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1405_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-10T01:40:17-07:00","id":1090639,"title":"","content":"I've finished to read yesterday. It's...gorgeous. I liked the art, the scripture..the only flaw it's too much short for me! Only 482 pages? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> And now some flaws about the background:<br /> <br /> -Where's Italy? There's a description about the Province of Venezia. And the rest?<br /> -The Galacian Confederation encompass Central and Oriental Europe. Perhaps you could include a few lines of the changeling kingdoms in Poland, Hungary, Bulgary and the Balkans as the Duchies not described in Concordia.<br /> -In Iberia There's the Kingdom of Le\u00f3n, not Leone. And it's a zone with atlantic weather, not mediterranean. The interior is more dry and cold.<br /> -Volcanoes in Denmark? Perhaps you want say Iceland.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2250-magus","name":"Magus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2250_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-10T05:54:11-07:00","id":1090690,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Anteros</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1086863-it-s-out?p=1090595#post1090595\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They're alright taken individually, but they all seem to promote rather anti-social behavior, so in the end they're all variations on the theme of being nasty.</div> </div> </div> </div>If it helps, don't forget that the secondary Legacy influences the primary one. My thought is that Legacies can go fairly extreme on their own, but the opposite court Legacy acts as a moderating influence. Normally breaking the Ban on a primary Legacy costs Willpower, but I added a rule that lets you break the Ban for free as long as you can justify it using your secondary Legacy.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Charlie Cantrell</b><br /> Onyx Path Freelancer <hr />Changeling: The Dreaming 20th Anniversary Edition, Conquering Heroes, Book of Freeholds, Guide to the Night, C20 Players Guide","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/648-pookaknight","name":"PookaKnight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar648_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"690"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-10T08:05:00-07:00","id":1090722,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=VwFnQVnO8pE&amp;t=628s\" target=\"_blank\">llustrating Fantasy in League of Legends</a> (<a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/channel/UC0JB7TSe49lg56u6qH8y_MQ\" target=\"_blank\">Game Design Conference</a>)<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5211-firkraag","name":"Firkraag","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5211_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-10T08:55:53-07:00","id":1090745,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PookaKnight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1086863-it-s-out?p=1090690#post1090690\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If it helps, don't forget that the secondary Legacy influences the primary one. My thought is that Legacies can go fairly extreme on their own, but the opposite court Legacy acts as a moderating influence. Normally breaking the Ban on a primary Legacy costs Willpower, but I added a rule that lets you break the Ban for free as long as you can justify it using your secondary Legacy.</div> </div> </div> </div>It does help! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>When will you rage?","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1405-anteros","name":"Anteros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1405_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-10T10:11:42-07:00","id":1090767,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CameraObscura83</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1086863-it-s-out?p=1090460#post1090460\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">see i am not getting the unseelie = bad seelie = good vibe... maybe because im hyper fixated on the Sidhe issue</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The sidhe issue is one that I'm focused on, as well. Maybe it is a sign of our current climate, but more than ever they seem like The Establishment. The commoners have a very nuanced relationship and place within the Dreaming, and I was hoping that the sidhe would get a more <i>explicit</i> nuanced presentation (because we can infer or extract interpretation based on our preferences all day long). For instance, I've always loved the idea that sidhe are dreams of power and grandeur made flesh; they are literally the fairy princes and princesses little boys and girls dream of growing up to be. The Dreaming created them to rule, so if they do not rule, they are betraying the Dreaming. I think it creates a more complex relationship with the Dreaming and with the commoners. Sure, I wholly accept that there are sidhe out there who are merely entitled brats with megalomania, but considering that the idea of nobility is literally written into the fabric of the Dreaming (supported by mechanics e.g. Fae 2, Sovereign and its relationship to Title) I would have loved more representation of Noblesse Oblige and the burden of leadership and the responsibilities of service to those you rule.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13420-gl1tterboots","name":"gl1tterboots","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"58"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-10T13:08:02-07:00","id":1090831,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>gl1tterboots</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1086863-it-s-out?p=1090767#post1090767\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> The sidhe issue is one that I'm focused on, as well. Maybe it is a sign of our current climate, but more than ever they seem like The Establishment. The commoners have a very nuanced relationship and place within the Dreaming, and I was hoping that the sidhe would get a more <i>explicit</i> nuanced presentation (because we can infer or extract interpretation based on our preferences all day long). For instance, I've always loved the idea that sidhe are dreams of power and grandeur made flesh; they are literally the fairy princes and princesses little boys and girls dream of growing up to be. The Dreaming created them to rule, so if they do not rule, they are betraying the Dreaming. I think it creates a more complex relationship with the Dreaming and with the commoners. Sure, I wholly accept that there are sidhe out there who are merely entitled brats with megalomania, but considering that the idea of nobility is literally written into the fabric of the Dreaming (supported by mechanics e.g. Fae 2, Sovereign and its relationship to Title) I would have loved more representation of Noblesse Oblige and the burden of leadership and the responsibilities of service to those you rule.</div> </div> </div> </div>I get the 'Arcadian sidhe are the 2%' stuff, and I've always agreed. They are bastards. But they were playable before--and you could ignore RL political analogues if you wanted to. <br /> <br /> Now it's just so lacking in subtlety that it doesn't leave room to manoeuvre. These things are better when they're more nuanced and less obvious.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":5291,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","user":"adambeyoncelowe","date":". 05-11-2017, 03:00 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-10T13:08:17-07:00","id":1090832,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>gl1tterboots</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1086863-it-s-out?p=1090767#post1090767\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> The sidhe issue is one that I'm focused on, as well. Maybe it is a sign of our current climate, but more than ever they seem like The Establishment. The commoners have a very nuanced relationship and place within the Dreaming, and I was hoping that the sidhe would get a more <i>explicit</i> nuanced presentation (because we can infer or extract interpretation based on our preferences all day long). For instance, I've always loved the idea that sidhe are dreams of power and grandeur made flesh; they are literally the fairy princes and princesses little boys and girls dream of growing up to be. The Dreaming created them to rule, so if they do not rule, they are betraying the Dreaming. I think it creates a more complex relationship with the Dreaming and with the commoners. Sure, I wholly accept that there are sidhe out there who are merely entitled brats with megalomania, but considering that the idea of nobility is literally written into the fabric of the Dreaming (supported by mechanics e.g. Fae 2, Sovereign and its relationship to Title) I would have loved more representation of Noblesse Oblige and the burden of leadership and the responsibilities of service to those you rule.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you for saying this a lot better than i ever could.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5533-cameraobscura83","name":"CameraObscura83","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5533_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"151"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-10T13:29:26-07:00","id":1090842,"title":"","content":"This is a good time to bring up something that's bothered me about authority and leadership in RPGs in general.<br /> <br /> Being in charge often means you have no choice but to give a certain order, or that you cannot give a certain order. Magic or not, you need to think about how you keep charge of your followers. &quot;Never give an order you know won't be obeyed&quot; and its corollaries just aren't portrayed well enough.<br /> <br /> If you're leading troops through hostile territory, get ambushed and your troops scatter and run, one of your best choices is to shout &quot;Take Cover!&quot; - sure, you had a complete breakdown of discipline, but after the encounter you can restore order among troops who jumped the gun a lot easier than among troops who outright betrayed you en masse.<br /> <br /> I'm not sure how you'd represent this in an RPG but I'm sure someone has an idea how to tie this in to fae nobility.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13395-daniel-knight","name":"Daniel Knight","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"96"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-10T15:19:08-07:00","id":1090891,"title":"","content":"I think that much could be done to mitigate the \u201cArcadian Sidhe are villains\u201d vibe if there's some tangible benefit that comes with rule by the Resurgent Houses. With that, you have a mixed bag where the downsides of a bunch of sanctimonious jerks forcing you to serve them is offset somewhat by the advantages that come with service to them; without that, you just have sanctimonious jerks forcing you to serve them.<br /> <br /> Tangible benefits for service to the Resurgent Houses also opens up the possibility of formerly Commoner motleys willingly signing up with the returned Nobility. That is, the Nobility isn't necessarily guys who forced their way into authority; many of them may have found themselves welcomed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-10T16:08:14-07:00","id":1090904,"title":"","content":"Honestly, I'd have been happy with little more than something like a note of &quot;a significant minority of Concordian nobles have chosen instead to keep their holds open, fighting to keep their peoples provided with glamour in a waning age. However this decision has exposed them to the censure of their peers. Their fellow nobility accuse them of everything from 'populist agitation of the commoners through the creation of unsustainable expectations', to outright treason against the will of the High King. Some retort that their accusers are merely driven by anger and shame at their own inaction, but the tensions remain. In the face of such ill will, the rulers of open holds have begun to formally reach out to each other for support, further factionalizing a political atmosphere already roiling with strife.&quot;<br /> <br /> Still keeps a big ol swath of the nobility being outright awful and still starving the rest of the kithain out, adds a conflict within the sidhe themselves, lets it feel a bit less &quot;your options for non villain sidhe are two houses out of 13, and some bits and pieces of the rest.&quot;<br /> <br /> And yeah, I'm sure I'm going to get &quot;then run your own campaign that way, no one's stopping you&quot;, but again, I also like to play Changeling, and I was hoping to keep buying whatever other books come out for C20, and the metaplot is leaving me cold on either.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12141-markk","name":"MarkK","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-10T16:15:43-07:00","id":1090909,"title":"","content":"That's what's in C20 though. You just phrased it a bit differently.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10243-zenten","name":"zenten","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10243_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"488"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-10T16:19:31-07:00","id":1090913,"title":"","content":"Where is that in C20?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12141-markk","name":"MarkK","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-10T16:24:08-07:00","id":1090916,"title":"","content":"One potential way to reframe Sidhe is...<br /> <br /> Make them distant, detached, somewhat cold even, blind to the plights of Commoners... Because they believe, they have the Mission (capital letter). They still live, socialize and make mistakes. But when Commoners raise the concerns close to them (personal, somewhat subjective, but always strong), Sidhe are not on the same page. Sifhe think with <b>ideologies</b> and <b>abstracts</b>. When Commoners act, Sidhe plan. When Commoners plan,<b> Sidhe strategize</b>. When Commoners blame Sidhe for indecisiveness, in fact, Sidhe prepares. Sidhe Knight roams the little towns and villages does that not because of a whim - he has some higher purpose (or thinks he has).<br /> <br /> Everything, that Sidhe do is grand scale, full of splendor and thoughtfulness. But to imbue their actions with that quality they have to gather intelligence, research, strategize, theorize, organize, engineer and most importantly knowingly sacrifice to achieve what they want.<br /> <br /> Of course, it doesn't mean, that all Commoners are shortsighted and limited or that no Sidhe can see what happens right under their noses. Or that Commoners can't think big ideas. What I'm talking about are frameworks. Sidhe, as a community used to think on the scale of decades and centuries. They rule and therefore they predict, research and try to predict what would happen...<br /> <br /> At the same time, Commoners spent generations trying to simply <b>survive </b>- mindset, that's ingrained in their collective consciousness and they excel at it. And they're much better at it than average Sidhe. They have knowledge, the Lore of the Prodigals, common sense, skills and Familiarity. <b>They adapt</b>.<br /> <br /> Obviously, that kind of difference will cause all kinds of conflicts.<br /> <br /> Now, Noble Houses have returned in <b>the </b><b>seventies</b> and you can expect, that almost half a century later <i>something</i> had changed. Commoners adapted. Adapted to Resurgence, Sidhe, Sovereign, Dreaming, Gallain, Thallain and Denizens. While whatever Arcadian Sidhe plan is grandiose, they surely need a shake-up. Some of the Sidhe, of course, embraced new ideas and changes, integrated Commoners into the highest echelons of power, taken them into a fold, invited Gallain even. Some places are war-torn and have rebellion after rebellion. Others are under the stable conservative feudal rule, for good or ill. But Holdings places have a mix of all I mentioned above and more.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>...","edited":{"userid":5211,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5211-firkraag","user":"Firkraag","date":". 05-10-2017, 07:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5211-firkraag","name":"Firkraag","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5211_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-10T16:32:01-07:00","id":1090918,"title":"","content":"That would just make them people starving the rest of kithain society to undoing not out of stated insecurity and cowardice, but some higher ideology they think no one else is cool enough to grasp. You can't really get around &quot;are keeping their holds closed and thereby glamour starving the other kiths&quot; as a thing. It's a huge evil thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12141-markk","name":"MarkK","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-10T16:51:59-07:00","id":1090924,"title":"","content":"I'd personally prefer to ignore &quot;Sidhe have shut in Freeholds, gatekeeping the Glamour&quot; because it goes against Escheat. If Escheat is ignored and Freeholds are closed - Sidhe aren't ruling anybody... it's Anarchy.<br /> <br /> Banality feedback from such large-scale violation of the Kithain Laws would make all Sidhe Oathbreakers and erase their Kith from the face of the Dreaming as if they never existed. <b><img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></b><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5211-firkraag","name":"Firkraag","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5211_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-10T17:26:03-07:00","id":1090935,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Firkraag</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1086863-it-s-out?p=1090924#post1090924\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd personally prefer to ignore &quot;Sidhe have shut in Freeholds, gatekeeping the Glamour&quot; because it goes against Escheat. If Escheat is ignored and Freeholds are closed - Sidhe aren't ruling anybody... it's Anarchy.<br /> <br /> Banality feedback from such large-scale violation of the Kithain Laws would make all Sidhe Oathbreakers and erase their Kith from the face of the Dreaming as if they never existed. <b><img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></b></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> If violating the Escheat makes you an Oathbreaker, then every damn kithain is an oathbreaker. Every Ravager, every person who's ever fought against another Kithain, every Kith who took land from Nunehei, every Kithain who does anything but go out and hunt down captured Changelings etc.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>changeling 2e</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Right of Safe Haven \u2014 All places of the Dreaming<br /> are sacred. Kithain cannot allow faerie places to be endangered.<br /> All those who seek refuge in such places must be admitted.<br /> Freeholds must be kept free of both Banality and worldly<br /> violence.<br /> Reality: Competition for the few freeholds that have<br /> survived the Shattering makes this tenet a hard one to<br /> enforce. Rival claims to the same spot of dream-infused<br /> ground often lead to warfare that encroaches upon its boundaries,<br /> although in most cases combat on the actual grounds<br /> of a freehold is restricted to chimeric battle. Some lords bar<br /> their freeholds to outsider changelings for fear that unwanted<br /> visitors may waste the Glamour inherent in their<br /> holdings. Despite the demands of hospitality and courtesy<br /> upon the domains of nobles, commoner freeholds are often<br /> more inclined than their noble counterparts to admit changelings<br /> seeking refuge.</div> </div> </div> </div>Now compare C20<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>c20</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Right of Safe Haven \u2014 All places of the Dreaming<br /> are sacred. Changelings cannot allow those places to be<br /> endangered. All who seek refuge in those places must be<br /> admitted, Freeholds must be kept free of worldly violence<br /> and Banality.<br /> Reality: Competition for the few freeholds to survive the<br /> Shattering make this law difficult to administer. Rival claims<br /> for the same area may lead to warfare, though combat on the<br /> actual grounds is usually restricted to chimeric combat. Some<br /> lords also bar their freeholds to outsiders, fearing they will<br /> drain the Glamour of the location needed to keep a supply for<br /> its residents. Despite the traditions of hospitality and courtesy,<br /> many nobles find that the demands are too heavy on them. Commoner<br /> freeholds are more likely to admit those seeking refuge.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> I don't have a copy of 1e readily available but I'm damned sure &quot;I can kick your ass out of my freehold&quot; has been something people have done since 1e and the dreaming hasn't marked them as Oathbreakers.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-10T17:32:20-07:00","id":1090938,"title":"","content":"I'm enjoying reading the discussion on the sidhe. Feels like it needs its own post by now, haha.<br /> <br /> As Firkraag mentioned, I struggle justifying a lot of the sidhe-as-written because these actions so vehemently violate the Escheat (abandoning the commoners and locking them out of Arcadia, willingly dooming them to die, for starters). I feel like I've had to do a lot of reworking of history and culture to make the sidhe palatable or even bare-bones sympathetic as characters and I wish that wasn't the case. It feels like, as written, they are textbook psychopaths. Which, sure, works on an individual level (I adore the psychopathic sidhe villain), but no other Kithain gets painted with a broad stroke like that. I don't think that's justifiable, considering Kithain are dreams of wonder and inspiration; the unsympathetic authoritarian nightmare works great for Thallain. Again, I'm not looking for sidhe to be made the heroes or even the <i>good guys</i>, but I feel like the game and the setting and the story dynamic is served better when they are explicitly complex characters. I want reasons to root for Arcadian Sidhe just like I root for Autumn Sidhe just like I root for Commoner Boggans.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13420-gl1tterboots","name":"gl1tterboots","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"58"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-10T17:33:57-07:00","id":1090940,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Firkraag</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1086863-it-s-out?p=1090924#post1090924\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd personally prefer to ignore &quot;Sidhe have shut in Freeholds, gatekeeping the Glamour&quot; because it goes against Escheat. If Escheat is ignored and Freeholds are closed - Sidhe aren't ruling anybody... it's Anarchy.<br /> <br /> Banality feedback from such large-scale violation of the Kithain Laws would make all Sidhe Oathbreakers and erase their Kith from the face of the Dreaming as if they never existed. <b><img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></b></div> </div> </div> </div>I'd prefer to at least heavily modify it for a bunch of already stated reasons, but, I mean, it's the plot now.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12141-markk","name":"MarkK","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-10T17:55:53-07:00","id":1090944,"title":"","content":"Something that always struck me about the shattering, If there were no other kithsin Arcadia BUT the sidhe, who exactly were they ruling... makes me wonder the full story of the shattering tbh.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5533-cameraobscura83","name":"CameraObscura83","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5533_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"151"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-10T18:15:23-07:00","id":1090950,"title":"","content":"I'm fine with the Shattering honestly. It was in the main mass panicked flight and the sidhe (and some small handfuls of commoners) managed to get the best of it before the gates snapped shut. Various books added nuance onto the circumstances of who left and didn't and why and how and such and aftermaths. Even the Resurgence/Accordance War itself was almost something of a cycle as far as commoners having themselves done up the nunnehi like that, as someone else mentioned, nor a war cleanly fought on either end. And there were places in the world where it went with less agony. Some domains managed to be ruled justly afterwards, that kind of thing. There was room to maneuver in all that, as someone else put it.<br /> <br /> You can't really get around starving the other kithain to undoing though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12141-markk","name":"MarkK","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-10T18:46:51-07:00","id":1090953,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MarkK</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1086863-it-s-out?p=1090940#post1090940\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">but, I mean, it's the plot now.</div> </div> </div> </div>Didn't stop me before. Won't stop me now.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5211-firkraag","name":"Firkraag","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5211_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-10T18:47:56-07:00","id":1090954,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Firkraag</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1086863-it-s-out?p=1090953#post1090953\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Didn't stop me before. Won't stop me now.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well hey, if you're ever inclined to run CtD online then..","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12141-markk","name":"MarkK","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-10T18:48:59-07:00","id":1090955,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MarkK</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1086863-it-s-out?p=1090950#post1090950\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm fine with the Shattering honestly. It was in the main mass panicked flight and the sidhe (and some small handfuls of commoners) managed to get the best of it before the gates snapped shut. Various books added nuance onto the circumstances of who left and didn't and why and how and such and aftermaths. Even the Resurgence/Accordance War itself was almost something of a cycle as far as commoners having themselves done up the nunnehi like that, as someone else mentioned, nor a war cleanly fought on either end. And there were places in the world where it went with less agony. Some domains managed to be ruled justly afterwards, that kind of thing. There was room to maneuver in all that, as someone else put it.<br /> <br /> You can't really get around starving the other kithain to undoing though.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was always wondering, what Arcadian Commoners would look like. =)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5211-firkraag","name":"Firkraag","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5211_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-10T18:52:57-07:00","id":1090956,"title":"","content":"Oh, and one more thing. If Sidhe are sitting behind the Freehold's raths they're missing out the most of Dreamers, which Commoners should be really good at finding and supporting. Even with the relative rarity of those, I doubt, that there are more Freeholds, than Dreamers. They require some work, but when did Commoner eschew from some honest work?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5211-firkraag","name":"Firkraag","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5211_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-10T18:57:42-07:00","id":1090957,"title":"","content":"I need to reread the relevant sections to remember what made the final cut and what didn't, but I don't think it's the majority of sidhe who've closed their doors. The impression I have (which, admittedly, could be based on a hodgepodge of different drafts) is that it's the noble equivalent of the 1% - the ones even other nobles look at and say, &quot;that's a lot of glamour.&quot; In practice it's only a handful of individuals, but because they have such a stranglehold on Glamour, their influence is far greater than their numbers.<br /> <br /> Of those individuals, it might not be entirely due to malice. Some of them may just be so insulated from the situation on the ground, they can't even conceive of the hardship the average Kithain faces. Others just spend so much time immersed in their Glamour, they've slide toward Bedlam. They too may not realize the harm they're causing. Only a few of these nobles may be acting out of selfishness or fear.<br /> <br /> Most nobles may genuinely want to help, but due to the Evanescence, they just don't have the resources anymore to effect change on a large scale.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Charlie Cantrell</b><br /> Onyx Path Freelancer <hr />Changeling: The Dreaming 20th Anniversary Edition, Conquering Heroes, Book of Freeholds, Guide to the Night, C20 Players Guide","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/648-pookaknight","name":"PookaKnight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar648_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"690"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-10T18:59:49-07:00","id":1090958,"title":"","content":"I'll double check but im fairly sure it says the majority of Sidhe held freeholds do this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5533-cameraobscura83","name":"CameraObscura83","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5533_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"151"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-10T19:07:41-07:00","id":1090961,"title":"","content":"Both the rise of Shadow Court as an open protest movement and the Starvation of Dreams and Present Day sections phrase it as pretty sweeping across the landed nobility. To the point that even commoners that are titled members of houses are shutting the rest of the fae out/ignoring their concerns. Talking about their fear and insecurity, throwing Sovereign around on commoners, on the extremes this is driving fae society to, phrases like the political and social landscape changing &quot;more than any noble is willing to admit&quot;. Presents it as a massive rift between faerie commoners and nobles, in those words. The presentation is that this is being done so at large across fae society that it is driving the kithain to desperation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12141,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12141-markk","user":"MarkK","date":". 05-10-2017, 10:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12141-markk","name":"MarkK","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-10T22:16:31-07:00","id":1090981,"title":"","content":"When I read over the Duchies of Concordia (asside from not having anything for Maryland) I noticed minor trend of sidhe nobles having treaties with the Nunnhei, even the Nunnehei section points out how the ones who are best off sided with the Sidhe in the accordance war. I'm definately starting to see a &quot;fuck you I got mine&quot; vibe from all levels of Changeling society, the only reason the commoners care is they don't have theirs but they'd easily shit on someone smaller.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-11T06:36:59-07:00","id":1091097,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CameraObscura83</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1086863-it-s-out?p=1090958#post1090958\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'll double check but im fairly sure it says the majority of Sidhe held freeholds do this.</div> </div> </div> </div>Freeholders and landed nobles have to offer at least one night of shelter and sustenance to those who request it. This is enforced by the Dreaming.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Luka Carroll</b><br /> Onyx Path Freelancer &amp; Developer<br /> <i>Working On: </i>C20 Player's Guide, Lunars<br /> <i>Worked On: </i>V20 TMR, Demon STG, C20, Book of Freeholds, Conquering Heroes, Building A Legend, Dragon-Blooded, The Realm","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3785-luka-c","name":"Luka C","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3785_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"175"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-11T07:20:36-07:00","id":1091116,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maggie C</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1086863-it-s-out?p=1091097#post1091097\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Freeholders and landed nobles have to offer at least one night of shelter and sustenance to those who request it. This is enforced by the Dreaming.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> But if I recall that same section of the book says that they are <i>not</i> required to allow those people access to the Balefire. Just food and shelter.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13420-gl1tterboots","name":"gl1tterboots","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"58"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-11T07:58:39-07:00","id":1091128,"title":"","content":"They aren't, no. But they can't just kick someone out wihout shelter or deny them sanctuary for a night, because the Dreaming enforces the Right of Hospitality. Denying someone shelter or passage into the Dreaming usually results in the freehold's benefits being withdrawn from its holder. Even Glamour-hoarding sidhe know better than to fuck with that law.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Luka Carroll</b><br /> Onyx Path Freelancer &amp; Developer<br /> <i>Working On: </i>C20 Player's Guide, Lunars<br /> <i>Worked On: </i>V20 TMR, Demon STG, C20, Book of Freeholds, Conquering Heroes, Building A Legend, Dragon-Blooded, The Realm","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3785-luka-c","name":"Luka C","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3785_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"175"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-11T09:23:59-07:00","id":1091159,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MarkK</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1086863-it-s-out?p=1090913#post1090913\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Where is that in C20?</div> </div> </div> </div>In a lot of the write-ups of the Houses and the descriptions of the various kingdoms, duchies, etc. Yes, the overall broad-view of the modern era is that it's characterised by sidhe increasingly closing their freeholds to all because of increasing banality. It broadly describes them as jackasses, the same way their behaviour was described during the Accordance War in all editions of this game. However, I think the nuance you're looking for is present when you look at explanations and descriptions of specific areas, individuals and institutions - again, as it always was. If I recall a lot of the canon you cited in support of a view that allowed for more sympathetic Arcadian sidhe was supplemental material based on the histories of individual Houses. That's material that in many cases is still there in C20.<br /> <br /> Examples:<br /> <br /> House Danaan is described as having an Eshu as High Lord, and as being welcoming to commoners.<br /> <br /> House Daireann are stated to retain their strict laws of hospitality and their freeholds (or cauldronhouses) are required to remain open to all as a result.<br /> <br /> House Eiluned foresaw the Shattering and left members behind to watch over their holdings. Most of those members became Unseelie as a result, but this is a clear indication that there is a contingent of Autumn fae in House Eiluned, and that they did not wholesale abandon their charges.<br /> <br /> House Fiona's entry notes that <i>many</i> of that house chose to stay behind during the Interregnum (including Fiona herself) and that they have one of the highest levels of ennobled commoners.<br /> <br /> House Gwydion is still stated to have retreated on the orders of their High Lord and against the will of many individuals.<br /> <br /> House Leanhaun's High Lord is said to be beloved by commoners because of her populist views in the Parliament of Dreams.<br /> <br /> House Liam, of course, is now one of the houses that stayed behind en masse but in addition, it's entry notes that while they do not have as many holdings as other houses, sidhe swearing fealty to House Liam are among the most widespread - a commoner-friendly house is apparently one of the ones you are most likely to meet.<br /> <br /> And, of course, House Scathach are still noted to have stayed in the Autumn world and are still said to welcome all kiths into their ranks.<br /> <br /> To move on to specific geographical areas, again there are a lot of places where there are either sidhe supported by commoners, welcoming commoners to their freeholds, ennobled commoner rulers successfully working within the existing sidhe-centric framework, or just sidhe generally not being jackasses to everyone around them:<br /> <br /> New York is ruled by a troll from House Fiona.<br /> <br /> Connecticut is currently ruled by an elected council.<br /> <br /> South Carolina is ruled by a Liam sidhe who challenges noble expectations and ideas about parentage, being born to Vietnamese immigrants, and he does not challenge the autonomous rule of the nearby Gullah fae.<br /> <br /> Some of the rulers of Appalachia are described as being in active alliance with the local Nunnehi.<br /> <br /> Duke Cormac of Virginia is described as having modern political ideals, which presumably implies a pro-commoner bent.<br /> <br /> It's said that Queen Mary-Elizabeth of the Kingdom of Grass welcomes all changelings to her freehold as long as they forswear violence and abide by the rules of Concordia.<br /> <br /> Chief Greyhawk (problematic descriptive language aside), ruler of the Kingdom of the Burning Sun seems to be moving away from traditional sidhe rule entirely in favour of following traditions aligned with the Nunnehi.<br /> <br /> In Phoenix, Arizona there's a Baron who has built a think-tank of many different houses and kiths in an attempt to study emerging patterns in Kithain politics and work out the best way forward for the fae in the face of the oncoming winter - a more flexible and inclusive response than shutting down the freehold to all and hoarding glamour.<br /> <br /> Tallahassee is ruled by a clurichaun duchess.<br /> <br /> Queen Aeron of Pacifica is expressly stated to keep her halls open to all fae, commoner, noble or gallain, regardless of court affiliation.<br /> <br /> And that's just Concordia. But it certainly seems to me like the book supports the notion that there is space for a variety of opinion and action on the part of the sidhe, and presumably also the commoners living under their rule.<br /> <br /> Anyway, that's why I agree with zenten. C20 presents the sidhe as - broadly - closing ranks, panicking and shutting down their freeholds in the 2010s due to the fear that winter is imminent. However, there is obviously a wide range of individual behaviour and the house and geographical descriptions bear this out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":187,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/187-beccatoria","user":"beccatoria","date":". 05-11-2017, 12:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/187-beccatoria","name":"beccatoria","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar187_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"85"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-11T11:27:27-07:00","id":1091205,"title":"","content":"The problem of that is that a lot of the stuff you're talking about with the houses are things the houses are noted as having done in the past, whereas the broad spectrum stuff is noted as what is by contrast happening now. Beyond that, the law of hospitality doesn't require the Daireann to have to offer glamour. Beyond /that/, it actually notes in the section on the Escheat that the Escheat is not actually backed by glamour, only by custom, and that the Dreaming only occasionally intervenes subtly against those who ignore it.<br /> <br /> As for describing the sidhe as jackasses, I will just say there's a difference between the Accordance War as a thing that happened in 1969, 20+ years before even the previous settings happened and which the vast majority of current wilder and childling sidhe would not have been able to take part in, and, say, currently actively starving the rest of kithain society to desperation and risk of undoing out of blind cowardice as the default state of affairs.<br /> <br /> Again, it mostly seems like people who felt the sidhe were previously awful anyway are cool with this, which, sure, understandable. For those of such views, I imagine the book seems even overly generous to have the options it does. I'm not one of such people, and it certainly previously felt like there was some space to not be one of them that doesn't exist at this point. As I otherwise noted, the whole &quot;the kith as a whole is starving the other kiths to death&quot;, is huge, and huge and evil to the point that it doesn't really feel like a thing to get past.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> To move on to specific geographical areas, again there are a lot of places where there are either sidhe supported by commoners, welcoming commoners to their freeholds, ennobled commoner rulers successfully working within the existing sidhe-centric framework, or just sidhe generally not being jackasses to everyone around them: </div> </div> </div>A bunch of the places you're talking about don't preclude the broad spectrum state of the setting being a thing there, it just notes who rules and some general details about them, again reducing then anyone bucking the overall trend to basically a handful. It doesn't help that some of your examples, Chief Greyhawk for instance is a hugely problematic character anyway, and Dice is.. I will just say a controversial figure. If Chief Greyhawk besides only achieves some measure of virtue by his breaking entirely with his own house and society, it makes the statement on the kith as a whole that it makes. It's also not great that House Danaan part achieves virtue by fact of not having the sidhe in a leadership position, itself something of a comment there. They're also barely directly active outside of the Dreaming. (Which? When the Dreaming is so personality distorting to fae, doesn't seem like it should even work, but that's something else entirely unrelated).<br /> <br /> Things like a place being ruled by an elected council, who themselves are noted as mostly getting by on that High King David has not actually commented on what they did one way or another yet, are again mostly &quot;this place overthrew the sidhe that ruled them, installed commoners in their place and are now better off.&quot; How that doesn't make the kith continue to look bad/verging on incompetent, I'm not sure.<br /> <br /> edit: I mean, even houses with titled commoners, the setting details took care of that one by throwing in that the titled commoner members of houses are also taking part in the overall current treatment of commoners by the nobility, disappointing the expectations for help from their fellow commoner kithain. Nothing really takes things especially far from &quot;but for 2 houses out of 13 and some handfuls, the nobility are godawful.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12141,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12141-markk","user":"MarkK","date":". 05-11-2017, 03:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12141-markk","name":"MarkK","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-11T11:32:18-07:00","id":1091208,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maggie C</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1086863-it-s-out?p=1091128#post1091128\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They aren't, no. But they can't just kick someone out wihout shelter or deny them sanctuary for a night, because the Dreaming enforces the Right of Hospitality. Denying someone shelter or passage into the Dreaming usually results in the freehold's benefits being withdrawn from its holder. Even Glamour-hoarding sidhe know better than to fuck with that law.</div> </div> </div> </div>It notes on page 64 that the Escheat specifically isn't backed by glamour like oaths are, and that the Dreaming only occasionally subtly steps in to put consequences onto people. Even under Safe haven it goes on a bit about the law falling down in practice and commoner freeholds being more likely to let fae in.<br /> <br /> If the idea was that no one can deny the right of hospitality without those consequences, the text there reads as contradicting that intent.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12141-markk","name":"MarkK","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-11T12:49:13-07:00","id":1091232,"title":"","content":"But I'm not trying to buck the overall trend, I'm trying to show the setting makes it clear the trend is not monolithic; that it's perfectly in keeping with C20 to state that there's a measurable minority who disapprove - that's what the conversation was referring to when you made the &quot;where does it say that?&quot; comment. <br /> <br /> I raised the historical references because you referenced Tamlin the Fiddler keeping the gates open and Gwydion's forcibly ordered retreat as 2e examples of nuance. In that vein I felt Fiona staying and Gwydion's orders remaining canon were absolutely relevant, as is establishing that Autumn sidhe exist in houses other than Liam or Scathach, since that's a whole new type of sidhe with different relationships to commoners, and a different set of ethical concerns. <br /> <br /> The references to the courts of Aeron and Mary-Elizabeth are absolutely current. I'm not particularly interested in defending Chief Greyhawk as I agree that both the concept and the language around it are problematic, but he exists in the setting and whether he proves the terribleness of House Gwydion or not, it's a third kingdom that's ruled by someone who, presumably, won't be shutting doors in the face of anyone without noble blood. <br /> <br /> Similarly, you may have excellent reasons for being leery of Dice and House Danaan, but the setting provides a noble house led by a commoner, so that's probably one more group of sidhe with better than average relationships with commoners.<br /> <br /> Again, with all this, and with the geographical list generally, my main point is simply variety. The new Connecticut Commonwealth may be new but this is a setting where it can exist! As can the other examples. <br /> <br /> Finally the Accordance War may have happened 25 years before 2e, but a lot of the sidhe participants were still around thanks to time spent in freeholds and the Dreaming. War criminals were still in charge, painting it as ancient history isn't quite accurate. Even setting that aside, Fool's Luck saw commoners and nobles on the verge of war. This conflict isn't new to the setting, nor is portraying the sidhe as an invading, occupying force.<br /> <br /> I don't think 2e painted the sidhe as blanket amtagonists, nor do I think C20 does. Like redcaps or the Unseelie Court, it's easy to make them antagonists, but I would not assume a redcap or Unseelie courtier I met in play was a villain, and the same goes for the sidhe. The setting, as written, provides plenty of options if you want to play a heroic sidhe unloathed by commoners. It's just also honest that a good portion of them see no moral issue with forcing people to adhere to the feudal system, violently if necessary - and it has always been honest about this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/187-beccatoria","name":"beccatoria","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar187_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"85"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-11T13:12:05-07:00","id":1091245,"title":"","content":"I wonder if part of the issue is Arcadian versus Autumn sidhe. In previous editions Autumn sidhe didn't even have rules outside of House Scathach, while in C20 they seem to make up the majority. And also in C20 Arcadian sidhe are presented as far more likely to be dicks. So if you're reading it thinking of your really cool and nice sidhe character from a previous edition you're disposed to think &quot;wait, my character has to be a dick now?!?&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10243-zenten","name":"zenten","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10243_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"488"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-11T13:29:23-07:00","id":1091249,"title":"","content":"Okay, then I would note that two houses+some few handfuls doesn't feel especially like a measurable minority or anything close. It mostly feels like &quot;the sidhe nobility are the default setting villains starving the fae to death barring the Fomorians/Thallain with rare exceptions&quot;. 2 out from 13 is pretty close to monolithic. The setting is doing a poor job at not making things feel monolithic unless you already happened to have a view of the kith as generally jerkasses anyway, in which case yes, I grant that the exceptions would feel notable, as opposed to feeling like a far lessened thing.<br /> <br /> The Connecticut Commonwealth exists because the commoners there overthrew the sidhe and installed themselves, that really doesn't say anything but.. the Connecticut Commonwealth exists because the commoners overthrew the sidhe, installed themselves, and are getting by on High King David not having commented one way or another yet. I'm not sure how that doesn't play in to the overall state of affairs or is some great stride in the sidhe as not the setting villains here. The entire idea is that the rule of the sidhe was so bad that they rebelled. Historical references again are stuff not changing that the current state is &quot;the sidhe on the whole are starving out the commoners&quot;.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The references to the courts of Aeron and Mary-Elizabeth are absolutely current. </div> </div> </div>That's two courts. Chief Greyhawk, without getting into anything else, boils down to &quot;the sidhe are okay.. when they completely abandon all their society, trappings and ties to their own kith&quot;. It's not great.<br /> <br /> House Danaan largely doesn't interact with the Autumn World and stays within the Dreaming, and given what the Dreaming does to the sidhe within it, for example, and that the house boon only protects from Bedlam, not the other stuff, their interpersonal relationships with commoners can't be all that great from simple mechanics. Even with setting that aside, it doesn't do much for the entire huge setting outside of the Dreaming, who can't really interact with it in much depth without risking Bedlam and other issues. And Dice as high lord is something of a &quot;sidhe are okay.. if they're not the ones actually running a thing&quot;. Setting any of that aside, they're noted out as a small group stretched between worlds who find the mortal world distasteful.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I don't think 2e painted the sidhe as blanket amtagonists, nor do I think C20 does. </div> </div> </div>They are, on the whole as a kith with small exceptions, starving the fae towards undoing, right now. Even the Accordance War ended and was a thing in the past of the setting. There's a significant line between &quot;enforcing feudal traditions&quot; and &quot;are currently actively starving out the other kiths through cowardice and blind ignorance&quot;.<br /> <br /> As far as Fool's Luck, that book came out during the &quot;High King David has vanished and now Concordia is spiralling towards multi factional civil war&quot; part of the plot, I couldn't see it not portraying things as heading towards war, that was the whole idea of Changeling around that period. It was however driven largely by &quot;David go poof, order collapses&quot;, not &quot;mass fae glamour starvation society wide&quot; <br /> <br /> As far as the Accordance War, while various participants were still around, a whole huge lot of fae, sidhe and otherwise, postdated it. That the various figures who did wretched things during it were around also is what I would have regarded as nuance and kiths being able to feel like they ran a gamut of awful to not. It's considerably different than what comes off as largely a broad sweeping statement of &quot;are starving the other kiths out, unless they are two houses, or some handfuls&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12141-markk","name":"MarkK","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-11T13:31:49-07:00","id":1091250,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>zenten</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1086863-it-s-out?p=1091245#post1091245\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wonder if part of the issue is Arcadian versus Autumn sidhe. In previous editions Autumn sidhe didn't even have rules outside of House Scathach, while in C20 they seem to make up the majority. And also in C20 Arcadian sidhe are presented as far more likely to be dicks. So if you're reading it thinking of your really cool and nice sidhe character from a previous edition you're disposed to think &quot;wait, my character has to be a dick now?!?&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>The Autumn sidhe comprise 2 out of 13 houses and some pieces of the others, that doesn't really make them a majority I would think. And honestly, the Autumn sidhe that are pieces of the other houses don't come off as being especially exempt from the current plot.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12141-markk","name":"MarkK","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-11T13:34:51-07:00","id":1091251,"title":"","content":"Liam is the most numerous house, and Arcadian sidhe don't come back, and were most numerous in the 70s.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10243-zenten","name":"zenten","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10243_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"488"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-11T13:46:13-07:00","id":1091258,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>zenten</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1086863-it-s-out?p=1091251#post1091251\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Liam is the most numerous house, and Arcadian sidhe don't come back, and were most numerous in the 70s.</div> </div> </div> </div>Arcadian Sidhe continue to come in in various glimmer rushes, there was that whole mass entry of the Lost Houses in the 90s besides. It's also more that Liam, lacking especially in lands, are particularly widespread. And again, it's not really like non Scathach and Liam sidhe of whatever stripe of the 13 houses are especially marked out as otherwise somehow exempt.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12141-markk","name":"MarkK","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-11T17:02:02-07:00","id":1091338,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MarkK</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1086863-it-s-out?p=1091208#post1091208\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It notes on page 64 that the Escheat specifically isn't backed by glamour like oaths are, and that the Dreaming only occasionally subtly steps in to put consequences onto people. Even under Safe haven it goes on a bit about the law falling down in practice and commoner freeholds being more likely to let fae in.<br /> <br /> If the idea was that no one can deny the right of hospitality without those consequences, the text there reads as contradicting thaty intent.</div> </div> </div> </div>The laws of hospitality are deeply woven into the mythology of all Fair Ones. Many cultures have ancient traditions of succor stemming from mythology. You give food and shelter because if you don't, bad things happen. <br /> <br /> If you want a tetchier answer, I wrote the Freehold section and am the developer for Book of Freeholds, which will go more deeply into the consequences of refusing to observe the Right of Hospitality. Suffice to say there are consequences. Freeholders don't have carte blanche to refuse to honor their Oaths, as long as the supplicant seeking sanctuary upholds their end.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Luka Carroll</b><br /> Onyx Path Freelancer &amp; Developer<br /> <i>Working On: </i>C20 Player's Guide, Lunars<br /> <i>Worked On: </i>V20 TMR, Demon STG, C20, Book of Freeholds, Conquering Heroes, Building A Legend, Dragon-Blooded, The Realm","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3785-luka-c","name":"Luka C","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3785_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"175"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-11T18:21:24-07:00","id":1091363,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maggie C</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1086863-it-s-out?p=1091338#post1091338\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The laws of hospitality are deeply woven into the mythology of all Fair Ones. Many cultures have ancient traditions of succor stemming from mythology. You give food and shelter because if you don't, bad things happen.<br /> <br /> If you want a tetchier answer, I wrote the Freehold section and am the developer for Book of Freeholds, which will go more deeply into the consequences of refusing to observe the Right of Hospitality. Suffice to say there are consequences. Freeholders don't have carte blanche to refuse to honor their Oaths, as long as the supplicant seeking sanctuary upholds their end.</div> </div> </div> </div>I apologize for prodding any tetchiness, I'm just rolling off what's noted in the core really.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12141-markk","name":"MarkK","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-11T19:23:50-07:00","id":1091385,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maggie C</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1086863-it-s-out?p=1091128#post1091128\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They aren't, no. But they can't just kick someone out wihout shelter or deny them sanctuary for a night, because the Dreaming enforces the Right of Hospitality. Denying someone shelter or passage into the Dreaming usually results in the freehold's benefits being withdrawn from its holder. Even Glamour-hoarding sidhe know better than to fuck with that law.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Under the &quot;Reality&quot; section on Right of Safe haven it straight up says Nobles regularly don't let people in. In France if you aren't oathbound as a commoner they don't let you in.. this seems in contradiction.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-12T01:06:18-07:00","id":1091450,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MarkK</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1086863-it-s-out?p=1091249#post1091249\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay, then I would note that two houses+some few handfuls doesn't feel especially like a measurable minority or anything close. It mostly feels like &quot;the sidhe nobility are the default setting villains starving the fae to death barring the Fomorians/Thallain with rare exceptions&quot;. 2 out from 13 is pretty close to monolithic. The setting is doing a poor job at not making things feel monolithic unless you already happened to have a view of the kith as generally jerkasses anyway, in which case yes, I grant that the exceptions would feel notable, as opposed to feeling like a far lessened thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay, I'm not sure how useful it's going to be to continue this because I don't feel much like you're engaging with my points, more repeating your perception of them. Which you know, fine, we have fundamentally different views of how it's presented, that's going to happen. But as an example of that, you've twice repeated that the only way you feel it's consistent between the editions is if you already saw the sidhe as jerks. I strongly disagree because I didn't view them as blanket jerks in either edition, and think they're consistent between the two. <br /> <br /> A sizable portion of the sidhe nobility becoming panicked and shutting their freeholds to outsiders and commoners is a background tension and rising political problem. That's how it feels to me. Commoners have their own freeholds and dreamers, and with Revelry now a part of the game, gathering glamour is a lot easier for an individual fae. A local sidhe lord suddenly becoming less free with the glamour is painful and difficult and might be the biggest tension in a chronicle's plot, but not necessarily. <br /> <br /> I also want to point out 2 out of 13 is 15%. That's definitely a measurable minority. That's not monolithic. It's also <i>not</i> 2 out of 13 houses. That's what I was trying to point out. House Fiona is stated to have left <i>many</i> behind, not handfuls. House Eiluned also left enough behind, in a structured way, it's worthy of named notice in their brief write-up. House Danaan is a third house that is actively friendly to commoners. House Daireann may not be required to provide glamour to commoners staying in freeholds, but in 2e I never assumed balefire access was part of freehold access. They're still required to provide a safe place to sleep free from the ravages of banality, safe from the ravages of time, with ready access to the Dreaming. That WILL save a changeling on the verge of forgetting who she is. House Leanhaun is said to be led by a noble much-admired by commoners. An individual Leanhaun may be hated by them, but many commoners are probably going to have a kinder view of that house if they know its leader is in the Parliament of Dreams advocating for political reforms that favour them. <br /> <br /> So, if you want to play a sidhe that's not a bad guy, or run a game where you have sidhe who aren't bad guys and aren't seen that way by commoners, you have a LOT of options. You have three commoner-friendly houses, including the most widespread house. You have a further two where it's extremely easy to justify an Autumn sidhe (and I have no idea why you think that's not relevant when everything in C20 that deals with Autumn sidhe goes to pains to explain that they're viewed differently by fae society). You then have a further two houses where their code of honour or their current leader can easily explain a better relationship with commoners <i>if you want to</i>. <br /> <br /> That's NOT two houses and a few handfuls unless you're invested in reading it that way. It's a broad statement about the current political climate followed by a much more mixed series of individual examples. But even if it were, it's definitely a measurable minority. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MarkK</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1086863-it-s-out?p=1091249#post1091249\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Connecticut Commonwealth exists because the commoners there overthrew the sidhe and installed themselves, that really doesn't say anything but.. the Connecticut Commonwealth exists because the commoners overthrew the sidhe, installed themselves, and are getting by on High King David not having commented one way or another yet. I'm not sure how that doesn't play in to the overall state of affairs or is some great stride in the sidhe as not the setting villains here. The entire idea is that the rule of the sidhe was so bad that they rebelled. Historical references again are stuff not changing that the current state is &quot;the sidhe on the whole are starving out the commoners&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>Again, I wasn't referencing the Commonwealth as an example of how great the sidhe may be, I was trying to point out all the situations that break from this monolithic setting C20 is apparently portraying. It's another place a game could be set - if one felt strongly that one had to stick strictly to canon - where sidhe might not be seen as oppressors, if they chose to stay and support the elected council. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MarkK</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1086863-it-s-out?p=1091249#post1091249\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's two courts. Chief Greyhawk, without getting into anything else, boils down to &quot;the sidhe are okay.. when they completely abandon all their society, trappings and ties to their own kith&quot;. It's not great.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's two courts run by two of the seven monarchs of Concordia. That carries weight. Two of the highest-ranking nobles in the entire land making a point of remaining welcoming to all in difficult times is surely indicative that this perspective isn't shockingly rare. <br /> <br /> Again, Chief Greyhawk isn't an example I raise to say &quot;oh look, the sidhe are okay,&quot; but rather, like the Commonwealth, to say, &quot;hey, here's yet another canonical setting where the sidhe will be interacting with commoners in a different way, indicating, yet again, that the broad trend is not monolithic.&quot; It's an example of an exception. I'm not saying that all exceptions are for the same reasons. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MarkK</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1086863-it-s-out?p=1091249#post1091249\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">House Danaan largely doesn't interact with the Autumn World and stays within the Dreaming, and given what the Dreaming does to the sidhe within it, for example, and that the house boon only protects from Bedlam, not the other stuff, their interpersonal relationships with commoners can't be all that great from simple mechanics. Even with setting that aside, it doesn't do much for the entire huge setting outside of the Dreaming, who can't really interact with it in much depth without risking Bedlam and other issues. And Dice as high lord is something of a &quot;sidhe are okay.. if they're not the ones actually running a thing&quot;. Setting any of that aside, they're noted out as a small group stretched between worlds who find the mortal world distasteful.</div> </div> </div> </div>And some changeling games are primarily set in the Dreaming. And again, a sidhe from House Danaan - commoners could validly go, &quot;Huh, a sidhe happy to serve a commoner lord, guess maybe this guy's not as much as a jerk as the others...&quot; They may be a small house, but they loom large within a specific setting of the game - the Dreaming. Their appearance is also a plot point, and they're said to be making contact for the first time in a long time, so they hold narrative weight. Yet again, it's an example of the canonical setting throwing out a TON of exceptions, in various ways, for various reasons.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MarkK</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1086863-it-s-out?p=1091249#post1091249\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They are, on the whole as a kith with small exceptions, starving the fae towards undoing, right now. Even the Accordance War ended and was a thing in the past of the setting. There's a significant line between &quot;enforcing feudal traditions&quot; and &quot;are currently actively starving out the other kiths through cowardice and blind ignorance&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>I disagree when enforcing feudal traditions involved murder and theft of freeholds that were once commoner run. I think being selfish about resources (which are available elsewhere, if not as easily), is far preferable to outright war. <br /> <br /> I also feel like there are a lot of exceptions to the view you're taking, which you choose to dismiss and decide don't count or aren't enough, which is your call, of course. But I don't think it's the objectively correct one. There's no more reason to give primacy to a paragraph in the historical section than there is to give it to the descriptions of the houses and holdings that make it clear not everyone is acting this way. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/187-beccatoria","name":"beccatoria","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar187_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"85"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-12T07:34:53-07:00","id":1091525,"title":"","content":"Did anyone post a link?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-12T07:37:50-07:00","id":1091527,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1086863-it-s-out?p=1091525#post1091525\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Did anyone post a link?</div> </div> </div> </div>To C20? The link is in your BackerKit account if you backed the Kickstarter.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Charlie Cantrell</b><br /> Onyx Path Freelancer <hr />Changeling: The Dreaming 20th Anniversary Edition, Conquering Heroes, Book of Freeholds, Guide to the Night, C20 Players Guide","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/648-pookaknight","name":"PookaKnight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar648_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"690"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-12T09:48:05-07:00","id":1091587,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Okay, I'm not sure how useful it's going to be to continue this because I don't feel much like you're engaging with my points, more repeating your perception of them. Which you know, fine, we have fundamentally different views of how it's presented, that's going to happen. But as an example of that, you've twice repeated that the only way you feel it's consistent between the editions is if you already saw the sidhe as jerks. I strongly disagree because I didn't view them as blanket jerks in either edition, and think they're consistent between the two. </div> </div> </div>Honestly by the same token it doesn't really feel much like you reply to mine? I talk about the current metaplot being the sidhe starving out the commoner kiths, and you keep noting stuff about sidhe having historically stayed behind repeatedly, which has absolutely nothing to do with that. That doesn't do anything about what the current plot is. You talk about &quot;I don't view them as blanket jerks&quot; but have previously noted how the sidhe are &quot;broadly speaking, pretty jerky&quot;, going on about the Accordance War and how many of the sidhe involved in it are war criminals that must still be around and what have you. It feels like &quot;I'm not saying they're jerks, I'm just saying, they're pretty jerky&quot;. I don't really see the difference?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> A sizable portion of the sidhe nobility becoming panicked and shutting their freeholds to outsiders and commoners is a background tension and rising political problem. That's how it feels to me. Commoners have their own freeholds and dreamers, and with Revelry now a part of the game, gathering glamour is a lot easier for an individual fae. A local sidhe lord suddenly becoming less free with the glamour is painful and difficult and might be the biggest tension in a chronicle's plot, but not necessarily. </div> </div> </div>Okay, similarly this, it feels like this kind of thing is not engaging with the setting itself in order to keep a debate going, which explicitly in so many words describes various freeholds as having outright collapsed, and a society so driven to the edge that open protest movements have sprung up, the nobility described in broad spectrum turns as keeping commoners out/ignoring their problems to the point that even the titled commoner members of houses are doing it, and that gathering glamour is so hard that some fae in desperation have begun to turn to the Fomorians/Thallain.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> House Fiona is stated to have left <i>many</i> behind, not handfuls. House Eiluned also left enough behind, in a structured way, it's worthy of named notice in their brief write-up. House Danaan is a third house that is actively friendly to commoners. </div> </div> </div>The first two things have nothing to do with the current state of the setting. And House Danaan again barely exists in the Autumn World, focused upon the Dreaming. It's also a bit frustrating when you cite the system over the setting for stuff like &quot;it's not that bad with glamour&quot;, then talk about House Danaan being actively friendly to commoners when the mechanics of sidhe in the Dreaming would put huge obstacles in the way of that. And again, House Danaan feels mostly like &quot;the sidhe are okay if someone else is leading&quot;.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> So, if you want to play a sidhe that's not a bad guy, or run a game where you have sidhe who aren't bad guys and aren't seen that way by commoners, you have a LOT of options. You have three commoner-friendly houses, including the most widespread house. You have a further two where it's extremely easy to justify an Autumn sidhe (and I have no idea why you think that's not relevant when everything in C20 that deals with Autumn sidhe goes to pains to explain that they're viewed differently by fae society). You then have a further two houses where their code of honour or their current leader can easily explain a better relationship with commoners <i>if you want to</i>. </div> </div> </div>You have two houses out of 13, a house that doesn't largely interact with the rest of the world, and pieces of other houses. And I don't really find it relevant when they're noted as still being part of the nobility, and the nobility right down to titled commoners are being described as broad spectrum acting a certain way. I don't really have any idea why you can set that part of the plot aside. Again, this mostly feels like we're talking past each other.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Again, I wasn't referencing the Commonwealth as an example of how great the sidhe may be, I was trying to point out all the situations that break from this monolithic setting C20 is apparently portraying. It's another place a game could be set - if one felt strongly that one had to stick strictly to canon - where sidhe might not be seen as oppressors, if they chose to stay and support the elected council. </div> </div> </div>It fits into a setting of the sidhe/nobility as jerkass oppressors just fine when it's a domain that to get by had to overthrow their sidhe rulership and put untitled commoners in charge.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It's two courts run by two of the seven monarchs of Concordia. That carries weight. Two of the highest-ranking nobles in the entire land making a point of remaining welcoming to all in difficult times is surely indicative that this perspective isn't shockingly rare. </div> </div> </div>It's all the same two courts, and it looks to carry not much weight given the description of the state of fae society overall, to the point that even the description of the realities of the Right of Safe Haven talk about the nobility being more inclined to ignore said piece of the Escheat compared to commoners.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Again, Chief Greyhawk isn't an example I raise to say &quot;oh look, the sidhe are okay,&quot; but rather, like the Commonwealth, to say, &quot;hey, here's yet another canonical setting where the sidhe will be interacting with commoners in a different way, indicating, yet again, that the broad trend is not monolithic.&quot; It's an example of an exception. I'm not saying that all exceptions are for the same reasons. </div> </div> </div>But again, you don't really address what I'm saying about what the exception says. It seems mostly to be for you that as long as you can point out some exception to the overall state of fae society, regardless of any actual details, it's clearly not that bad as far as the depiction of the sidhe in relation to current affairs, despite being described outright in so many words as that bad. And when an issue multiple posters in the thread are having is &quot;the sidhe come off as starkly godawful jerks in a way they didn't in previous editions&quot;, pointing to &quot;well there's this guy who completely abandoned the mores and trappings of his own kith&quot;, doesn't really deal with that at all.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And some changeling games are primarily set in the Dreaming. And again, a sidhe from House Danaan - commoners could validly go, &quot;Huh, a sidhe happy to serve a commoner lord, guess maybe this guy's not as much as a jerk as the others...&quot; They may be a small house, but they loom large within a specific setting of the game - the Dreaming. Their appearance is also a plot point, and they're said to be making contact for the first time in a long time, so they hold narrative weight. Yet again, it's an example of the canonical setting throwing out a TON of exceptions, in various ways, for various reasons. </div> </div> </div>Most fae who go to the Dreaming will be largely unable to remember in any great detail, or detail at all, of what they experienced in the Dreaming, a place where they can't stay that long besides or fall into Bedlam. So, your exceptions are, two courts, a guy who basically threw off his own kith, the sidhe being kicked out of power in Connecticut for the poor quality of their rule, two houses, the sidhe being okay when they cast off overall authority otherwise, two houses in the Autumn World. In the face of a sweeping description of an overall setting, I have to ask you if it's really that hard to understand why there have been various posts going &quot;oof, the sidhe come off way more awful here&quot;.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I disagree when enforcing feudal traditions involved murder and theft of freeholds that were once commoner run. I think being selfish about resources (which are available elsewhere, if not as easily), is far preferable to outright war. </div> </div> </div>But again, all that stuff was setting backdrop. It came to an end years before the setting started. Starving the other kiths to Undoing is happening right now. And the setting does not treat said resources as being available elsewhere in the manner and frequency you are talking about. By the setting, glamour has grown scarce, entire holds have collapsed, the fae as a society are growing desperate and angry. It feels mostly like you want to gloss over that. It's kind of hard to gloss over when that's the default setting.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I also feel like there are a lot of exceptions to the view you're taking, which you choose to dismiss and decide don't count or aren't enough, which is your call, of course. But I don't think it's the objectively correct one. There's no more reason to give primacy to a paragraph in the historical section than there is to give it to the descriptions of the houses and holdings that make it clear not everyone is acting this way. </div> </div> </div>When it's the section that provides the current state of the world? When it's described in such starkly dramatic terms? To the point that the Escheat itself is impacted by it? The Starvation of Dreams, the Present Day, the Shadow Court reborn as desperate protest movement are more than &quot;a paragraph&quot;, and it feels pretty dismissive to be told that putting credence in what they say is objectively wrong. I mean one of the sections is outright called &quot;the Starvation of Dreams&quot;, that's a pretty dramatic thing to wave off to talk about how it's not really that bad.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12141,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12141-markk","user":"MarkK","date":". 05-12-2017, 12:52 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12141-markk","name":"MarkK","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-12T09:59:40-07:00","id":1091595,"title":"","content":"Just on the &quot;measurable minority&quot; thing, as I sort of missed it in the sprawl as far as what I wanted to say there. When in previous editions the state of the sidhe as a kith came off as well more mixed, it doesn't feel like a measurable minority, it feels like a huge reduction of things. When your counterarguement to that is &quot;no, that's totally in line with their previous portrayal&quot;, that mostly comes off as saying &quot;no, the sidhe were always a people where only a minority were not jerks.&quot; You might think that people who didn't view the setting that way are wrong, but is it possible to note that if they did view the setting differently, this portrayal would feel like a huge shift to them? It feels mostly like being told &quot;well if you thought that then, you didn't get Changeling then either&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12141,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12141-markk","user":"MarkK","date":". 05-12-2017, 01:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12141-markk","name":"MarkK","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-12T10:13:46-07:00","id":1091602,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MarkK</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1086863-it-s-out?p=1091595#post1091595\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It feels mostly like being told &quot;well if you thought that then, you didn't get Changeling then either&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>A point which cuts both ways so we should probably leave it there. <br /> <br /> We disagree on which parts of the book hold the most weight when drawing a picture of the setting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/187-beccatoria","name":"beccatoria","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar187_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"85"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-12T10:21:36-07:00","id":1091607,"title":"","content":"Well, on the &quot;there is nothing new under the sun&quot; side of things, if there was anything previously defining about Changeling and the talks around it that has definitely carried over.. *cough*<br /> <br /> (A joke. No one has called the sidhe p-zombies yet, this has definitely been one of the more restrained discussions on the kith I've seen on the internets. So I appreciate that at least.)<br /> <br /> Edit: I suppose I'll just leave it with this as far as what I'm mostly getting at here. For me, and I'm really just saying for me, it sort of says something that the previous edition's sidhe argument was mostly in my experience &quot;are the sidhe jerks or not&quot;, with various credible arguments either way, and it made it feel like there was some space on the issue, and in the game itself, to find whatever position. Here the big debate has been &quot;is there enough of a minority of the sidhe who aren't jerks so that the kith doesn't feel godawful as a whole.&quot; And that's a reduction in a particular direction.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12141,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12141-markk","user":"MarkK","date":". 05-12-2017, 01:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12141-markk","name":"MarkK","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-12T10:35:08-07:00","id":1091613,"title":"","content":"I have decided from this that when I run C20 just about all the Sidhe Freeholder owners will (at least very grudgingly) respect the Right of Safe Haven. <br /> <br /> Out of curiosity, what's the rules (as in in game official legal position) regarding the Right of Safe Haven on Oathbreakers, minor criminals, etc?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10243-zenten","name":"zenten","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10243_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"488"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-12T10:50:16-07:00","id":1091618,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MarkK</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1086863-it-s-out?p=1091607#post1091607\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, on the &quot;there is nothing new under the sun&quot; side of things, if there was anything previously defining about Changeling and the talks around it that has definitely carried over.. *cough*<br /> <br /> (A joke. No one has called the sidhe p-zombies yet, this has definitely been one of the more restrained discussions on the kith I've seen on the internets. So I appreciate that at least.)<br /> <br /> Edit: I suppose I'll just leave it with this as far as what I'm mostly getting at here. For me, and I'm really just saying for me, it sort of says something that the previous edition's sidhe argument was mostly in my experience &quot;are the sidhe jerks or not&quot;, with various credible arguments either way, and it made it feel like there was some space on the issue, and in the game itself, to find whatever position. Here the big debate has been &quot;is there enough of a minority of the sidhe who aren't jerks so that the kith doesn't feel godawful as a whole.&quot; And that's a reduction in a particular direction.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> But I think, at least in part, that's down to framing. The discussion started because some people, including yourself, felt the sidhe were suddenly portrayed in a much more villainous fashion - that means that the sidhe's level of villainy is centred immediately. Had the discussion started because someone was incredibly happy that the Autumn sidhe now existed in a more formal way, or who were thrilled at the way is was now possible to play a Leanhaun who wasn't utterly amoral, or who loved House Danaan, or what have you, then the discussion might have been framed very differently and might have been, much more, about whether or not the sidhe were jerks or not? <br /> <br /> I suppose, just to try and clarify my position for a final time, I think the Men in Black quote is appropriate: &quot;A person is smart. People are dumb, panicky, dangerous animals and you know it.&quot; I feel like the sidhe, overall, are kinda jerks. Not evil, just...kinda jerks. The feudal system isn't kind to those at the bottom of it and the sidhe, overall, are keeping it in place, so, overall, they're kind of jerks. Individual sidhe within that run the entire gamut from evil to selflessly heroic. There will be some that are heroic by fighting the feudal system and some that are heroic by believing in it but being truly benevolent and kind rulers. And I suspect that, outside radical elements, most changelings are able to understand that difference between the sidhe as an institution and individual sidhe they meet as well. <br /> <br /> I hope that's clearer at least. <br /> <br /> But to reiterate, I don't think we'll get much further on this, and if all we're doing is making each other feel we don't &quot;get&quot; the setting, that's not fun and we shouldn't do it. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/187-beccatoria","name":"beccatoria","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar187_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"85"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-12T11:05:48-07:00","id":1091624,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I hope that's clearer at least. </div> </div> </div>Not really to be honest with you. I'm just not going to be able to put &quot;mostly starving the rest of the kithain out&quot; as something that can be moved past/around. But I think all that can be said there has largely been said at length. <br /> <br /> Anyway, if we've hit the point of discussing this only being an issue because some people, myself included, framed it as an issue (which is not great as discussions that treat the other party as credible go), it's probably for the best to leave it there, yeah.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12141-markk","name":"MarkK","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-12T11:21:08-07:00","id":1091630,"title":"","content":"I didn't mean it was only an issue because you framed it as one. I meant that the way an issue is raised frames the <i>discussion</i>, but this is<i> always</i> the case and was not intended to be dismissive. Apologies if it sounded that way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/187-beccatoria","name":"beccatoria","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar187_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"85"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-12T14:23:19-07:00","id":1091706,"title":"","content":"Fair enough then. But there's not really a way for people to bring up &quot;the sidhe come off far more terribly in this edition than before&quot; without basically saying, well, that, in one form or another.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12141-markk","name":"MarkK","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-13T00:57:42-07:00","id":1091857,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MarkK</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1086863-it-s-out?p=1091706#post1091706\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Fair enough then. But there's not really a way for people to bring up &quot;the sidhe come off far more terribly in this edition than before&quot; without basically saying, well, that, in one form or another.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Agreed! I just don't think raising it proves an objective shift either. That was all I meant.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/187-beccatoria","name":"beccatoria","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar187_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"85"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-13T12:09:46-07:00","id":1092034,"title":"","content":"Okay. I don't by contrast think &quot;is the gone into at length default plot&quot; can be waved off like that.<br /> <br /> But really, the book is done barring errata, and it is what it is. Those who feel put off by that stuff feel put off by it, and those who don't, well, they have a new edition of Changeling to enjoy.<br /> <br /> It's a shame, as there's any number of things the book did that I really, really liked, but if there's one thing the discussions and replies in this thread crystalized for me, it's that I'm probably not going to be into the line going forward if this is the take on things it runs with. I imagine plenty of people will, and it's honestly good that they have stuff to look forward to.<br /> <br /> (*counts down to someone drive by-ing with &quot;well it's a good thing no one is coming to take your old books away&quot;, notes ahead of time that it hardly matters if most people move on from using them*)<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12141,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12141-markk","user":"MarkK","date":". 05-13-2017, 03:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12141-markk","name":"MarkK","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-13T12:12:35-07:00","id":1092036,"title":"","content":"I'm a bit confused why this that strong of an issue for you. Making it fit how you want is a really easy setting change with no mechanical impact, and I don't see that being different for future supplements.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10243-zenten","name":"zenten","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10243_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"488"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-13T12:17:10-07:00","id":1092040,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>zenten</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1086863-it-s-out?p=1092036#post1092036\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm a bit confused why this that strong of an issue for you. Making it fit how you want is a really easy setting change with no mechanical impact, and I don't see that being different for future supplements.</div> </div> </div> </div>The default setting characterizes default play, and if most of your gaming is with groups of total strangers who've never really met before (which in my own experience a lot of gaming increasingly is), the path of easiest to get a game going is to run with it. It basically boils things down to &quot;well so long as you're the one running and can get everyone else to agree to the changes you want to make..&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12141-markk","name":"MarkK","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-13T12:23:37-07:00","id":1092044,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MarkK</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1086863-it-s-out?p=1092040#post1092040\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The default setting characterizes default play, and if most of your gaming is with groups of total strangers who've never really met before (which in my own experience a lot of gaming increasingly is), the path of easiest to get a game going is to run with it. It basically boils things down to &amp;quot;well so long as you're the one running and can get everyone else to agree to the changes you want to make..&amp;quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, that is how I approach games like Changeling the Dreaming. I don't think I could play/run any White Wolf game successfully in the mode you're talking about because of the rules not being well defined.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10243-zenten","name":"zenten","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10243_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"488"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-13T12:28:31-07:00","id":1092047,"title":"","content":"We've had different experiences in gaming then?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12141-markk","name":"MarkK","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-13T12:32:12-07:00","id":1092050,"title":"","content":"Obviously so","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10243-zenten","name":"zenten","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10243_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"488"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-13T12:53:02-07:00","id":1092058,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>zenten</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1086863-it-s-out?p=1092044#post1092044\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ah, that is how I approach games like Changeling the Dreaming. I don't think I could play/run any White Wolf game successfully in the mode you're talking about because of the rules not being well defined.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm the same way. I don't think I've run any game exactly as written, and I doubt I ever will (including C20 which I helped write!).<br /> <br /> The sidhe thing is such a minor item overall in C20, it's simple to modify to make it more palatable. I even offered an alternate take earlier in the thread that makes most sidhe heroic without contradicting C20's state of the world.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Charlie Cantrell</b><br /> Onyx Path Freelancer <hr />Changeling: The Dreaming 20th Anniversary Edition, Conquering Heroes, Book of Freeholds, Guide to the Night, C20 Players Guide","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/648-pookaknight","name":"PookaKnight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar648_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"690"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-13T13:50:17-07:00","id":1092087,"title":"","content":"I've certainly modified rules when I've run, and what all ever else, but as a player (and sometimes as a GM talking things out with players honestly) I've largely found that people hew to the setting that's there. If your experience has been different, that's great. If you find the whole thing minor, I can certainly see how it could be looked on that way given where someone might put priority or emphasis. For me, it's a take on what feels like most of an entire kith, and significant for me thereby.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12141-markk","name":"MarkK","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-13T14:55:49-07:00","id":1092110,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MarkK</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1086863-it-s-out?p=1092034#post1092034\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay. I don't by contrast think &quot;is the gone into at length default plot&quot; can be waved off like that.<br /> <br /> But really, the book is done barring errata, and it is what it is. Those who feel put off by that stuff feel put off by it, and those who don't, well, they have a new edition of Changeling to enjoy.<br /> <br /> It's a shame, as there's any number of things the book did that I really, really liked, but if there's one thing the discussions and replies in this thread crystalized for me, it's that I'm probably not going to be into the line going forward if this is the take on things it runs with. I imagine plenty of people will, and it's honestly good that they have stuff to look forward to.<br /> <br /> (*counts down to someone drive by-ing with &quot;well it's a good thing no one is coming to take your old books away&quot;, notes ahead of time that it hardly matters if most people move on from using them*)</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> I feel like the old books were.. probably worse on the sidhe? the Unseelie houses are no longer explicitly a fifth column for the Formorians(even fi they can be duped into it), Autumn Sidhe are inherently going to &quot;Win out&quot; the demographics war (assuming final winter doesn't happen). They now are responsible for many Nunehei reclamations in a post Ressurgence. Yes there are 1 percenters who won't let you in their freehold.. but as I quoted the same exact thing is there in the 2e book. Autumn Sidhe by themselves let you play up everything about Sidhe and you know not become a heartless bastard n the Dreaming.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-13T15:27:01-07:00","id":1092115,"title":"","content":"Compared to Kithbook: Eshu, C20 is positively loving with the Sidhe.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>When will you rage?","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1405-anteros","name":"Anteros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1405_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-13T15:30:28-07:00","id":1092118,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Anteros</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1086863-it-s-out?p=1092115#post1092115\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Compared to Kithbook: Eshu, C20 is positively loving with the Sidhe.</div> </div> </div> </div>A bar so low that it sits near the asthenosphere.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-13T15:38:49-07:00","id":1092121,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1086863-it-s-out?p=1092118#post1092118\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> A bar so low that it sits near the asthenosphere.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> or Fools Luck. Or the Shining Host, Or the first two Book of Houses...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-13T15:51:59-07:00","id":1092127,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1086863-it-s-out?p=1092110#post1092110\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> I feel like the old books were.. probably worse on the sidhe? the Unseelie houses are no longer explicitly a fifth column for the Formorians(even fi they can be duped into it), Autumn Sidhe are inherently going to &quot;Win out&quot; the demographics war (assuming final winter doesn't happen). They now are responsible for many Nunehei reclamations in a post Ressurgence. Yes there are 1 percenters who won't let you in their freehold.. but as I quoted the same exact thing is there in the 2e book. Autumn Sidhe by themselves let you play up everything about Sidhe and you know not become a heartless bastard n the Dreaming.</div> </div> </div> </div>The plot in 2e doesn't note the sidhe as a kith keeping the commoners from freeholds to the point that kithain society is facing glamour starvation, so commonly that even commoners who are members of houses are doing it. And really only the Balor were a fifth column for the Fomorians, the Ailil were just inclined to use Thallain as servants, they had no desire to see Fomorian win and had groups in house that fought against the very idea (the Cold Riders and what have you). The unseelie houses that came over in the lost house wave generally actively placed themselves against the Fomorians, and the Leanhaun had their own agenda exclusive to themselves kept secret from all.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Compared to Kithbook: Eshu, C20 is positively loving with the Sidhe. </div> </div> </div>If we're at the point of &quot;hey, at least they're better treated than in kithbook Eshu.&quot; That's not.. great, y'know? That basically is &quot;be happy it's not worse.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Or the first two Book of Houses... </div> </div> </div>The first two books of houses are places where you get things like &quot;the Dougal had a chunk of their house that stayed behind, but were murdered off by the commoner kiths, the modern Dougal politely try to pretend this isn't a thing&quot;. Even Shining Host is where you get stuff like the sidhe being split amongst political movements that included reformists and modernists and etc. I guess I found that state of affairs more mixed. Like I say, and it seems to be the thing here, if you thought the sidhe came off badly before/were basically awful before anywho, C20 seems generous. If you didn't, it doesn't.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12141-markk","name":"MarkK","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-13T16:04:41-07:00","id":1092132,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1086863-it-s-out?p=1092121#post1092121\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> or Fools Luck. Or the Shining Host, Or the first two Book of Houses...</div> </div> </div> </div>Or KB Redcaps, or War in Concordia...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10243-zenten","name":"zenten","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10243_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"488"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-13T16:32:11-07:00","id":1092143,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>zenten</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1086863-it-s-out?p=1092132#post1092132\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Or KB Redcaps, or War in Concordia...</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Is anyone treated well in KB Redcap?<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MarkK</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1086863-it-s-out?p=1092127#post1092127\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The plot in 2e doesn't note the sidhe as a kith keeping the commoners from freeholds to the point that kithain society is facing glamour starvation, so commonly that even commoners who are members of houses are doing it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Right they were just kicking them out to starve in the streets because they were assholes. Now they actually have some reasons. The 1e and 2e Escheat actively say that Nobles regularly were already doing this.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And really only the Balor were a fifth column for the Fomorians, the Ailil were just inclined to use Thallain as servants, they had no desire to see Fomorian win and had groups in house that fought against the very idea (the Cold Riders and what have you). The unseelie houses that came over in the lost house wave generally actively placed themselves against the Fomorians, and the Leanhaun had their own agenda exclusive to themselves kept secret from all. </div> </div> </div>The Entire Unseelie court was treated on and off as a Fifth column for the Formorians. Balor was most extreme about this but there were plenty of bits like this. I'll also point out you can play a Seelie Balor now, Balor actively aren't Formorian fifth columnists anymore. Lets compare Leanhaun's House flaw's nerf with brought them down from &quot;Unplayable monsters&quot; to something <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The first two books of houses are places where you get things like &quot;the Dougal had a chunk of their house that stayed behind, but were murdered off by the commoner kiths, the modern Dougal politely try to pretend this isn't a thing&quot;. Even Shining Host is where you get stuff like the sidhe being split amongst political movements that included reformists and modernists and etc. I guess I found that state of affairs more mixed. Like I say, and it seems to be the thing here, if you thought the sidhe came off badly before/were basically awful before anywho, C20 seems generous. If you didn't, it doesn't. </div> </div> </div>I don't feel that the older books were more mixed in their discussion. There definately were profound exceptions to &quot;The nobles are assholes&quot; but a general refrain of &quot;Nobles are kind of assholes&quot; because you know WOD GothPUNKness is pretty solidly there. Yeah the starvation of Dreams is the big scary thing for changeling and the reason why they are totally about to go to war(like how it was in 2e) but when you get to the write up of Concordia you have a wide variety of domains from commoner run commonwealths to those who don't turn away anyone to those who are friends with the Nunehei etc.<br /> <br /> I straight up think there's greater diversity on Sidhe in C20 than there was in the 2e Core, and at has much fewer &quot;OH MY GOD EVIIIIIIIIL&quot; bits than Shining Host, Fools Luck, First two book of Houses. Yeah they aren't being &quot;good&quot; rulers but they also aren't hitting the heights of monstrocity either. And serious if we are comparing Sidhe in the entiriety of 2e vs Sidhe in C20 you have to include Kithbook Eshu and how much it pulls it down. <br /> <br /> Conversely Autumn sidhe basically seem to have run off with most of what I used to try and argue for the Good parts of Sidhe.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-13T18:15:58-07:00","id":1092175,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Right they were just kicking them out to starve in the streets because they were assholes. Now they actually have some reasons. The 1e and 2e Escheat actively say that Nobles regularly were already doing this. </div> </div> </div>The point would be that it wasn't so common that nobles did this to the point that the Shadow Court becomes a mass protest movement nor that it was done so commonly as to be a broad spectrum problem, nor that it was a behaviour noted to even titled commoners.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Is anyone treated well in KB Redcap? </div> </div> </div>Redcaps. But various of the kithbooks are pretty crappy to the other kiths not the central kith of the book and all. Sluagh had that whole &quot;all Changelings become sluagh and trolls as a kith are racist morons&quot; thing or something like that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Entire Unseelie court was treated on and off as a Fifth column for the Formorians. Balor was most extreme about this but there were plenty of bits like this. I'll also point out you can play a Seelie Balor now, Balor actively aren't Formorian fifth columnists anymore. Lets compare Leanhaun's House flaw's nerf with brought them down from &quot;Unplayable monsters&quot; to something </div> </div> </div>When I'm giving repeated examples of &quot;entire houses were in fact not&quot;, I really don't know what to tell you. 2e in a bunch of places went in pretty hard that the unseelie were waging war with the Fomorians just fine. Even in Shadow Court, the big 1e book that was all &quot;the Shadow Court is totes in love with the Fomorians and every other awful thing&quot;, it still had the Knights of the Cold Watch going &quot;nope!&quot; The big exception, certainly in 2e, was House Balor to the point that it was held up their big secret from the rest of the fae, unseelie included, that they served the Fomorians, to the point that it was one of House Scathach's big in house aggravations of not being able to expose what they were doing to the rest of the fae. The Leanhaun didn't serve the Fomorians in 2e, they served themselves and their own hidden Armageddon prophecy agenda. Also when ravaging is a banality trigger and glamour is otherwise supposed to be scarce and whatever, and musing requires pretty huge piles of glamour to work, the Leanhaun flaw, while certainly kinder on them than previous, is not /that/ kind.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I don't feel that the older books were more mixed in their discussion. There definately were profound exceptions to &quot;The nobles are assholes&quot; but a general refrain of &quot;Nobles are kind of assholes&quot; because you know WOD GothPUNKness is pretty solidly there. Yeah the starvation of Dreams is the big scary thing for changeling and the reason why they are totally about to go to war(like how it was in 2e) but when you get to the write up of Concordia you have a wide variety of domains from commoner run commonwealths to those who don't turn away anyone to those who are friends with the Nunehei etc. </div> </div> </div>For the simple lack of not currently actively starving the rest of fae society to undoing by their cowardly ignorance, the older books were more mixed in their discussion. The Accordance War being an in the past event that a bunch of faerie society now postdated as far as having nothing to do with it, as opposed to a big current sweeping societal thing, made the older books more mixed in their discussion. Exceptions to &quot;the nobles are assholes&quot; came in the form of entire pan house factions/movements within the sidhe to the point that the movements had names for being prevalent enough as opposed to &quot;two houses out of 13, a few courts, and maybe some pieces of others, but then again even the titled commoners that are part of houses are being bastards, so..&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> (like how it was in 2e) </div> </div> </div>They were about to go to war in 2e because everyone was about to go to war in 2e for whatever cause High King David's presence had restrained that was now gone with his absence, they weren't going to war out of &quot;because one side is currently slowly murdering the other side as a society anyway&quot;. Seelie vs Unseelie, Noble vs Commoner, Noble faction vs Noble Faction, Shadow Court shenanigans, the risen Fomorian hosts, etc. The Commoners themselves were divided amongst those various axes as far as who and where they supported.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I straight up think there's greater diversity on Sidhe in C20 than there was in the 2e Core, and at has much fewer &quot;OH MY GOD EVIIIIIIIIL&quot; bits than Shining Host, Fools Luck, First two book of Houses. </div> </div> </div>Shining Host also had stuff about things like being bound to obey the high king's command to withdraw, the sidhe having sizable progressive political movements within them, and examples of nobles ruling well, and what have you. Fool's Luck as the big commoner perspective book, I'm pretty sure that wasn't going to be a thing favourable to the sidhe. The first book of houses had a pretty big variety of things in them favourable to the sidhe, from House Dougal and Fiona's &quot;we totally had people stay behind or took the time to give commoners our stuff and titles before going&quot; to various pieces of the Gwydion section for better things they did, to with even House Eiluned going &quot;yeah, we were the ones that did the night of iron knives&quot; removing &quot;the sidhe as a wider group thing did the night of iron knives&quot;, and even in the unseelie one, what the Balor actually were was something they particularly hid even from the rest of the Unseelie, sidhe included, the Ailil were a mixed bag, and the Leanhaun were their own thing (their own crazy thing, one grants).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> but when you get to the write up of Concordia you have a wide variety of domains from commoner run commonwealths to those who don't turn away anyone to those who are friends with the Nunehei etc. </div> </div> </div>I feel like I'm restaging a discussion I already had, but commoner run commonwealths don't say anything about the sidhe other than &quot;the sidhe rule was so bad that they needed to be overthrown and replaced&quot;, what about them makes the sidhe come off any better? There are any number of holds that are just described for what they are, and &quot;the sidhe are fine if they adopt the culture and trappings of the nunnehi instead of their own&quot; with regards Chief Greyhawk is just... hugely problematic.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Yeah they aren't being &quot;good&quot; rulers but they also aren't hitting the heights of monstrocity either. </div> </div> </div>I'm pretty sure we're just going to have to agree to disagree on that &quot;mass starving the other kithain as a societal trend&quot; isn't hitting the heights of monstrosity.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And serious if we are comparing Sidhe in the entiriety of 2e vs Sidhe in C20 you have to include Kithbook Eshu and how much it pulls it down. </div> </div> </div>And again we're back at &quot;this one kithbook basically portrayed them as basically soulless baby eating monsters, therefore this is totally an across the board improvement.&quot; I'm comparing 2e to C20 because the examples of Sidhe not being godawful as compared to places where they were portrayed as godawful felt bigger and more significant, and certainly more impactful for a variety of reasons, the most basic being that they were prevalent enough that the default state of the commoners was not noted as &quot;starving towards desperation and undoing&quot;.<br /> <br /> edit: at this point this mostly feels entirely like restaging the previous editions' &quot;sidhe, jerks or not?&quot; argument, with the added dimension of &quot;they were totally jerks, so this edition is in fact being generous to them to allow what it does&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12141,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12141-markk","user":"MarkK","date":".  clarified a gwydion thing and a war in concordia thing 05-13-2017, 09:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12141-markk","name":"MarkK","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-13T20:01:16-07:00","id":1092200,"title":"","content":"So I went back and reread page 41 which where we get the wonderfully colourful title &quot;Starvation of Dreams&quot; and I read carefully and.. there is no mass movement of sidhe or commoner nobles to starve huge swaths of changeling society of glamour. The page going forward merely says there's an issue with freeholds dying and new freeholds not letting in refugees. That those who have had time to build up their stocks aren't as empathic to newer changelings who haven't had decades to build up stores of glamour. That members of Parliment care more for getting points for their Court than for actually coming up with solutions that help everyone.<br /> <br /> So yeah I'm going to go with Sidhe are better off in c20 than 2e because they don't have the Shadow Court as the rulers of the Unseelie. The Unseelie are separate. The Shadow Court is a protest outside it. That multiple Houses were cleaned up from unplayble monsters and Autumn Sidhe were buffed and made playable across the board so you can now play a sidhe who enters the dreaming and isn't a complete asshole. <br /> <br /> And no there aren't writeups for progressive societies but that cancels out lack of writeups for groups like Beltane blade, Bright Pilgrims, Children's Crusade, the Ranters","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-13T20:51:29-07:00","id":1092210,"title":"","content":"Dude, on the very same page it talks about fae getting so desperate from lack of glamour that some of them have started willingly joining the Thallain/Fomorians to avoid undoing. The page going forward talks about a massive rift between the commoners and the nobility as a result of this stuff, it talks about nobles as a collective group refusing to admit how the world has changed, and under the very section you're talking about it talks about commoners clustering to their leaders for help and receiving nothing, in those words, it talks about going to titled commoners that are part of the houses for help and &quot;being met with the same ignorant replies&quot; as from Tara Nar, which straight up talks about suggesting austerity as far as the word from there. At this point you're straight up talking about a different book to the point that it's not really worth either of our time to keep discussing this I think.<br /> <br /> All the same: The Shadow Court were pretty often not the rulers of the Unseelie in 2e despite that you keep saying they were or multiple books where indeed they weren't the rulers of the Unseelie would make no sense whatsoever. Two Houses out of 13 were outright monsters secretly working for the Fomorians or otherwise trying to destroy the world for their own hidden agenda, as a contrast to now of Two Houses out of 13 being majority salutary Autumn sidhe types (who, while there, said two houses are noted for having a general comparative lack of lands and high titles compared to the other houses), a house that exists primarily outside the Autumn world, and otherwise just pieces of the rest, maybe, who aren't really exempt from how the book talks about the landed nobility acting.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Autumn Sidhe were buffed and made playable across the board so you can now play a sidhe who enters the dreaming and isn't a complete asshole. </div> </div> </div>So, two houses out of 13, one that already lives there, and some pieces of others.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And no there aren't writeups for progressive societies but that cancels out lack of writeups for groups like Beltane blade, Bright Pilgrims, Children's Crusade, the Ranters </div> </div> </div>It's as though previously, there were both good and bad groups within the sidhe, large enough to be actual groups that spanned across houses, as opposed to a state of affairs of &quot;some exceptions to being jerks overall.&quot;<br /> <br /> Anyway, at this point I think I've said anything I could ever possibly say on this topic and am inclined to leave it there, particularly when we've reached &quot;well then we're reading completely different books.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12141,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12141-markk","user":"MarkK","date":".  clarification of a statement 05-14-2017, 12:05 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12141-markk","name":"MarkK","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-14T02:37:08-07:00","id":1092280,"title":"","content":"Just curious how was it ever a secret how evil House Balor was... I mean they are called house Balor... how is that even a thing...?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-14T03:21:19-07:00","id":1092293,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1086863-it-s-out?p=1092280#post1092280\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just curious how was it ever a secret how evil House Balor was... I mean they are called house Balor... how is that even a thing...?</div> </div> </div> </div>The majority of fae thought it was a twisted joke or targeted insult at the seelie in the main that they picked that name for themselves, and look at the Balor maintaining and guarding various paths/trods through the Dreaming for all fae to use, they surely can't be that bad! Who trusts the Scathach anyway, not me! And etc.<br /> <br /> It was a sort of similar deal to how the Followers of Set get by despite being named, the Followers of Set (&quot;oh the name's not that serious&quot;).<br /> <br /> You had stuff like the Ailil knowing the Balor wanted to murder them and take their place someday (though particularly not the Fomorian servant part), but they shrugged and went &quot;eh, that's unseelie politics, and so long as we know that, we can use them.&quot; There were some groups that knew, but in general they had terrible/questionable reputations in wider society as far as proving what they knew (the Beaumayn, the Scathach), or were markedly terrible at sharing secrets (the Eiluned, who also had their own reputation problems really). Some of the Lost Houses that rolled in remembered the truth of the Balor, but they were extremely recent arrivals and Changeling kinda ended at the time before anything could really come of that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12141,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12141-markk","user":"MarkK","date":". 05-14-2017, 06:33 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12141-markk","name":"MarkK","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-14T11:04:19-07:00","id":1092381,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MarkK</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1086863-it-s-out?p=1092175#post1092175\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Shining Host also had stuff about things like being bound to obey the high king's command to withdraw, the sidhe having sizable progressive political movements within them, and examples of nobles ruling well, and what have you. Fool's Luck as the big commoner perspective book, I'm pretty sure that wasn't going to be a thing favourable to the sidhe. The first book of houses had a pretty big variety of things in them favourable to the sidhe, from House Dougal and Fiona's &quot;we totally had people stay behind or took the time to give commoners our stuff and titles before going&quot; to various pieces of the Gwydion section for better things they did, to with even House Eiluned going &quot;yeah, we were the ones that did the night of iron knives&quot; removing &quot;the sidhe as a wider group thing did the night of iron knives&quot;, and even in the unseelie one, what the Balor actually were was something they particularly hid even from the rest of the Unseelie, sidhe included, the Ailil were a mixed bag, and the Leanhaun were their own thing (their own crazy thing, one grants)</div> </div> </div> </div>Argh, okay, I know I should let this go, especially because I am genuinely fine with us having different views on how the sidhe are portrayed - I don't need to convince you otherwise on that point; we disagree and that's okay. <br /> <br /> But this, here, as a point of logic - C20 still includes Gwydion being bound by an order to withdraw, it still includes Fiona leaving large numbers of people stay behind and it still includes Eiluned taking the time to pass on their titles and holdings, and I pointed all this out previously, and was told it wasn't relevant because it was ancient history. But now you're using it - for a second time - as an example of 2e's more nuanced view of the sidhe. <br /> <br /> So like, have whatever opinion you want, maybe this stuff isn't highlighted enough for your tastes, or you don't think it counts for C20 for some other reason, and that reason might be perfectly legitimate. But like...for the sake of consistency if it can be used in defence of 2e sidhe I think it should be able to be used in defence of sidhe in C20.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/187-beccatoria","name":"beccatoria","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar187_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"85"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-14T11:20:43-07:00","id":1092390,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Argh, okay, I know I should let this go </div> </div> </div>And yet, here we are again.<br /> <br /> And in response, as a point of logic, and as something I already said to you, all that stuff is stuff the houses did in the past, which in 2e is fine, because the sidhe aren't near collectively engaged in something utterly godawful in the current era in 2e. It's fine for a &quot;no, they vary in not being douchebaggy coward jerks who responded to the Shattering by being the ones to successfully run in fear the fastest.&quot; There's nothing going down in the modern era to render such things functionally meaningless. When the discussion I was having at that point was &quot;no, in 2e their portrayal was pretty varied&quot;, that's what I'm noting it for.<br /> <br /> In C20, by marked contrast, it boils down to things they did in the past that don't really matter in the face of that they are currently starving the other kiths out. Whatever they did then, that is what they're doing now to the point of broad spectrum portrayal. When they're doing such a starkly wretched thing now, whatever they did before feels largely irrelevant.<br /> <br /> Considering that's exactly how I replied to you on this when you brought it up, it kinda feels like you weren't especially reading my posts outside of scanning for stuff to pick apart? That feels really frustrating and is a good part of why this discussion hasn't exactly helped the negative impression I've come off with.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12141,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12141-markk","user":"MarkK","date":". 05-14-2017, 02:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12141-markk","name":"MarkK","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-14T11:57:23-07:00","id":1092411,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MarkK</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1086863-it-s-out?p=1092390#post1092390\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Considering that's exactly how I replied to you on this when you brought it up, it kinda feels like you weren't especially reading my posts outside of scanning for stuff to pick apart? That feels really frustrating and is a good part of why this discussion hasn't exactly helped the negative impression I've come off with.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a pretty crappy thing to say. I don't think I deserve to be blamed for your negative feelings about the setting, or accused of bad faith. I did my best to end the conversation on reasonable terms. So for the record, no, I wasn't doing that. It's just that your perspective on this makes no sense to me, something you are surely familiar with since you straight up said that my explanations weren't making things any clearer to you, and you simply restated your original position.<br /> <br /> As you said before to me, no, this doesn't make your position clearer. You're still using historical behaviour as part of the reason that the 2e sidhe were more nuanced, then saying that historical behaviour <i>can't</i> be used to explain that C20 sidhe are more nuanced, essentially because of an arbitrary decision about how bad their current behaviour has to be before their 600-year old actions cease being relevant.<br /> <br /> If your want to argue that the weight of their historical behaviour holds a certain amount of weight and for you that ameliorates their 2e behaviour but not their C20 behaviour, then that's a position that can be debated. But it's frustrating to see it brought up repeatedly as a <i>direct</i> contrast to C20 - as if this material isn't present in C20 when it <i>is</i> - as it's also an impossible challenge. This content is apparently only allowed to work for one side of the argument.<br /> <br /> So I stand by my original point: this material is in C20 and if it's evidence of nuanced sidhe in 2e, then it is in C20 too. Maybe not <i>enough</i> for you, maybe not to the degree you need. And again, that's fine. But it IS present. It's a question of degree not presence.<br /> <br /> ETA: I just went back and reread our previous conversation on page 20 to be sure I was remembering things correctly and I'm satisfied that this was not, in fact, something you already said to me.<br /> <br /> This is the section I think you mean: <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The problem of that is that a lot of the stuff you're talking about with the houses are things the houses are noted as having done in the past, whereas the broad spectrum stuff is noted as what is by contrast happening now. </div> </div> </div>I can see now that you mean this comparatively between the presentation of 2e sidhe and C20 sidhe, but respectfully it's not completely clear and at the time I read it - I feel reasonably given the somewhat awkward syntax at the end of the sentence - that you simply meant &quot;that stuff happened in the past, whereas by contrast we're talking about the present,&quot; rather than, &quot;that stuff happened in the past and doesn't offer appropriate contrast to what's happening in the present.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":187,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/187-beccatoria","user":"beccatoria","date":". 05-14-2017, 03:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/187-beccatoria","name":"beccatoria","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar187_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"85"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-14T12:08:47-07:00","id":1092415,"title":"","content":"Maybe he's saying that the sidhe have become less nuanced in C20. Not in terms of presentation, but saying that he sees C20 as saying that between 1996 and 2016 the sidhe themselves have become much less sympathetic?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10243-zenten","name":"zenten","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10243_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"488"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-14T12:36:16-07:00","id":1092428,"title":"","content":"When you bring up &quot;the sidhe are nuanced just fine in C20, they're noted as doing all this stuff in the past like this&quot; and I reply &quot;that doesn't really come off as mattering considering what they're doing now&quot;, and then a jillion posts later you say &quot;What's going on? You just said the thing I said about the stuff in the past, therefore you're illogical&quot;, in a way that has nothing to do with why or how I brought it up, that's how it comes off.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It's just that your perspective makes no sense to me, something you are surely familiar with since you straight up said that my explanations weren't making things any clearer to you, and you simply restated your original position. Which, again, is fine, we do not see eye to eye on this. </div> </div> </div>It doesn't really seem fine by you when instead of &quot;fine, we don't agree, we'll just leave it there&quot; you're back onto going on at length about how nothing I say makes any sense?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> As you said before to me, no, this doesn't make your position clearer. You're still using historical behaviour as part of the reason that the 2e sidhe were more nuanced, then saying that historical behaviour <i>can't</i> be used to explain that C20 sidhe are more nuanced, essentially because of an arbitrary decision about how bad their current behaviour has to be before their 600-year old actions cease being relevant. </div> </div> </div>Because in 2e, the sidhe were not currently engaged in a collective activity that would make any past good deeds basically meaningless, you can thus point to past good deeds they've done as something that still have relevance. That you think this is arbitrary means I frankly have no idea what to tell you. They're broad spectrum starving the rest of the fae, that outweighs pretty hard and sweepingly whatever salutary behaviour can be attributable to them during the Shattering. I don't have any more basic way to say that, but I guess I can try.<br /> <br /> So, Magneto from the comic books, right? Some writers like to portray him as this sort of conflicted, sympathetic character who in some ways has some measure of justification to what he's doing and is even outright heroic sometimes. And other writers like to have him go on high innocent body count mass murdering rampages. The first group of writers try to retcon that stuff as hard as they can when they get their hands on the character once again, because they realize that whatever heroic thing they want to say he's done/had him do before, it's pretty staggeringly meaningless in the face of mass murdering rampages.<br /> <br /> Whatever salutary things the sidhe might have done in the past in C20, the glamour austerity thing is what they are doing now down even to the commoner members of their houses following the pattern. I don't see it as arbitrary to note &quot;this horrible, blind, cowardly, mass suffering causing thing they are doing right now as the setting speaks, as a broad spectrum group, pretty heavily shunts to the side whatever might have been done before.&quot;<br /> <br /> I realize I'm opening myself to all of this being entirely dismissed on &quot;it's not like the sidhe are a single guy going on mass murdering rampages, therefore nothing you say makes sense&quot;, so, again, this is an analogy. When the sidhe are doing a blisteringly crappy thing as a group right now, stuff they did before doesn't hold a lot of weight. When the sidhe are not doing a blisteringly crappy thing as a group right now, stuff they did before is an example in a chain of behaviour stretching down into the current setting of being a more mixed bag as a kith, there's nothing to throw it off with &quot;but as a group, they are, right now, doing this abominable thing instead, actively&quot;.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If your want to argue that the weight of their historical behaviour holds a certain amount of weight and for you that ameliorates their 2e behaviour but not their C20 behaviour, then that's a position that can be debated. But it's frustrating to see it brought up repeatedly as a <i>direct</i> contrast to C20 - as if this material isn't present in C20 when it <i>is</i> - as it's also an impossible challenge. This content is apparently only allowed to work for one side of the argument. </div> </div> </div>This is only possible if you ignore a bunch of the things I've said or dismiss the broad spectrum suffering thing as merely an arbitrary detail, while basically just picking stuff out of context. I don't know how clearer to say &quot;these are things from the books in 2e that demonstrate the books in 2e being nuanced, nothing rolls along later to paint them as meaningless. In C20, when the modern state of what the sidhe are doing is so terrible, things they might have done in the past become without a lot of weight.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> So I stand by my original point: this material is in C20 and if it's evidence of nuanced sidhe in 2e, then it is in C20 too. Maybe not <i>enough</i> for you, maybe not to the degree you need. And again, that's fine. But it IS present. It's a question of degree not presence. </div> </div> </div>Again, it doesn't seem like it's fine at all, because here we are once again, and capitalizing for emphasis even. And I'm not sure at this point what you want to get out of this really as far as bringing things back? We're obviously not going to agree, we obviously don't think the other person is making sense or being consistent at this point. Unless your posts are mostly for the sake of &quot;see how little sense this guy makes?&quot; for other people, what do you feel is being accomplished by drawing this out past the point where we decided to previously leave things? For my own part, I'm mostly trying to elaborate on why it is that my stance is what it is, why other people might be bugged by these things, but I've said basically everything I can possibly say on the matter at this point, down to at this point having to note the consistency of my own thoughts.<br /> <br /> So.. I mean.. respond to this as you like as far as what you feel is my contradictory illogic? But I'm kinda done at this point as far as talking this one out. It doesn't feel like there's anything remotely resembling a point remaining to doing so.<br /> <br /> I mean..<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I can see now that you mean this comparatively between the presentation of 2e sidhe and C20 sidhe, but respectfully it's not completely clear and at the time I read it - I feel reasonably given the somewhat awkward syntax at the end of the sentence - that you simply meant &quot;that stuff happened in the past, whereas by contrast we're talking about the present,&quot; rather than, &quot;that stuff happened in the past and doesn't offer appropriate contrast to what's happening in the present.&quot; </div> </div> </div>We're now in semantics land. I think journeying to that land should be a statement in and of itself on this discussion.<br /> <br /> For the record, I said it again here, in that discussion:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I talk about the current metaplot being the sidhe starving out the commoner kiths, and you keep noting stuff about sidhe having historically stayed behind repeatedly, which has absolutely nothing to do with that. That doesn't do anything about what the current plot is. </div> </div> </div>I said it again here, in that discussion:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The first two things have nothing to do with the current state of the setting. </div> </div> </div>When I say a thing three times, I don't know what to tell you on that you feel I'm not being clear enough for your liking.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12141,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12141-markk","user":"MarkK","date":". 05-14-2017, 04:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12141-markk","name":"MarkK","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-14T12:42:11-07:00","id":1092431,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>zenten</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1086863-it-s-out?p=1092415#post1092415\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe he's saying that the sidhe have become less nuanced in C20. Not in terms of presentation, but saying that he sees C20 as saying that between 1996 and 2016 the sidhe themselves have become much less sympathetic?</div> </div> </div> </div>That's in terms of presentation just fine, but yes, I'm saying that I see C20 as going &quot;the sidhe as a broad spectrum group are now doing this terrible godawful thing, whatever they might have done or not done before this terrible godawful thing falls away in the face of the thing they are doing, right now.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12141-markk","name":"MarkK","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-14T13:09:09-07:00","id":1092447,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> When you bring up &quot;the sidhe are nuanced just fine in C20, they're noted as doing all this stuff in the past like this&quot; and I reply &quot;that doesn't really come off as mattering considering what they're doing now&quot;, and then a jillion posts later you say &quot;What's going on? You just said the thing I said about the stuff in the past, therefore you're illogical&quot;, in a way that has nothing to do with why or how I brought it up, that's how it comes off. </div> </div> </div>And <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It doesn't really seem fine by you when instead of &quot;fine, we don't agree, we'll just leave it there&quot; you're back onto going on at length about how nothing I say makes any sense? </div> </div> </div>No, I really don't care if we disagree. My perception of the lack of logic in only allowing historical comparisons for one edition bothered me and I shouldn't have picked at it, but I did. It bugged me because I brought that stuff up originally because I'd seen you referencing it earlier in the thread before I joined. You dismissed it as being irrelevant because it wasn't current. I pointed out to you I'd done it because you'd raised it previously, and you didn't respond to that point, so I didn't get an answer on what the difference was. So for me, it wasn't unrelated, it was a point in the conversation that left me legitimately confused and frustrated because of a lack of an answer. <br /> <br /> I do now understand your position on it, so that's something. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Again, it doesn't seem like it's fine at all, because here we are once again, and capitalizing for emphasis even. And I'm not sure at this point what you want to get out of this really as far as bringing things back? We're obviously not going to agree, we obviously don't think the other person is making sense or being consistent at this point. Unless your posts are mostly for the sake of &quot;see how little sense this guy makes?&quot; </div> </div> </div>You seem to believe that everyone is out to hurt you, and to be responding in kind, and I'm sorry if my frustration added to that, but I promise you, I'm not. As I noted in my edited section, I can see where the confusion arose and why you thought you'd explained your position, while I found it very unclear.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/187-beccatoria","name":"beccatoria","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar187_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"85"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-14T13:28:01-07:00","id":1092459,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You seem to believe that everyone is out to hurt you, and to be responding in kind </div> </div> </div>No, not particularly, but similarly I can really only say that and people can believe it or not as they choose, and considering how we respond to each other's posts, it is what it is. I certainly apologize if my posts have read as some effort to hurt you, that is not my intent. I'm pretty cool with people not thinking the things I think and saying as much. Other dude when I said &quot;I'd rather just drop it, it seems like we're reading completely different books than each other&quot;, looks to have obligingly dropped it. Which I frankly super appreciate of them, that's rare for the internet. But &quot;your posts are illogical, your standards are arbitrary, your grammar is awkward, your statements are unclear, you're overly sensitive&quot;, as the subject matter of reviving a discussion that ended, it's kind of thing? <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> As I noted in my edited section, I can see where the confusion arose and why you thought you'd explained your position, while I found it very unclear. </div> </div> </div>Then I would suggest we leave it at that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12141-markk","name":"MarkK","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-14T13:38:35-07:00","id":1092464,"title":"","content":"Why doesn't Freehold Background correspond in any way with Starvation of Dreams, though? Rules-wise Freeholds work just fine.<br /> <br /> <br /> There's also no special rules, etc.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5211-firkraag","name":"Firkraag","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5211_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-14T13:40:28-07:00","id":1092467,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Firkraag</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1086863-it-s-out?p=1092464#post1092464\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why doesn't Freehold Background correspond in any way with Starvation of Dreams, though? Rules-wise Freeholds work just fine.<br /> <br /> <br /> There's also no special rules, etc.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's kind of funny. By strictly rules changes Banality is much less of a threat now, and Glamour is much more available.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10243-zenten","name":"zenten","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10243_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"488"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-14T13:47:40-07:00","id":1092470,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Firkraag</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1086863-it-s-out?p=1092464#post1092464\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why doesn't Freehold Background correspond in any way with Starvation of Dreams, though? Rules-wise Freeholds work just fine.<br /> <br /> <br /> There's also no special rules, etc.</div> </div> </div> </div>The book has a few places where the mechanics and the non mechanics material don't exactly match up. That's not really new as a thing in Changeling though, I would say.<br /> <br /> edit: I mean, that's not really new as a thing in OWoD stuff generally, y'know? Or white wolf generally. Hell, Aberrant made it pretty hard to get taint points, despite novas becoming taint blasted monstrosities being a huge setting deal and problem. (Dear people working on Aberrant 2.0, this should not be taken to mean that I want taint to be easier to get. Thank you.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12141,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12141-markk","user":"MarkK","date":". 05-14-2017, 04:52 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12141-markk","name":"MarkK","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-14T13:53:29-07:00","id":1092474,"title":"","content":"Go figure.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5211-firkraag","name":"Firkraag","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5211_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-14T13:53:59-07:00","id":1092475,"title":"","content":"I think it matches up fine in just C20. If you're running by the book 2nd ed rules and setting, then shift to by the book C20 rules and setting then yes, that's going to be weird.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10243-zenten","name":"zenten","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10243_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"488"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-14T14:03:47-07:00","id":1092481,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Firkraag</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1086863-it-s-out?p=1092474#post1092474\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Go figure.</div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly, for people less inclined to deal with the current setting, the less house ruling needed to do so the better. For those dealing with the current setting, it's not hard to say &quot;freehold as a background is restricted&quot; or &quot;in game you'll be dealing with a lot of npc interest in your hold as a plot point for stories&quot; or whatever.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12141-markk","name":"MarkK","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-14T14:13:40-07:00","id":1092489,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MarkK</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1086863-it-s-out?p=1092481#post1092481\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Honestly, for people less inclined to deal with the current setting, the less house ruling needed to do so the better. For those dealing with the current setting, it's not hard to say &amp;quot;freehold as a background is restricted&amp;quot; or &amp;quot;in game you'll be dealing with a lot of npc interest in your hold as a plot point for stories&amp;quot; or whatever.</div> </div> </div> </div>Exactly. One thing the system is *not* meant to do is provide some sort of statistical representation of the setting. Freeholds are rare, but by the rules you can take a hugely powerful one at character creation. Just like you can be mega rich, or be good enough to win a gold medal in the Olympics.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10243-zenten","name":"zenten","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10243_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"488"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-14T14:18:26-07:00","id":1092492,"title":"","content":"I mean, you could start the game as a Duke, it's not like they're at all common on the ground (ugh, again, I did a pun again. I am shamed). If your particular ST was cool with it, your group could be the all Duke motley or whatever. (Initial potential motley name &quot;the Dukes of Earl&quot;, they're a group of dukes who are also a Soul/doo-wop band in the mortal world, touring Concordia and getting into adventures. I am further shamed.)<br /> <br /> (Other potential motley name. The Dukes of Hazzard. They're a group of renegade Dukes in the Kingdom of Willows staying one step ahead of King Melige's shadowed tyranny in their Treasure car, though their popular support is damaged by their use of frankly entirely heavily inappropriate iconography. The shame rolls on...)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12141,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12141-markk","user":"MarkK","date":". 05-14-2017, 05:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12141-markk","name":"MarkK","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-14T14:25:23-07:00","id":1092495,"title":"","content":"a motley of landless dukes could be really interesting, that said if everyone was playing a duke Id give them all title 5 for free as its sortof essential to the plot....u